{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread","id":58142,"title":"The LGBT Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-26T09:45:37-08:00","id":58142,"title":"The LGBT Thread","content":"Because I like having one of these around.<br /> <br /> * * *<br /> <br /> I came out to someone this week.<br /> <br /> It couldn't possibly have gone better than it did - she encouraged me to embrace how I was feeling and to do what makes me happy, and she reassured me that my gender/sexual identity doesn't drastically change who I am or pigeonhole me. She also talked a bit about how her own experiences went - she is herself bisexual, and leads a thoroughly interesting life besides. (Part of why I chose to come out to her first is because her adventures have distanced her from people closer to home.)<br /> <br /> It felt really, really good to talk to her about it and to receive such a warm response. I've been weighing the idea of coming out to my family, but as you might expect, that makes me very nervous. It was a bit of a struggle just bringing up these feelings with a distant friend, and I more or less knew she would be accepting and kind about it. Still, I feel a strong urge to get it out in the open. And I don't think telling my family would prompt any horrible backlash - no screaming, no disowning me, no cutting me off - but I do worry about the idea of being loved less, of being viewed as an embarrassment or tactfully ignored. (&quot;Let's not talk about Cielle's situation.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Any advice for how to tell my family I'm trans? Or about how you came out, or about coming out in general? I was planning a soft approach, and talking to one parent to start with - I've heard that being outnumbered is a recipe for problems - but I think you guys have more experience than me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","user":"Cielle","date":". 01-26-2014, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T10:44:53-08:00","id":58179,"title":"","content":"I would absolutely talk to them separately, and don't be super-surprised if it doesn't exactly go as planned. Brace for &quot;So...you're a cross dresser?&quot;<br /> <br /> A lot of times (my personal experience included) even if your parents are open-minded about LGBT things, they'll try to insist that they're cool with transpeople, but you're absolutely not one of them, no way, they know their son and their son's no girl! etc etc etc.<br /> <br /> If it goes well, holy shit is that the best thing ever or what? Unfortunately I've never heard of that happening. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Best of luck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I had a signature but now I don't but it won't let me leave this blank so yeah.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/199-yue","name":"Yue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T10:52:40-08:00","id":58182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread#post58142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I came out to someone this week.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're actually trans? Last I'd heard, you were still exploring it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T11:46:23-08:00","id":58216,"title":"","content":"I know I'm going to get some flack for saying this but I will anyways, this conversation has virtually nothing to do with onyx path products, I'm a member of the lgtb community and I support you coming out but im honestly surprised that you used this forum as a place to host this discussion. I hope your family is as supportive as mine was opposed and that everyone you have contact with is supportive as well, I hate to say this but if you identify as trans and let that be known then you will likely have great difficulty being accepted, its tragic but a lot of people aren't willing to accept that many people are unhappy as the gender they're born as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T11:58:55-08:00","id":58227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dream_Walker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=58216#post58216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I'm going to get some flack for saying this but I will anyways, this conversation has virtually nothing to do with onyx path products, I'm a member of the lgtb community and I support you coming out but im honestly surprised that you used this forum as a place to host this discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, the off-topic portion of these forums is open to any non-rulebreaking discussions its participants are willing to entertain. Most of the discussions in this subforum have nothing to do with Onyx Path products, because that's not what this particular subforum is <i>for.</i> Indeed, there were several LGBT threads in the prior incarnation of these forums. You are of course free to report the thread if you feel it violates forum rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=58182#post58182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're actually trans? Last I'd heard, you were still exploring it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I was thinking of saying was along the lines that I'd been dealing with some issues about gender identity and looking into possible solutions, and outline some of the stuff I was thinking of doing - potentially including hormone treatments, etc. All of which certainly fits the &quot;trans&quot; label. To be totally honest I'm not entirely sure where this particular path would take me, but...the thought of doing it makes me happy. And I think that's probably an indicator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","user":"Cielle","date":". 01-26-2014, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T14:43:57-08:00","id":58326,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">The off topic forum is for discussing any subject that hasn't been prohibited, it doesn't matter if the subject has nothing to do with OP or its products, that's kind of the point of this subforum.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T04:38:39-08:00","id":58629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=58326#post58326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">The off topic forum is for discussing any subject that hasn't been prohibited, it doesn't matter if the subject has nothing to do with OP or its products, that's kind of the point of this subforum.</span></div> </div> </div> </div> Understood. I saw this topic as it was the most recent post and didn't know there WAS an off topic forum, I thought the reason for this forums existence was to discuss OP publishing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T04:51:59-08:00","id":58630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=58227#post58227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As I understand it, the off-topic portion of these forums is open to any non-rulebreaking discussions its participants are willing to entertain. Most of the discussions in this subforum have nothing to do with Onyx Path products, because that's not what this particular subforum is <i>for.</i> Indeed, there were several LGBT threads in the prior incarnation of these forums. You are of course free to report the thread if you feel it violates forum rules.</div> </div> </div> </div> I support freedom of speech and dont believe in reporting people on the forum regardless of what they say. For what its worth I support you and all our fellow members of the lgtb community, when I saw this topic it was at the top of the home page as it was the most recently posted on topic and not seem in the off topic forum, which I didn't even know existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T08:16:56-08:00","id":58725,"title":"","content":"Wow, Cielle! I'm so glad you had such a great coming out experience there. As disheartening as negative coming out experiences can be, you (and by you, I mean we) should always work to fortify ourselves with the positive ones. Also, good luck with your family.<br /> <br /> I don't have a recent coming out story, alas, though I am dealing with dating again, and that's rough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns","name":"widdershawns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T10:02:10-08:00","id":58817,"title":"","content":"I hope everything goes well for you, my coming out was actually quite violent and if it weren't for my mother intervening I think my father and brother would have severely beaten me, it was pretty bad and we all walked away with some serious injuries, I havent spoken to either of those two men since, that was back in 02 Let's hope your comong out goes better than mine, Yue's advice was good, I advise speaking to your family members one at a time (that way you have more control of the situation) and also suggest slowly introducing them to transgender issues before bringing up your own gender identity if they are not already knowledgeable and accepting in regards to gender issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T23:19:32-08:00","id":59553,"title":"","content":"I'm cheering for you, Cielle! I'm glad things are going well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=58179#post58179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately I've never heard of that happening. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm lucky to have a family that includes a trans parent, a poly relationship, and a pansexual parent. Absolutely no one was surprised that I am pan and poly, the only real surprise was identifying as a demigirl. And even that just got an &quot;Oh. Okay!&quot; so c: Now you have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T23:45:01-08:00","id":59569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tluthal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=59553#post59553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm cheering for you, Cielle! I'm glad things are going well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm lucky to have a family that includes a trans parent, a poly relationship, and a pansexual parent. Absolutely no one was surprised that I am pan and poly, the only real surprise was identifying as a demigirl. And even that just got an &quot;Oh. Okay!&quot; so c: Now you have?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Well, shit, that's great! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I had a signature but now I don't but it won't let me leave this blank so yeah.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/199-yue","name":"Yue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T15:20:59-08:00","id":61106,"title":"","content":"Tluthal, you gave me so much stuff to wiki just now...<br /> <br /> Cielle, I'm crossing my fingers for you.<br /> <br /> I came out almost two years ago to my parents, after everyone else in my life already knew and accepted it. I was terrified about how they would react to their son being gay. My uncertainty fueled my imagination, coming up with thousands of terrible scenarios. My fear and imagination kept me from coming out for so long. Before I finally did I'd made arrangements should the worst happen and I had someone I trusted with me for the strength to actually go through with it. As it turned out, it wasn't really necessary to make all these arrangements, they just said they didn't like it and that was that. It was oddly anticlimactic. To this day they pretend it isn't true, but I can deal with that. I came out for my own sake, not theirs. I didn't want their acceptance, I wanted to be freed from the burden of keeping this secret.<br /> <br /> Though the arrangements proved useless, in this case, I'm glad I made them anyway. I made sure I was financially independent and living on my own, I told them in front of someone who didn't live in their house, I made other plans for the day so that people, who I had told about my plan, would worry if I didn't show up, and take measure, I told my neighbors to call emergency services if they heard me yell. I kept my shoes and my jacket on, sat close to the door and kept a table between me and my parents, just in case I needed to make a run for it. I know, its paranoid, but its important to have some measure of stability and safety in moments when you feel insecure about the situation. Maybe you don't want to go overboard like I did, but the general advice is sound.<br /> <br /> When you're telling them, stay calm and take your time to say what you want to say. I told my parents I wanted to tell them something important and I did nothing but stare at my feet for some twenty minutes before I finally got the words out of my mouth.<br /> <br /> I hope my little story and my advice are useful to you. I wish you all the luck in the world and I hope you can draw strength, if even just a sliver, from the knowledge that there are people out there who support you no matter what happens. Stay strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2054-whim","name":"Whim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T16:21:34-08:00","id":61137,"title":"","content":"I wish I had saved a link to a story I found a month or two ago. A kid was on the phone with his boyfriend one night, making plans to come out to his parents the next day after school, but when he woke up, they had left him a note on the fridge that went something like, &quot;We overheard you on the phone last night. No worries about coming out; just bring home some OJ when you come home. Love, your parents. PS, you and your boyfriend make a cute couple.&quot;<br /> <br /> That note is as close to accurately reproduced as I can recall (which means I did my best but can't vouch for it), and I was wondering, how would you guys feel about receiving that note? I'm torn. On the surface, it seems fine, but I think I'd be disappointed at losing the chance to make a big declaration for my own sake, you know, to take a stand and be brave. My suspicious mind would also wonder the circumstances of them overhearing me, and why they seem to be trying to talk me out of talking about my orientation and what it means to me; like, is it an attempt to leave it an unspoken secret that's swept under the rug? I also might resent that they tried to decide it's not a big deal when it's probably a very big deal for me. People die for being gay.<br /> <br /> But that's me, and I'm an angry sort of person. How would any of you feel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T23:11:01-08:00","id":61334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=61106#post61106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tluthal, you gave me so much stuff to wiki just now...</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I don't have a whole lot of info on trans* so I'll let you do your wiking yourself, but a few links to help you out:<br /> <br /> Poly - short for polyamory. I direct pretty much everyone to <a href=\"http://www.morethantwo.com/polyamory.html\" target=\"_blank\">this site here</a>, it's pretty great.<br /> Pansexual - <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bv5k9w6Hpi4\" target=\"_blank\">This video</a> has a good explanation. Slightly NSFW. Basically most people would identify me as bisexual.<br /> Demigirl is the one where things get iffy, it's a term I came across recently for a certain type of nonbinary gender orientation. Basically means I mostly identify as female, but not 100%.<br /> <br /> Hope that helped!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T03:00:26-08:00","id":61422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=61137#post61137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish I had saved a link to a story I found a month or two ago. A kid was on the phone with his boyfriend one night, making plans to come out to his parents the next day after school, but when he woke up, they had left him a note on the fridge that went something like, &quot;We overheard you on the phone last night. No worries about coming out; just bring home some OJ when you come home. Love, your parents. PS, you and your boyfriend make a cute couple.&quot;<br /> <br /> That note is as close to accurately reproduced as I can recall (which means I did my best but can't vouch for it), and I was wondering, how would you guys feel about receiving that note? I'm torn. On the surface, it seems fine, but I think I'd be disappointed at losing the chance to make a big declaration for my own sake, you know, to take a stand and be brave. My suspicious mind would also wonder the circumstances of them overhearing me, and why they seem to be trying to talk me out of talking about my orientation and what it means to me; like, is it an attempt to leave it an unspoken secret that's swept under the rug? I also might resent that they tried to decide it's not a big deal when it's probably a very big deal for me. People die for being gay.<br /> <br /> But that's me, and I'm an angry sort of person. How would any of you feel?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be incredibly relieved, to tell the truth. In my opinion the big declaration, taking a stand and being brave, are not that important, compared to having this burden lifted from you. I'd still want to talk about it, and I'd still be nervous and have to gather up the courage to do even that, just because its an uncomfortable topic to talk about with your folks. I probably wouldn't think they were trying to avoid the conversation, I'd think they're just trying to give me the space I need before I'm ready to talk about it. Frankly, I'd be glad if they wouldn't consider it a big deal, because it shouldn't be. They got it right where so many others did not. One of the few things I loathe about being gay is that every time I tell someone its almost always made into a big deal, as if it isn't utterly normal. I'd rather people just acknowledge it and move on to a different topic. I won't get mad or anything when people don't, I figure its part of the times we live in now, its just a bit tiresome and sometimes frustrating. I try not to make a big deal out of it myself. Of course, it doesn't feel that way when you're just starting coming out to people, it does feel like a big deal. Those feelings are, actually, much more so than coming out itself, and you deserve to talk about them, get them off your chest. If you're not given the opportunity to do that, don't wait, just take it.<br /> <br /> I'd be pissed they overheard me on the phone though and I'd definitely start inquiring about that. Nothing quite like an utterly normal domestic dispute about privacy to underline that nothing's really changed between each other. I might 'forget' to bring the OJ too, while I'm at it. Depends on if I want OJ, really...<br /> <br /> All that being said I'm afraid I'm an odd duck too. I've had numerous conversations on the topic and most people don't share my opinion and/or feelings.<br /> <br /> @Tlutha, I haven't wiki'd them yet and I cannot do so right now, same goes for the links in your post. I'll probably do so late at night when I can check it out in peace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2054-whim","name":"Whim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T03:43:16-08:00","id":61443,"title":"","content":"My personal coming out (bi/leaning pan) was almost a non-event, weirdly enough. I told my sister, who told me she was bisexual as well in response. I told my mom, she shrugged. My closest aunt was also relatively unfazed by my announcement. I'm not sure if my grandfather actually knows, as I've rarely sat down to have a real chat with the man, but my grandmother just cheerfully ignores the &quot;and men&quot; part of my sexuality and talks about future grandchildren.<br /> <br /> \u200bOf course, the local state legislature legalized gay marriage recently, so I suppose she's good on the grandkids front either way.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy sister has recently become the head of the LGBT alliance group (it has a proper name, but I'm totally blanking) at the investment firm she works for. She was super thrilled when she called to tell me. I'm proud of her.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut anyway, I'm in need of a cuddle. I'm a sad little firestorm. Being lonely sucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 08-12-2014, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T08:10:06-08:00","id":61551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=61137#post61137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish I had saved a link to a story I found a month or two ago. A kid was on the phone with his boyfriend one night, making plans to come out to his parents the next day after school, but when he woke up, they had left him a note on the fridge that went something like, &quot;We overheard you on the phone last night. No worries about coming out; just bring home some OJ when you come home. Love, your parents. PS, you and your boyfriend make a cute couple.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Here you go:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.huffpost.com/gen/1039604/thumbs/o-FATHER-SON-NOTE-COMING-OUT-facebook.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns","name":"widdershawns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T08:17:17-08:00","id":61557,"title":"","content":"Thanks for that, Widdershawns.<br /> <br /> (I'm pretty proud of how close I was.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T10:01:09-08:00","id":61604,"title":"","content":"Hmm... As for the note thing... I can't really comment too much because I did pretty similar to my stepmother when I was ten.<br /> <br /> See, she came over for christmas one year so she could propose to my mom. Naturally she came out at the same time. I happened to overhear them discussing how to tell me, and sat down and thought a while and kind of went... &quot;oh okay no that makes sense okay cool.&quot; As one might imagine, they were a little blown away to have a ten year old be utterly unfazed by her soon-to-be stepmother coming out and asking if it was okay to marry her mom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T15:47:29-08:00","id":61794,"title":"","content":"So I finally did some wiki-ing and checked out those links. I have to say there's way too much info to take in in one sitting. I'm comfortable knowing the basics so I sorta figure I'm done now, until I hit upon something that strikes me as new pushes me back into researchmode. I did find that there were some things that proved insightful and might affect my own definition of my own sexuality. On the other hand it might've confused me. It was so easy when I was still ignorant...<br /> <br /> For instance, I think I sorta 'get' polyamory (though it isn't an easy concept to wrap your head around so I might be completely off), specifically because it is concerned with romantic relationships as opposed to sexual ones. I don't really enjoy sex or even have much of a sexdrive, yet I still crave this emotional intimacy with someone (and cuddle, I crave cuddling too). I've often thought that any partner of mine should be free to have sex with others, as long as he is still committed to me (and promises to be safe out there!). I wouldn't mind if this were extended to include an emotional commitment to these others as well. I probably wouldn't have a problem doing the same, on an emotional level at least. I already know I won't have the time or energy to actually do so, so I'd basically be 'monogamous by default' but I feel like that shouldn't be much of a problem.<br /> Apparently, there's even such a thing as panromantic where you are romantically attracted to all kinds of people, as opposed to sexually. Kinda like elevating your friends to a higher level of emotional intimacy, I guess. Its hard to find the line where a friend becomes a romantic interest, but not a sexual one, but I feel like I might already be in a couple of these relationships anyway.<br /> <br /> I don't really get 'demigirl' though, or any other terms used for and by people who identify with multiple gender identities (simultaneously). I'm a guy and identify myself as such, but I realize I have some traits which are considered by most as feminine but I'm completely comfortable with them and don't apologize for them (though I do oppose traits being 'genderized' with a fiery passion. I absolutely loathe being told I'm less of a man than any other because of x trait and y behavior). What is the difference between me and a demigirl?<br /> <br /> Thanks for confusing me, Tlutha!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2054-whim","name":"Whim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T22:27:11-08:00","id":62001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=61106#post61106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tluthal, you gave me so much stuff to wiki just now...<br /> <br /> Cielle, I'm crossing my fingers for you.<br /> <br /> I came out almost two years ago to my parents, after everyone else in my life already knew and accepted it. I was terrified about how they would react to their son being gay. My uncertainty fueled my imagination, coming up with thousands of terrible scenarios. My fear and imagination kept me from coming out for so long. Before I finally did I'd made arrangements should the worst happen and I had someone I trusted with me for the strength to actually go through with it. As it turned out, it wasn't really necessary to make all these arrangements, they just said they didn't like it and that was that. It was oddly anticlimactic. To this day they pretend it isn't true, but I can deal with that. I came out for my own sake, not theirs. I didn't want their acceptance, I wanted to be freed from the burden of keeping this secret.<br /> <br /> Though the arrangements proved useless, in this case, I'm glad I made them anyway. I made sure I was financially independent and living on my own, I told them in front of someone who didn't live in their house, I made other plans for the day so that people, who I had told about my plan, would worry if I didn't show up, and take measure, I told my neighbors to call emergency services if they heard me yell. I kept my shoes and my jacket on, sat close to the door and kept a table between me and my parents, just in case I needed to make a run for it. I know, its paranoid, but its important to have some measure of stability and safety in moments when you feel insecure about the situation. Maybe you don't want to go overboard like I did, but the general advice is sound.<br /> <br /> When you're telling them, stay calm and take your time to say what you want to say. I told my parents I wanted to tell them something important and I did nothing but stare at my feet for some twenty minutes before I finally got the words out of my mouth.<br /> <br /> I hope my little story and my advice are useful to you. I wish you all the luck in the world and I hope you can draw strength, if even just a sliver, from the knowledge that there are people out there who support you no matter what happens. Stay strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is good, comprehensive advice. Honestly, I would not call you paranoid at all. Making sure you can function independently before sharing something that has ruined other parent-child relationships is just common sense.<br /> <br /> I remember asking my mother, &quot;What would you do if I was gay?&quot; She cried and said she would feel sad...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T23:22:13-08:00","id":62015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=61794#post61794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for confusing me, Tlutha!</div> </div> </div> </div>[Psst, Tlutha<b>l</b>.]<br /> <br /> You're welcome! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think you're just cis? *shrug* I have reasons for identifying as demigirl but they're not things I'm particularly comfortable discussing with people I don't know extremely well. Sorry!<br /> <br /> As for &quot;getting&quot; poly, yeah, I think you've kind of got it. I know I personally have enough emotional energy for two people, so that's what I stick to. It kinda sounds like you're ace [asexual] or gray-a. Remember that sexuality and romance are two different things. Yeah, for the majority of the population they're very similar, but for example... I tend to be more<i> physically</i> attracted to people who physically present as female or ambiguous, and more <i>emotionally</i> attracted to people who identify as male. I'm physically attracted regardless of bits and identity, but I'm generally going to get distracted by the sexy by female-presenting people more often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T02:27:44-08:00","id":62052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is good, comprehensive advice. Honestly, I would not call you paranoid at all. Making sure you can function independently before sharing something that has ruined other parent-child relationships is just common sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. To be fair I exhibit paranoid behavior in a lot of situations, its often hard for me to see when its actually appropriate and when it isn't. Stating it up front, rather than in response to someone calling it out, makes me feel like I'm more in control of the conversation. Its a topic for another thread though, one which I dare not enter! I'm just glad its useful advice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember asking my mother, &quot;What would you do if I was gay?&quot; She cried and said she would feel sad...</div> </div> </div> </div>Why did you ask if you didn't have to? I'm curious because its such a loaded question and most wouldn't bother opening that can of worms in that situation. Though your mothers answer is disappointing at least its honest and had no other consequences. That is a sign of a good relationship, I think. If you were to tell her one day I'm pretty positive she would get over the initial shock eventually and be supportive. You're lucky. Even more so considering you don't have to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tluthal</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Psst, Tlutha<b>l</b>.]</div> </div> </div> </div>Give me a break :P That post was filled with red squiglies telling me the words were bad (to the point that you could interpret it as a commentary on mainstream society's perspective)! I forgot a letter, just one letter, in that huge mess of a post!<br /> On the other hand it works... I'm not likely to make that mistake ever again! (I wanted to bold the 'l-s' in the 'Post quoted by [name]' thing for comical emphasis, but I couldn't make it work...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tluthal</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're just cis?</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn it! Will it ever stop! Now I need to wiki again!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tluthal</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrug* I have reasons for identifying as demigirl but they're not things I'm particularly comfortable discussing with people I don't know extremely well. Sorry!</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, no worries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tluthal</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for &quot;getting&quot; poly, yeah, I think you've kind of got it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wooh! At least I<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tluthal</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It kinda sounds like you're ace [asexual] or gray-a.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought I'd actually said the word asexual in my post (because you're right) but I didn't. Thanks for pointing it out. To be fair I do experience physical attraction, I just don't feel the need to act on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tluthal</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that sexuality and romance are two different things. Yeah, for the majority of the population they're very similar...</div> </div> </div> </div>I know and its very frustrating to me. Its difficult, to put it mildly, to find someone to enter into a relationship with, where both are attracted to one another, without either side being forced into doing something they don't want or abstaining from the same. A lot of the time this isn't a big deal, I can cope with it, distract myself from the loneliness but sometimes... well, not so much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tluthal</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to be more<i> physically</i> attracted to people who physically present as female or ambiguous, and more <i>emotionally</i> attracted to people who identify as male. I'm physically attracted regardless of bits and identity, but I'm generally going to get distracted by the sexy by female-presenting people more often.</div> </div> </div> </div>To extend the previous part of my post, I cannot imagine how difficult it must be for you to find someone (let alone a second) you're compatible with. I don't know, or need to, for that matter, what your current situation is, but I do want you to know that I wish for you to have that happiness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2054-whim","name":"Whim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T05:28:46-08:00","id":62089,"title":"","content":"You've probably found this out, but &quot;cis&quot; is short for &quot;cisgendered.&quot; It means whichever kind of crotch you have, your identity matches it; so if you have a woo-hoo, you're male, and if you have a hoo-ha, you're female.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T05:30:08-08:00","id":62090,"title":"","content":"Is it too weird that all my friends know that I'm gay while my family does not ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T06:26:35-08:00","id":62129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=62089#post62089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've probably found this out, but &quot;cis&quot; is short for &quot;cisgendered.&quot; It means whichever kind of crotch you have, your identity matches it; so if you have a woo-hoo, you're male, and if you have a hoo-ha, you're female.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, found out about it. I guess I am cis than.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it too weird that all my friends know that I'm gay while my family does not ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. At least, I don't think so. I told my friends before I told my family as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2054-whim","name":"Whim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T06:41:21-08:00","id":62134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=62090#post62090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it too weird that all my friends know that I'm gay while my family does not ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty normal phase, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T21:11:12-08:00","id":62713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=62052#post62052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Give me a break :P That post was filled with red squiglies telling me the words were bad (to the point that you could interpret it as a commentary on mainstream society's perspective)! I forgot a letter, just one letter, in that huge mess of a post!<br /> On the other hand it works... I'm not likely to make that mistake ever again! (I wanted to bold the 'l-s' in the 'Post quoted by [name]' thing for comical emphasis, but I couldn't make it work...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahaha, naw, it's fine. I only pointed it out because it happened in the previous post too. :3 Wasn't a big deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=62052#post62052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn it! Will it ever stop! Now I need to wiki again!</div> </div> </div> </div>NEVAR<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=62052#post62052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought I'd actually said the word asexual in my post (because you're right) but I didn't. Thanks for pointing it out. To be fair I do experience physical attraction, I just don't feel the need to act on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=62052#post62052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know and its very frustrating to me. Its difficult, to put it mildly, to find someone to enter into a relationship with, where both are attracted to one another, without either side being forced into doing something they don't want or abstaining from the same. A lot of the time this isn't a big deal, I can cope with it, distract myself from the loneliness but sometimes... well, not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can only imagine!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=62052#post62052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To extend the previous part of my post, I cannot imagine how difficult it must be for you to find someone (let alone a second) you're compatible with. I don't know, or need to, for that matter, what your current situation is, but I do want you to know that I wish for you to have that happiness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahaha, it's not really much of a problem for me? I get attracted to people regardless of gender, I just tend to get emotionally attached to guys first and physically attracted to gals first. And I'm happily in a relationship right now, not really looking for a second. My boyo and I are pretty much of the opinion that &quot;we'll deal with it when it comes up.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://tludoesart.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">Check out my art here!</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mu-Kbt6birt-A0ODsNbqabRC0PRG5brJtKl48DUou7c/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">You can see my stuff from the old forum here.</a><br /> Two Exalted Bound In Chains of the Sun","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/35-tluthal","name":"tluthal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar35_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T09:57:06-08:00","id":62959,"title":"","content":"I'm the Bacon on the LG