em, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T13:13:13-08:00","id":64254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=62090#post62090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it too weird that all my friends know that I'm gay while my family does not ?</div> </div> </div> </div>As other's said, I beliebe is pretty usual. Your friends are your familiy of choice, so to speak. All my friends know that I am bisexual but none of my family (except for a bunch of cousins that are also close friends).<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> Awwww! That little pig is so cute!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T15:56:23-08:00","id":64368,"title":"","content":"Most of the people I'm close to know that I'm bisexual, though some family members choose to completely ignore that facet of who I am, which I both accept and kinda (Kinda.) understand.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, you're darn tootin' that little piggy is cute! \u00a6(8)<br /> <img src=\"http://justcuteanimals.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/cute-animal-pictures-rabbit-kissing-piglet.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> piggy kisses. They heal Agg. damage. True story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 02-03-2014, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T07:00:02-08:00","id":65652,"title":"","content":"I'm a queergendered pan/bisexual (with biological male parts ^^). Most of my friends know it and support it even when they don't really understand what it means. My mum wasn't surprised with that. It makes talking about relationship difficult with my brother, since he is a bit edgy around those topics, but otherwise things are pretty cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T15:15:12-08:00","id":71654,"title":"","content":"So a new question for all you peoples under the rainbow flag: <b>what's your experience been with queer-oriented hangouts? Or just &quot;queer culture&quot; in general?</b><br /> <br /> While talking to my therapist today, he asked about whether I'd ever visited some of these places. And I was a bit surprised, because - having never really thought about it - I had never considered that there might be queer-oriented businesses besides gay/lesbian bars. Nope; after a quick search, there are a fair number of coffeeshops, restaurants, and yearly events which apparently draw a predominantly queer crowd. Kinda made me wonder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T03:52:02-08:00","id":71902,"title":"","content":"Never went to any myself, but a gay club called &quot;Sex Machine&quot; in my College city. And I went there because my straight friends (mostly women, and the ocasional guy loking for low guard girls) wanted to go there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":".  I had fRiends in College, not fiends :P 02-14-2014, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T06:26:28-08:00","id":71940,"title":"","content":"I climb with an LGBT climbing group (climbcrux.org) in New York. The people are great, and we have a shitton of fun. Mind you, when we climb indoors, it's not like we're the only people around, but we congregate and socialize, and I really like them. I've been climbing with them since July.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns","name":"widdershawns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T08:29:29-08:00","id":71993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=71654#post71654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While talking to my therapist today, he asked about whether I'd ever visited some of these places. And I was a bit surprised, because - having never really thought about it - I had never considered that there might be queer-oriented businesses besides gay/lesbian bars. Nope; after a quick search, there are a fair number of coffeeshops, restaurants, and yearly events which apparently draw a predominantly queer crowd. Kinda made me wonder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than spending some time in Diesel, the local Bi-Poly-Pagan-Geek hangout in Somerville, I actually haven't. While the world writ large is fairly uncomfortable with me, my friends have been nothing if not supportive of queerness, though sometimes they don't realize some of their internalized prejudices, they generally take well to instruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T03:24:29-08:00","id":72538,"title":"","content":"I dislike most 'queer-oriented hangouts' because they're 'queer-oriented'. I have no problem with the idea of a place where you can feel comfortable and safe being yourself but too often it actually is about 'being queer'. Understandable and to be expected, sure, but it seems to dominate the atmosphere. My sexual orientation/gender identity is only a facet of my personality and it really doesn't rank that high among the traits I consider most defining. For some reason, most of these places seem to foster very one-dimensional social interaction. In addition, I don't like that they're often meatmarkets for people looking for or finding sexual partners. For these reasons I usually go to 'hangouts' that cater to my interests and tastes. <br /> Its not always like that though, but it seems the good places usually don't survive for long <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2054-whim","name":"Whim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T09:32:32-08:00","id":72665,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.rollingstone.com/movies/news/ellen-page-comes-out-as-gay-with-inspiring-speech-20140215\" target=\"_blank\">Ellen Page came out.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T10:42:20-08:00","id":72700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=72665#post72665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.rollingstone.com/movies/news/ellen-page-comes-out-as-gay-with-inspiring-speech-20140215\" target=\"_blank\">Ellen Page came out.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>This is the first time I've heard that someone was gay and been surprised by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T15:33:27-08:00","id":72847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=72700#post72700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the first time I've heard that someone was gay and been surprised by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was surprised when Brian Boitano came out just before the Olympics, but that was because I thought he'd already done that years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T05:29:48-08:00","id":73138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daydreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=72665#post72665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.rollingstone.com/movies/news/ellen-page-comes-out-as-gay-with-inspiring-speech-20140215\" target=\"_blank\">Ellen Page came out.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! Look at that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm sorry for all the stress she suffered, hope she's better from now on.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T06:28:37-08:00","id":73152,"title":"","content":"I'd have sworn she made noises about or allusions to being gay not so very long ago, but trying to do a news search for it just floods me with results for the speech itself, so I guess never mind. It's not like it's important anyway when she might have implied being gay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T18:08:37-08:00","id":73483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread#post58142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I like having one of these around.<br /> <br /> * * *<br /> <br /> I came out to someone this week.<br /> <br /> It couldn't possibly have gone better than it did - she encouraged me to embrace how I was feeling and to do what makes me happy, and she reassured me that my gender/sexual identity doesn't drastically change who I am or pigeonhole me. She also talked a bit about how her own experiences went - she is herself bisexual, and leads a thoroughly interesting life besides. (Part of why I chose to come out to her first is because her adventures have distanced her from people closer to home.)<br /> <br /> It felt really, really good to talk to her about it and to receive such a warm response. I've been weighing the idea of coming out to my family, but as you might expect, that makes me very nervous. It was a bit of a struggle just bringing up these feelings with a distant friend, and I more or less knew she would be accepting and kind about it. Still, I feel a strong urge to get it out in the open. And I don't think telling my family would prompt any horrible backlash - no screaming, no disowning me, no cutting me off - but I do worry about the idea of being loved less, of being viewed as an embarrassment or tactfully ignored. (&quot;Let's not talk about Cielle's situation.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Any advice for how to tell my family I'm trans? Or about how you came out, or about coming out in general? I was planning a soft approach, and talking to one parent to start with - I've heard that being outnumbered is a recipe for problems - but I think you guys have more experience than me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cielle,<br /> <br /> While I can't speak to the nature of coming out (I'm straight), I will speak as a parent. My wife and I have both talked about this in relation to our children <i>(A 9-yo girl, 6-yo boy -- &quot;physically&quot; that is...to be determined by them as life moves on...they are who they decide they are after all...)</i>, and we have both decided that to us as long as our children are happy, then we're cool. We, as parents are doing our best to keep our &quot;lines of communication open&quot;<i> (that's &quot;olde foaggie&quot; for talking <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</i> them and not at them. I don't know you're family, but maybe sitting down and just talking with them might be the best? Or...maybe some sort of surprise for them (A Cake w/message, a Painting or sorts, etc??)?? You know them best, but I've always believed that being up front and honest is the best way to do things.<br /> <br /> Anyway, good luck, and know that there are plenty of people out here <i>(Of all types)</i> who support you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Blessed Be.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T08:55:29-08:00","id":77665,"title":"","content":"Told my mom. Wish I hadn't. She didn't take it horribly or anything, but I've still felt like crap since then, questioning myself quite a bit. Going to talk to my therapist about antidepressants, see if those might help on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T09:55:39-08:00","id":77701,"title":"","content":"How did she take it, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T23:53:47-08:00","id":80062,"title":"","content":"Thanks for making this thread, Cielle. You're right, it is nice to have one of these just to talk about stuff.<br /> <br /> Wherever you are in your path of self realization I hope you have a good support network. That includes us here, if I may speak for the board.<br /> <br /> I hope that, whatever you choose to identify as, you feel comfortable in your own skin. That's the most important thing. Labels are useful because they help our minds get wrapped around the complexity of reality, but in the end it is more important that you feel comfortable with the complex chaos that is reality, both external and internal.<br /> <br /> Some days there's no telling what your internal universe if going to throw at you, but if you use your own comfort or faith in your ability to weather whatever comes your way as a lodestone, you should be able to make it.<br /> <br /> You be you, there's nothing more beautiful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for me, I'm pretty comfortable living in the label of gay man. Been with my husband since 2001, married since 2008. As an old married couple, we don't really go out to strictly &quot;gay&quot; places anymore and didn't even when we were dating. I appreciate that they exist, but don't frequent them myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T15:13:51-08:00","id":80547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=71654#post71654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a new question for all you peoples under the rainbow flag: <b>what's your experience been with queer-oriented hangouts? Or just &quot;queer culture&quot; in general?</b><br /> <br /> While talking to my therapist today, he asked about whether I'd ever visited some of these places. And I was a bit surprised, because - having never really thought about it - I had never considered that there might be queer-oriented businesses besides gay/lesbian bars. Nope; after a quick search, there are a fair number of coffeeshops, restaurants, and yearly events which apparently draw a predominantly queer crowd. Kinda made me wonder.</div> </div> </div> </div>My experience has been good. Here's the thing: If you are popular in general, you'll be popular in a queer social space. If you're shy, nervous, and awkward in general, that's not going to change when you're around a group of non-straight/cigendered types.<br /> <br /> Ironically, the people who need such spaces least tend to get the most out of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T02:11:25-08:00","id":83877,"title":"","content":"I'm in agreement with Ophidimancer. Thank you very much for making this thread, as it would be odd for a &quot;straight guy&quot; <i>(more labels, as Ophidimancer mentioned)</i> to bring up LGBT issues.<br /> <br /> And as a &quot;straight guy&quot; <i>(and an old one at that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)</i> I think it's good to talk sometimes, even if it's just &quot;shooting the breeze.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Cielle, I hope you are feeling better...and here is something that I hope will cheer you up.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://cdn.viralnova.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/07/cat-hugs9.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Because everyone is a beautiful person, and everyone deserves to be happy.<br /> <br /> Peace.<br /> <br /> <br /> ~ N","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is timing in everything. Timing in strategy cannot be mastered without a great deal of practice. There is also timing in the Void. You win battles with the timing in the Void born of the timing of cunning by knowing the enemies' timing, and thus using a timing which the enemy does not expect.&quot; <i>Shinmen Musashi no Kami Fujiwara no Genshin, Go Rin No Sho (The Book of the Five Rings)</i>","edited":{"userid":2141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","user":"Nadrakas","date":". 03-04-2014, 05:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2141-nadrakas","name":"Nadrakas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T00:53:25-08:00","id":85167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=72538#post72538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dislike most 'queer-oriented hangouts' because they're 'queer-oriented'. I have no problem with the idea of a place where you can feel comfortable and safe being yourself but too often it actually is about 'being queer'. Understandable and to be expected, sure, but it seems to dominate the atmosphere. My sexual orientation/gender identity is only a facet of my personality and it really doesn't rank that high among the traits I consider most defining. For some reason, most of these places seem to foster very one-dimensional social interaction. In addition, I don't like that they're often meatmarkets for people looking for or finding sexual partners. For these reasons I usually go to 'hangouts' that cater to my interests and tastes.<br /> Its not always like that though, but it seems the good places usually don't survive for long <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I see this sometimes. That's why it seems more comfortable in areas with just larger percentage of LGBT, like hang outs in college campuses and the like. For instance it seems RPGs seem to have a disproportionate amount of LGBT players, and it isn't an activity about sexual orientation/gender identity but because there are a lot of LGBT folks playing or tagging along it generally promotes a comfortable atmosphere. And it seems kind of just a coincidence that many of my players are LBGT because often people joined my games by word of mouth and being a friend of a friend, and often never having played a Pen and Paper RPG before.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never really gone to a genuinely &quot;queer-friendly&quot; establishment before, but I'm aware that there are a few in the city nearest my town. I'm generally very shy, but I've been seriously considering going to one of these places just to see if I'm comfortable. It would be so nice to be open about my sexuality and other sex/gender particulars while socializing for a change.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's sad. My I grew in a small town and one of my best friends was gay and it seemed to take its toll on him for growing up in a small town. Meanwhile when I moved to a larger town for college many of the LGBT friends I had there were quite happy to be able to just be free about there identity and finally having people to talk to about it, even if they weren't LGBT themselves the atmosphere of acceptance was something that was quite relieving to many of them.<br /> <br /> I hope find a friendly atmosphere somewhere. Hell its nice for anyone to find just generally friendly accepting places. Its a nice salve for the old anxiety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T07:18:43-08:00","id":85290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is a subject that I would be very interested in seeing opinions, anecdotes and ideas regarding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not bring up the topic of sexuality in front of real people (as opposed to internet people; I can talk about pretty much anything with someone I'm incapable of looking in the eye). I'm uncomfortable with it. I don't bring up sexual orientation either, because even though it's not the same thing as sexuality, it's close enough that I don't want to open the door for a conversation about the sex people like to have. There are only maybe three real people in the world I trust and am comfortable enough with to feel no shame or panic at learning details of their sex lives, so between that and the fact that I have no gaydar, what I can say is made of more caveats than actual statements.<br /> <br /> For instance, almost everyone I have ever roleplayed with has been in a heterosexual relationship at the time. That in and of itself is not proof of heterosexuality, but of the maybe fifty roleplaying partners I've had, they've all been in a straight relationship. I only know of one person who, after I stopped gaming with her (and stopped talking to her entirely because the bitch owes me six hundred bucks she refuses to pay back, instead insisting that my best friend shoulder the debt, which he has agreed to for reasons I'll never understand), declared herself gay.<br /> <br /> I'm a little surprised that, of all the people I'd played with, I only have proof of one of them being anything other than straight. This is particularly peculiar to me since I live in a town with two colleges and one university, so we pull in a lot of out-of-towners who are, if stereotypes are to be believed, in a stage where they experiment with their sexual orientations. I assume a big part of the issue is living in Missouri, where our state policies are pretty solidly homophobic, so gay or gay-curious people either don't come here or stay in the closet. I also assume that if those experimenting kids are around, they're too busy experimenting and/or going to school to come to play D&amp;D with me and chat about their orientations.<br /> <br /> As a perhaps final note about the roleplaying environment I live in, this area is, as I've said before several times in the past, Pathfinder country. That is the only game in town. No one wants to play anything else. I don't know what correlation Pathfinder has with alternate sexualities, if any; the only time I've ever seen the topic brought up is in a player resource for a published adventure path which included a romance mechanic for four important NPCs whom the GM were encouraged to treat as bisexual. Compared to a game like Exalted, whose new edition will have a trans person as a signature character, I treat the lack of discussion on the topic as an assumption that players and characters are all hetero.<br /> <br /> I'd actually like to talk about Exalted's upcoming Prince Diamond in some more detail, but later. I got shit to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T07:47:47-08:00","id":85317,"title":"","content":"I have to wonder if there's any correlation between the RPG and the percentage of LGBT players. I mean, I know White Wolf has always been not just accepting, but active in making sure there was regular use of gay characters in their books, and so was always a draw for people I knew. But what about other games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns","name":"widdershawns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T09:39:58-08:00","id":85411,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of interesting conversations going in this thread, but I wanted to go ahead and say what makes my gender/orientation identity because I don't get to talk about it too much.<br /> <br /> In the shortest form, I'm cissex male, gender-neutral, pansexual, and (maybe) biromantic.<br /> <br /> To break that down ... <br /> <br /> <b>Cissex male:</b> I feel comfortable being physically male or, in other words, having boy parts and male secondary sexual features like facial hair, larger hands/feet/joints, etc. That feels correct to me. However . . . <br /> <br /> <b>Gender neutral:</b> . . . I don't have any inward internalization of any of that. Put another way, I have no inner sense of maleness or any kind of male identity. This means a lot of things, but most practically, I don't have any instant sympathy for other men nor instant friction with other women. There's just no substance to that kind of identity. (As a strange aside, sexism didn't make sense to me for a long time because I was all, &quot;. . . but we're all people. Why would gender identity matter?&quot; I'm still that way to a significant degree.)<br /> <br /> <b>Pansexual:</b> I'm sexually attracted to people of nearly every gender identity and sexual feature configuration you can think of: pre-op transwomen, men, women, androgynous biomales ... Not androgynous biofemales, though, go figure. There is a lot more gradation and specifics within each of those categories, but that's the short version.<br /> <br /> <b>Biromantic:</b> This means that I have had romantic feelings for and could pursue romantic relationships with both men and women. I put &quot;maybe&quot; with this because I have emotional hang-ups about dating men that I'm working to get over, I've only dated women so far, and I have yet to meet a nonbinary person for whom I felt romantically.<br /> <br /> Hope that all made sense!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T09:47:44-08:00","id":85416,"title":"","content":"So, funny thing, I think I've got anecdotes from both sides.<br /> <br /> When I was participating in LARPs regularly, we had at least 3 or 4 people who were part of the LGBT crowd in each different LARP group. Granted, sometimes it was some of the same people, but not always. One was in the middle of gender reassignment while participating, so he played a female character until he was a she.<br /> <br /> But when it came to the table top groups I played in, it's pretty much the same thing JimB was just saying - lots of hetero relationships and no one giving any indication they were interested in anything else. Nobody ever bothered playing another gender (except the ST, of course, who has no choice).<br /> <br /> So, maybe there's a different crowd drawn in when the &quot;gateway&quot; is different. Table top brings in the suburbanite crowd. LARP brings in the metropolitan crowd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T06:35:33-08:00","id":85969,"title":"","content":"I taught a roleplaying workshop to a bunch of highschoolers at MIT in 1999. When the concept of in-character sexuality was brought up (particularly relevant since we had both boys and girls playing), all of the girls pondered what sort of sexuality their character might have -- &quot;I think I'll play a bisexual.&quot; - &quot;Ooh, I'll play a lesbian&quot; -- and the boys were all trying to convince me that their characters was straighter than all of the other boys' characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T11:43:15-08:00","id":86904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=85969#post85969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I taught a roleplaying workshop to a bunch of highschoolers at MIT in 1999. When the concept of in-character sexuality was brought up (particularly relevant since we had both boys and girls playing), all of the girls pondered what sort of sexuality their character might have -- &quot;I think I'll play a bisexual.&quot; - &quot;Ooh, I'll play a lesbian&quot; -- and the boys were all trying to convince me that their characters was straighter than all of the other boys' characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is somehow both illuminating and adorable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42-aranis","name":"Aranis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar42_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T13:54:25-08:00","id":86985,"title":"","content":"I took him as meaning it's relevant because of the gender divide among the responses, but now that you mention it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T02:52:43-07:00","id":143245,"title":"","content":"Hi, I simply declare myself as bisexual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T14:20:59-07:00","id":166222,"title":"","content":"Never give someone a FOURTH chance to participate in a healthy relationship. I just adopted the three strikes rule. ......<br /> <br /> Also, my aunt asked if, by chance, my ongoing psychiatric problems were really a &quot;cry for help because you're having trouble coming out as gay&quot;.<br /> ....WHAT in the flying fuckballs? I came out as bisexual+ YEARS AGO.<br /> Yes, I just typed bisexual+. Just invented the term. Seems to fit.<br /> <br /> So, I've been out of the loop recently, and I'm at the point where me being anythingsexual is the LEAST of my concerns, but I'm forced to reiterate and confirm my orientation just to avoid weird theories being traded like pokemon cards amongst my family members.<br /> <br /> Oh, and that sister I mentioned has effectively ruined any pride I took in being related to them. LGBT related breakup? Sister went back to women? Fuck no.<br /> Just stole her roommate's/best friend's fiance, dumped the husband (he chose Me to be his Best Man. He has 4 brothers and more than a few dudefriends.) and used me as a Patsy by making everyone visiting their house the weekend I came to visit think I was gunning to move in on her friend.<br /> So, I just turned around and told her friend (VtM and WtA player, all around nice lady) what was going on.<br /> <br /> A shitstorm followed.<br /> <br /> I found out that my sister decided to blame me for telling the truth to a person who, in my eyes, was being casually victimized, through Facebook. The Fuck, reality? Being Facebook-Disowned is a thing?!??","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 08-12-2014, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T20:45:59-07:00","id":166511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=85416#post85416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, funny thing, I think I've got anecdotes from both sides.<br /> <br /> When I was participating in LARPs regularly, we had at least 3 or 4 people who were part of the LGBT crowd in each different LARP group. Granted, sometimes it was some of the same people, but not always. One was in the middle of gender reassignment while participating, so he played a female character until he was a she.<br /> <br /> But when it came to the table top groups I played in, it's pretty much the same thing JimB was just saying - lots of hetero relationships and no one giving any indication they were interested in anything else. Nobody ever bothered playing another gender (except the ST, of course, who has no choice).<br /> <br /> So, maybe there's a different crowd drawn in when the &quot;gateway&quot; is different. Table top brings in the suburbanite crowd. LARP brings in the metropolitan crowd.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's weird but other than a few of my characters most of my games have been very devoid of relationships to the point where it's practically asexual. It's been mostly mystery focused though so I guess it can hamper on the relationship aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T04:38:37-07:00","id":166848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=166222#post166222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and that sister I mentioned has effectively ruined any pride I took in being related to them. LGBT related breakup? Sister went back to women? Fuck no.<br /> Just stole her roommate's/best friend's fiance, dumped the husband (he chose Me to be his Best Man. He has 4 brothers and more than a few dudefriends.) and used me as a Patsy by making everyone visiting their house the weekend I came to visit think I was gunning to move in on her friend.<br /> So, I just turned around told her friend (VtM and WtA player, all around nice lady) what was going on.<br /> <br /> A shitstorm followed.<br /> <br /> I found out that my sister decided to blame me for telling the truth to a person who, in my eyes, was being casually victimized, through Facebook. The Fuck, reality? Being Facebook-Disowned is a THING??? I got unfriended and the<br /> n it's &quot;I don't have a brother anymore.&quot; on the phone. End of story. All parties involved have chosen to simply act as if they'd never met me, even the new gaming enthusiasts I was introduced to and told I had befriended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for what happened. I'll make an assumption, but people who behave like assholes, act that way regardless their sexuality. And yes, it can happen to relatives as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Love is weird. Why do I date women and daydream about cuddling comforting men? Why do I date habitual cheaters of BOTH genders? I'm so tired of this monotonous, binary bullshit.<br /> <br /> Orientation: Anyone who would love me genuinely. I'd dig up the fucking Elephant Man if I thought the zombie bones of Joseph Merrick would have me.<br /> <br /> I feel so alone. Why is everything so confusing? Maybe I'm just confused. </div> </div> </div>Well yes, you don't need to care about the gender, but you should go after the person (or person<b>s</b>) who makes you feel the best.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If my homophobic dad knew I was anything but straight, he'd try to bash my head in. I'm at a breaking point. I can't be me. I can't be someone else. I can't be anything. ...so, I'm nothing. Not Nobody, of course. I like Nobody. I don't like the nothing I am. I just want love and a tiny bit of understanding. Nothing wants to be something. Nothing ever changes. Nothing. The new me.<br /> <br /> Hi, I'm _____and I ____. Problem solved.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf anyone needs me, just... just kidding. I'm unnecessary. </div> </div> </div>I understand you are a bit confused. That happened to me sometimes too. Perhaps you should look up to your priorities and what you really look for, and act on it. Of course you need to be careful (especially with your father), and look for people who you can trust.<br /> <br /> May I suggest you to watch a LGBT channels on Youtube? I found &quot;GirlfriendsTV&quot; to be really helpful for these kind of things. While Arielle is lesbian, her channel is about all kind of sexualities, and some of the difficulties LGBT people might have to encounter emotionally and about relationships. She covered emotional wounds, trust, bisexuality, pansexuality and affection and things like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: A virtual hug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 06-12-2014, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T05:07:23-07:00","id":166857,"title":"","content":"What is Froggy's deal...<br /> <br /> Gay. Male. A &quot;Bear&quot; if you are familiar with that group...<br /> <br /> I came out to myself when I started going to college. I secretly knew I was gay all through high school, and some of my classmates picked up on it (even though I am not particularly effeminate, I do tend to wear my emotions on my sleeve and the school bullies picked up on that. I denied it to myself and everyone else until I was able to get myself out of that environment.<br /> <br /> I kind of wish I could go back and do it again, only out and proud, because as near as I can tell I had nothing to lose. I tried my damnedest to be as anonymous as possible, and I suppose I was scared that I might get even more attention and negative... I don't know...<br /> <br /> It took me a long time to come out to my gaming group. I knew they would approve, but the fact that I hadn't gotten the courage to do so already in its own way just made it harder. Plus, when it was game time it was all business, so it was kind of hard to find a moment to say... &quot;Awesome, natural 20! By the way, I prefer to have sex with other men, if anyone was wondering.&quot;<br /> <br /> I met my BF, who I will refer to as CMS to protect the guilty, shortly before that. He was the one that actually introduced me to the whole &quot;bear&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Basically, Bears are kind of a gay male subculture, which instead of preferring men who are smooth/shaven, thin, or athletically built (what our culture as a whole holds up as what an attractive male is supposed to look like) prefer men who have body hair, beards, body fat and/or muscles. We have lots of stupid names for lots of different body shapes and types<br /> <br /> My experience with Bears has actually been somewhere between positive and negative.<br /> <br /> On the positive side, I think bears have actually changed what I see as attractive to a degree? Or perhaps just invited me to explore what I felt was attractive about other body types that I hadn't considered before... It's actually pretty hard to tell, as it was so gradual, and makes me wonder how much control the media really has over what we find attractive. While I think most people would put what we find attractive strictly in the realm of biology, I think media and culture plays a much larger part than most people would guess.<br /> <br /> Sorry, tangent.<br /> <br /> Also, it was the first time in my entire life someone had told me I was attractive.<br /> <br /> On the negative side, it seems the Bear community, or the bear community that is easy to find, lean heavily toward polyamory and open relationships, whereas I am more of a monogamous kind of guy.<br /> <br /> My experience with bears in person has been somewhat negative as well... When CMS and I started dating, he took me to a local bear mens group. My experiences with that group were less than positive, such as the organizer's boyfriend who couldn't keep his hands to himself, and a trip to a cabin in Des Moines that made me feel out of place, like I had stepped out of my life and into somebody else's... Being in my early 20's, surrounded by much older men, all over one another... one guy (who I didn't know) noticed I was tense, and tried to make me feel more comfortable by giving me a shoulder massage... It didn't help. That night I couldn't sleep, over the sounds of sex downstairs... they had even given CMS and I the best bed in the house, but that just made me feel even more awkward and out of place. I would have left, but my car was pinned in, and I don't think CMS ever did understood how I felt that night. I was upset and he was upset that I was upset, not to mention that I never wanted to go on that trip in the first place, but only went because CMS basically begged me to go...<br /> <br /> So, the whole Bear thing has been both a blessing and a curse... Great idea, but not a fan of the community as a whole.<br /> <br /> CMS and I were together for 10 years. We had a good 5 years and a bad 5 years. Right there in the middle I discovered CMS had been cybering with another guy (CMS had wanted an open relationship from the start, but I insisted on monogamy) and I was left to try to pick up the pieces. Any time I brought the issue up, he deflected the whole issue by talking about how the guy he cyber cheated on with and I needed to &quot;make up and be friends again.&quot; Which I never understood because he and I were never friends to begin with. He forced a confrontation, and I ended up saying some rather cruel things to said &quot;friend&quot;.<br /> <br /> Nothing ended up getting resolved, but I did end up giving CMS my trust again, because I loved him, but the relationship felt broken from then on. He even asked me to marry him at one point, and I turned him down. Years later CMS did it again, and feeling hollow inside, I ended the relationship.<br /> <br /> Right now I am back living with my parents, trying to figure out what to do next. CMS has found someone new, and I am happy for him, but also a little jealous... he found a great guy who was able to give him the open relationship he wanted, while I am stuck alone without prospects trying to figure out what my next move is going to be. I know it's time to live for me, but I guess I haven't figured out what that entails yet...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","user":"Froggy711","date":". 06-12-2014, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T09:31:33-07:00","id":166989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=166857#post166857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now I am back living with my parents, trying to figure out what to do next. CMS has found someone new, and I am happy for him, but also a little jealous... he found a great guy who was able to give him the open relationship he wanted, while I am stuck alone without prospects trying to figure out what my next move is going to be. I know it's time to live for me, but I guess I haven't figured out what that entails yet...</div> </div> </div> </div>General advice? The biggest thing is getting comfortable with the idea that you might be alone. If you go out hunting for a relationship without that, it will continually cause problems, because you're looking for &quot;The One&quot;. Strive to be comfortable with the idea that you are yourself, and that even if things don't work out and you are alone, that's okay.<br /> <br /> Reach that point and you can focus on relationships without the trying to settle down drive, without fear of &quot;what if it doesn't work out&quot; driving you to keep it alive even if it's not working.<br /> <br /> It's kinda a glib thing to say, but it's not easy. But it is what I'd suggest anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":31,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","user":"Odd_Canuck","date":". 06-12-2014, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T09:40:37-07:00","id":166996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=166989#post166989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest thing is getting comfortable with the idea that you might be alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>This x 1000","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T16:39:08-07:00","id":167342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=166989#post166989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">General advice? The biggest thing is getting comfortable with the idea that you might be alone. If you go out hunting for a relationship without that, it will continually cause problems, because you're looking for &quot;The One&quot;. Strive to be comfortable with the idea that you are yourself, and that even if things don't work out and you are alone, that's okay.<br /> <br /> Reach that point and you can focus on relationships without the trying to settle down drive, without fear of &quot;what if it doesn't work out&quot; driving you to keep it alive even if it's not working.<br /> <br /> It's kinda a glib thing to say, but it's not easy. But it is what I'd suggest anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're absolutely right. I do miss being in a relationship, but I can definitely see how my desire to be in a relationship can sabotage things... I think part of the reason CMS and I were together for so long was because I was scared of being alone. That said my experience online so far has been that I don't have a whole lot of prospects in this area. Which makes me want to move to greener pastures, but beyond my desire for a relationship I don't really have any reason to move.<br /> <br /> The big question in my life right now seems to be &quot;So now what?&quot; I was thinking yesterday that maybe I need to pick up my life right where I left off before I met CMS. Go back to school... get a degree... and see where that takes me. OTOH, it does seem to be rather late in my life (I'm 33) to be trying to get a degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T07:52:18-07:00","id":167915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=167342#post167342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big question in my life right now seems to be &quot;So now what?&quot; I was thinking yesterday that maybe I need to pick up my life right where I left off before I met CMS. Go back to school... get a degree... and see where that takes me. OTOH, it does seem to be rather late in my life (I'm 33) to be trying to get a degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's never too late. I'm 34, and I'm going back to school in the fall for a pharmacy degree that I won't actually see until I'm 40. It's still totally worth it!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns","name":"widdershawns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T09:12:08-07:00","id":167966,"title":"","content":"Myself, I'm a bi (but mostly gay) geek bear in late 20's. I'm having on and off partner from over 3 years. Sometimes I love this guy, sometimes I just want to kil... get over him. None the less, I'm loving him much more than my previous girlfriend and her I loved A LOT.<br /> <br /> The Gay Bears are like this! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://scontent-b-fra.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfa1/t1.0-9/313783_1815952133454_975099372_n.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> And a movement has history like this... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://fbcdn-sphotos-f-a.akamaihd.net/hphotos-ak-prn2/t1.0-9/1450753_10200443205037562_800977353_n.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T11:44:54-07:00","id":168120,"title":"","content":"<br /> Imma go find someone special to cuddle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 08-12-2014, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T11:55:39-07:00","id":168130,"title":"","content":"Virtual hugs!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 08-12-2014, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T08:58:05-07:00","id":171677,"title":"","content":"I forgot to introduce myself. I'm a 24 year Italian old boy. I've always had the impression women weren't THAT interesting to me, though I did prefer girl's company because they were less of an asshole, compared to male schoolmates, at least up to junior high school. Plus, horrible dreams about the cross, being crucified and Jesus going after me to punish me for my sins, tormented me up until about when I turned 21 yo.<br /> <br /> My family is loving and while religious, it's quite tolerant and permissive. It's not like I asked much anyways. I've also always been both introverted and <u>attention whore</u> at the same time. I feel bad during parties when people do not pay attention to me, any kind of attention, positive or negative.<br /> <br /> I realized my sexual orientation while fantasizing about a whipping session between the protagonist from Gothic 1 (the sub) and a female NPC of the videogame (the mistress). I understood I was keeping attention only to the male character. It was about the same period when I realized I was an atheist.<br /> So, after being bullied for being weak during the three years of junior high school, I spent my first years of high school desperate for my future. I was a closeted gay atheist. I didn't fear my family THAT much.<br /> <br /> What I did fear was the possibility I'd die alone. I viewed my existence as meaningless. <i>Humans are born to procreate, but I'm not willing to go with a woman</i>, <i>so</i> <i>what's my purpose?</i>, I thought. Plus, being introverted and having no contact with gay people was discouraging, and led me to think I would never find anyone who loves me.<br /> I was continually thinking about death. My reasoning was that if I had no purpose, there was no use in doing anything. Plus, while an atheist, I still feared religion, and the dreams where still there.<br /> <br /> About 2007 I had my first short relationship with a dickish bisexual older boy. About 2008 I came out to my parents, because I was having really bad marks at school, and my mind was focused on a school crush I had. And because I wanted them to care about me instead of attacking me. And because I'm an <u>attention whore</u>.<br /> My parents didn't react particularily bad, so that was useless. I also came out to my school crush, in vain. And that ended my darkest period (which compared to other people might actually seem not that dark).<br /> About 2009 I started to connect with gay people more thanks to my best friend coming out to me and introducing me to his friends. About 2011 I got rid of religion, my scary dreams.<br /> <br /> From then on, I live my life telling myself that &quot;life's meaning is what you make out of it&quot;. I stopped whining and started living. Now I'm dating a man which is about 40 yo, and I was questioning myself if dating someone who's that much older is good for me. But...I don't really care that much anymore. Life is short, and I should live it how I want it.<br /> <br /> As long as it works, I'll be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 06-17-2014, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T06:42:24-07:00","id":174070,"title":"","content":"The Congress of my country just revise the marriage law today, and refuse/ignore to legalize gay marriage, saying something along the line of &quot;it's not real marriage&quot;. I always though my country or Singapore would be the first Asian country to legalize gay marriage but it's seem like such a pipe dream now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T06:58:32-07:00","id":174084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=174070#post174070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Congress of my country just revise the marriage law today, and refuse/ignore to legalize gay marriage, saying something along the line of &quot;it's not real marriage&quot;. I always though my country or Singapore would be the first Asian country to legalize gay marriage but it's seem like such a pipe dream now.</div> </div> </div> </div>/hugs<br /> <br /> I'm sure it will happen. Not necessarily just now. These things eventually become a torrent, and once the floodgates are open, they work themselves into every aspect of life. At least, that's my view. I'm an optimist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns","name":"widdershawns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T09:38:46-07:00","id":174221,"title":"","content":"In Poland they don't even want give us Civil Partnerships... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T11:39:59-07:00","id":174379,"title":"","content":"Sorry, Jen and wyrdhamster. That sucks pretty harsh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T12:00:45-07:00","id":174410,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone, just introducing myself. I'm pansexual and gender-fluid with generally more feminine leanings, but unfortunately have to present entirely male most of the time. I'm an actor professionally, and as a business where appearance is everything, I can get turned down for an acting job for reasons that would absolutely never fly in any other business. So even though I would ideally like to take estrogen and present generally more feminine most of the time, it's just not a realistic option for me. In part because I make a reasonably attractive man, and despite my partner's assurances I don't feel at all confident about my appearance when I present how I would like to, but also because I'm already established as a male actor and transitioning would dramatically change the kind of roles I would be considered for. I also have a really deep voice, which would be a big obstacle to getting female roles if I did transition. And on top of all that, I've basically spent my entire life learning to pretend to be someone I'm not and be damn convincing at it, so I have an incredibly easy time living in the closet in my professional life. It's a little disheartening to not be able to be myself at work, but at the same time, being someone else is pretty much my job description, and it's something I came to accept a long time ago. In my personal life though, I am pretty open about my gender. I don't think my family really &quot;gets it&quot;, even though I've come out to them. They're very open-minded and accepting, and were totally fine with my identity and sexuality, but since I generally dress and act in a typically male manner, I'm not sure they entirely understand. Luckily my partner is incredibly supportive, and makes me happy to be who I am, which helps me not get beaten down by the necessity to constantly hide my identity. It also helps to have places like this I can come to and not be judged by my appearance. So thanks to everyone here for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T11:38:11-07:00","id":184971,"title":"","content":"^^^And won't happen soon since Law and Justice and Congress of New Right are on rise. I wonder how much time it will take for people to get disillusioned with the conservative right and elect more progressive politicians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T13:13:13-07:00","id":204127,"title":"","content":"Dear Santa Claus,<br /> <br /> I want a shiny. Wait, never mind. Me found my shiny!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 08-12-2014, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","tit