ember/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T20:32:06-07:00","id":204608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=204600#post204600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm hurting because I want someone I have feelings for to hold me, and I know that they never will. People have prayed for milder pains than that to be relieved.<br /> <br /> /self-pity</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure it counts as self-pity when I asked you like three times to tell me. You probably get a pass under those circumstances.<br /> <br /> Sorry about your love life.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T21:54:17-07:00","id":204659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=204600#post204600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I've had a lot of changes in my life in the last few months, especially regarding the personal relationships in my life. I was left by my fiance, who was rather gender fluid in private. I was almost often the &quot;girl&quot; in the relationship as she was, really. I mourned that relationship and am trying to move on. I'm not entirely sure if I'm done missing them, but that's life.<br /> <br /> Since then, I've completely humiliated myself in front of the only woman I found attractive in my distant social circle, and we haven't spoken since. Simultaneously, I find myself developing romantic feelings, to the point of sappy saccharine daydreaming, for some of my male acquaintances and friends. I know that those feelings are destined to go completely unrequited and they'll likely lead me to more sadness if I try to pursue them. That hurts me. It hurts for many reasons, but I think I'll save all that heartache for a rant in the Hate thread someday.<br /> <br /> So, I'm hurting because I want someone I have feelings for to hold me, and I know that they never will. People have prayed for milder pains than that to be relieved.<br /> <br /> /self-pity</div> </div> </div> </div>If it makes you feel better you're not in any way alone in being in that sort of situation. Many, I dare say most people have been at that low point in a romantic life.<br /> <br /> All I can really do is offer you the same advice I got that worked well. Stop thinking about being in a relationship, instead focus on making yourself content with your own life by yourself. As you improve, start to make efforts to deliberately broaden your social circles and meet people and possibly friends. Become comfortable and generally good possibilities open up. If on the other hand, you go out looking for relationships while in a desperate for love/attention/bonding mindset you're mostly going to attract people that either want to &quot;fix&quot; you of the problem, on whom you'll end up emotionally dependent, or else people that intentionally or otherwise seek to use it as an avenue of control or abuse.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T22:36:55-07:00","id":204684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=204659#post204659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it makes you feel better you're not in any way alone in being in that sort of situation. Many, I dare say most people have been at that low point in a romantic life.<br /> <br /> All I can really do is offer you the same advice I got that worked well. Stop thinking about being in a relationship, instead focus on making yourself content with your own life by yourself. As you improve, start to make efforts to deliberately broaden your social circles and meet people and possibly friends. Become comfortable and generally good possibilities open up. If on the other hand, you go out looking for relationships while in a desperate for love/attention/bonding mindset you're mostly going to attract people that either want to &quot;fix&quot; you of the problem, on whom you'll end up emotionally dependent, or else people that intentionally or otherwise seek to use it as an avenue of control or abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to emphatically agree with this. I always hate having to give the cliche &quot;you have to be happy with yourself before you can be happy with someone else&quot; consolation, because I've been in that position before and I remember hearing that same advice. I remember what absolute bullshit that sounded like coming from people who were in healthy, loving relationships, and how sick I would get of being told to love myself before trying to love someone else. It was absolutely infuriating, and so I can't help but cringe every time I have to give someone that same advice that I used to hate to hear. But the truth is, it worked for me. The moment I gave up on trying to find a relationship and decided to actually try to enjoy being single instead of looking for the next relationship, I suddenly found myself in the best relationship of my life. Now, my experience is obviously not going to be the same as anyone else's, but it really is true that when you are actively looking for a relationship, the ones you find tend not to work well, for the reasons Old Canuck explained. If you're not trying to fulfill a desire for a relationship, you have no need to compromise to achieve that goal, so if you do find yourself in one, it will only be because it truly makes you happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T08:57:37-07:00","id":205005,"title":"","content":"So I totally should've mentioned this before this weekend, but I just got back from an event called Homoclimbtastic, which is a gathering of LGBT climbers in West Virginia for an extended weekend in July, and if any of you fun gays/etc climb, it might be a thing you should consider for next year. (there are requirements for climbing level and such...if you wanna know....ask me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns","name":"widdershawns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T05:37:43-07:00","id":216681,"title":"","content":"Eh, I somehow just accidentally come-out to my mom when she ask me to stop posting male pictures on my ahem.......FB page (don't laugh at me T-T ). It went better than I expected nyan nyan :3<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"J