8-24T10:24:01-07:00","id":239310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=239160#post239160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that I'm new to this thread, but hey.<br /> <br /> I just wanted to give you a hug, man. I'm sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I appreciate it. I'm trying to have another guy come over - not someone I'm really attracted to and I know I'm his second choice but I'm just lonely and desperate to be with someone. Anyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=239169#post239169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, that sucks. Did you express to your roommate your feelings about the matter? Maybe he didn't know. Either way, it sucks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to after the guy leaves; they're still in his bedroom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=239177#post239177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, don't put yourself down like that, I think you're a beautiful man !</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I don't often feel that way but I appreciate the compliment <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=239181#post239181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, Wulf. Sometimes people are dicks like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>My roommate is a good guy, he doesn't mean to be a dick. So I can't really be mad at him, just at the situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amadeu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=239201#post239201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but most of the times it works perfectly. Met my partner there. We r together now for 1 year and a half. Best relationship ever!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're one of the lucky ones. The guys I meet on there are either way older than me or way younger (and looking just for a hookup). Everyone around my age is already in a relationship or they won't even give me the time of day like I'm some kind of deformed wildebeast.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T11:25:22-07:00","id":239374,"title":"","content":"@wulf : I hope this guy can cheer you up.<br /> <br /> So, I've read through the whole thread, and I figured that I should share my own tale.<br /> <br /> I am a bisexual man. I know that since I'm 16. I'm more attracted to men than women, but I don't really know if I should consider myself gay. In fact, it's kinda weird. When I think about a man, I think about having sex with him. When I'm attracted to a woman, I don't really fantasize about sleeping with her, but I have an easier time envisioning a lasting relationship. But I don't really have any ground to compare. I've only had one girlfriend two years ago, and what we had was hardly a relationship. Our first kiss was two months after our first date, and we didn't really see each other. In fact, I'm still a virgin at 23. Never had any boyfriend. Had and have some crushes on friends, but I know they're straight or not interested in men anymore. I only know three gay guys, and the only one living near my city is 15 years older than me.<br /> I'd like to be free, and I envy those who can have one-night-stand, or even short relationships. But I can't. First of all, I'm desperately romantic, and I have trouble flirting with people. It's awkward, and friends keep telling me I'm too subtle in my clues. And I've only been hit on once, and by a druken guy : I'm suffering from the Nice Guy Syndrome. People find me funny, and nice, but apparently I'm no Boyfriend Material. Also, when it comes to men, I have trouble identifying myself with the LGBT community. I don't like how we're represented, with the flamboyant gay stereotype. I'd like to meet someone... &quot;normal&quot;. You know, someone that isn't defined by his sexuality, that doesn't dress in a way that screams &quot;I LIKE GUYS&quot;. It's not a matter of shame, it's more like... I don't know, I don't see why we should be seeing this as something to be proud of. It's just a part of who we are, nothing more.<br /> That's also why I'm having trouble finding someone. I don't go to gay bars : they're really not my kind of place. If I wanna go for a drink, I'd rather go to a pub. I thought about exploring the bear community, but I'm hardly a bear myself, and I'm kinda afraid of being rejected. Also, you know, I don't have any close gay friend, so if I go to those places, I'm gonna be on my own, and I'll feel kinda awkward.<br /> <br /> So yeah. I feel lonely at times. I'm not feeling depressed or anything, I have friends, hobbies,.. But I'd just like to finally have someone. My friends keep saying that I'll certainly meet someone that i deserve soon, that I shouldn't rush it... But I'm so tired of waiting. I'm a student, I should be experimenting stuff. I'm at the prime of my life, dammit. So why can't I have someone?<br /> <br /> <br /> There. Sorry to unwind all of this on you guys, but this rant really helped me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-24-2014, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T12:06:18-07:00","id":239392,"title":"","content":"I'd be careful about using the words &quot;Noce Guy&quot; to describe yourself, especially with the Capitol-N Capitol-G. A lot of self-proclaimed &quot;Nice Guys&quot; are very much the antithesis of boyfriend material, and contrary to what they seem to think, it has nothing to do with being &quot;too nice&quot;. I'm not saying you're one of those guys. You sound like a genuinely kind and sincere person who has had a run of bad luck. Just be careful using that phrase because it has some very negative connotations and you don't want to accidentally associate yourself with some of the people who self-identify as &quot;Nice Guys&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T12:16:20-07:00","id":239394,"title":"","content":"Ah, yeah. I see how it might sounds...hypocritical. I'm just using this term because a friend once used it to describe my &quot;case&quot;. But I guess it makes me sound like a guy trying to get out of the &quot;friendzone.&quot; Which I'm not, I guess. The only friends I have a crush on are straight. So I'm not really eligible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T12:42:11-07:00","id":239471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=239374#post239374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought about exploring the bear community, but I'm hardly a bear myself, and I'm kinda afraid of being rejected.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are bears looking for 100% twinks, if you know. Bear community is open and based on idea &quot;everythink you like is fair game&quot;. Myself, I even like &quot;typical gay&quot; guys ( totally twinks, really ) from time to time. On GROWLr I'm hitted by normal ( not bear ) guys all the time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> My partner is rather typical chaser ( he was even cub years before ), but sexy guy is sexy guy. And hot chick is hot chick. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T13:28:11-07:00","id":239526,"title":"","content":"I'm definitely not a twink though. Maybe a cub. And there's no gay bar in my town, unfortunately, so I think I'm gonna have to rely on the internet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T15:58:39-07:00","id":239633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=238635#post238635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was odd. Funny, but odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absurdity to prove a point often does.<br /> <br /> I wanted to say thank you for your post also Evilmarmelade. I am bisexual myself, though I would say on the opposite end of the spectrum. Almost all of my relationships have been with females. I have a daughter, now nine but over the last few years in Seattle I've had the opportunity to be more open and honest with myself about being bisexual and trying to be part of the LGBT community. I wouldn't say it's something I've struggled with per say but it's something I've given thought to a lot lately. To explain up until a few years ago, maybe late 2012 or so being bisexual hasn't really been something I've thought it. At least in the sense you mean. I've had LGBT friends but never considered myself part of the community you could say. At my last job I had a great opportunity to be a part of a group of work friends the majority of whom were gay, lesbian or transgender. Before that the most I ever brought it up was a throwaway conversation I had over dinner for my twenty eighth birthday with my mother before she passed. I told her I would date a man and that was about it. I don't think it bothered her but I don't honestly know what she thought of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've had the opportunity to date someone from that work group but so far it never amounted to much. We've fooled around, been out to eat a few times, once just us, once with friends but that is it. Mostly I worry about hurting someone. I've been honest that I still prefer girls to men, and on one has ever bothered me. But I worry that if I get serious with someone of the same sex I'm going to find out I'm not as enthusiastic about it as I feel and end up hurting someone. On top of it I'm having a difficult time mustering up the emotional and physical energy for a relationship. Over the last few years i just feel worn thin. I joke that it's like I've been carrying the One Ring or something but it's true. I feel weary and my sex drive doesn't much exist these days. I worry that given both factors that I'm just going to hurt the friend of mine that wants to date. He's a fair bit younger than me and I think that all in all I'm just going to be a drag on him. The Seattle LGBT community, the part I've seen anyway, has been a big help in this. Great people, no pressure. There's a pretty neat gay bar called Neighbors that has been a great spot for LGBT and straight folk alike. But all in all it's something I'm trying to make sense of.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T17:24:03-07:00","id":239691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=239394#post239394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, yeah. I see how it might sounds...hypocritical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much hypocritical as the term having been stained by shitnozzles like, say, Elliot Rodgers, who insisted he wasn't getting dates because he was a nice guy before he committed mass murder. The most misogynistic elements of the MRA movement have claimed the term for themselves, and that stink don't wash off easy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T20:57:18-07:00","id":239886,"title":"","content":"Ah, alright. I'm not American though, that's why I didn't have all the... Social implications. @TyrannicalRabbit : Man, dating is hard, huh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T21:06:17-07:00","id":239892,"title":"","content":"Dating and relationships are always difficult, and develop more issues when you have a more limited pool for one or more reasons. This is unfortunately one of the headaches of life in general, and also why I pretty much universally recommend people get comfortable with the idea of NOT being in a relationship. <br /> <br /> Still, I wish everyone good fortune in searching for suitable emotional and/or physical partnerships of whatever forms you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":31,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","user":"Odd_Canuck","date":". 08-25-2014, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T00:41:00-07:00","id":239991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=235601#post235601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'am Bara Bear. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But I'm more Matsu and Mizuki guy. I'm always wonder if Mentaiko works should be be treated as proper Bara. I'm also interested in &quot;western Bara&quot;, like <a href=\"http://captaingerbear.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>CaptainGerBear</b></a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Checking the Bara tag on Pixiv, I even see swimmer-build teenager. Hmmm, maybe Bara is different from Bear in someway that I do not know.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I'm going to have a presentation about Christianity in Singapore, and Holy Shit, that country is homophobic as hell.<br /> <br /> I kinda surprise since they try so hard to maintain racial and religious harmony ever since a bunch of riot in the past kill hundred of people. Every gay new is swarmed with &quot;Stop cramming your homosexual down our throat&quot; or &quot;The Bible say this and that&quot;, the Archbishop pray that God will cure the gay disease of Singaporean, The National Council of Churches in Singapore telling people to not assault the Pink Dot Gay Pride but start their announcement by quoting the Bible with the typical hatespeech.<br /> <br /> I wonder if I should include this in my presentation since I afraid my teacher gonna say that I'm spreading hatred and fling a zero into my face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T01:10:45-07:00","id":240013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=239310#post239310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're one of the lucky ones. The guys I meet on there are either way older than me or way younger (and looking just for a hookup). Everyone around my age is already in a relationship or they won't even give me the time of day like I'm some kind of deformed wildebeast.</div> </div> </div> </div>but try to amplify your search. There are so many places that people are mainly looking for someone to talk rather than, well, you know. Even within your game community you can find someone nice. Perhaps you should open your eyes every time you visit your local rpg store or similar places. You have to remember it's easier to keep a relationship if you both have a lot in common, and places like comic book stores or conventions would help you a lot with that. <br /> <br /> I've found out bar is also an awesome place to find the one because odds are, people want to talk first. It makes easier to separate those who just want1 hour with you and those who want to invest into something *deeper.<br /> <br /> *No second meaning intended. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, sorry guys.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","name":"Amadeu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T01:28:25-07:00","id":240024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=239886#post239886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, alright. I'm not American though, that's why I didn't have all the... Social implications. @TyrannicalRabbit : Man, dating is hard, huh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Lol you're not kidding. I sympathize as well. I'm not well I have American citizenship but I hesitate to call myself entirely part of it. It also makes it tough because I tend to wonder at times if someone is dating me for gimmicky reasons. Had that happen with the last person I dated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T02:05:56-07:00","id":240047,"title":"","content":"@wulf: If the photo you have on your avatar is your face, you're pretty good looking.<br /> <br /> Well, what to say. I had some discussion with my boyfriend lately. Personality and temperament clashes.<br /> He's the Supernal symbol of Extroversion. I'm the Supernal symbol of Introversion.<br /> I've struggled all my life with introversion. I don't like being with many people at a time for a long period. I don't talk much. I'm nerdy, I like routine and fear the unknown. I don't like to take risks, I don't like to go shopping for the sake of it. I don't like to test new food, and if I do, I do it with the eyes and nose more than my tongue. I don't drink alcohol and people look at me like an alien for this. I can't improvise chattering like extroverted people can.<br /> I like singing, even when it's not appropriate. I have some childish behaviour. I like to disengage myself from discussions to avoid being drained by socialization. When I text people, I don't give a &quot;good morning&quot;, because I'm accustomed to forums, where you don't need to. I do give &quot;Good morning&quot;s to people I meet in person, but my boyfriend would much prefer me to say it even when texting.<br /> This is leaving my boyfriend confused, and wanting me to change a little bit. I know he doesn't expect a sudden change. Still, I'm worried. I can't be someone else. Introversion is genetic, and it's about how your mind works by default. I have changed since I was in high school, I've grown. But that still isn't enough.<br /> <br /> I really don't know what to do. It's not a huge problem, but I understand how introversion might look akward and alien to extroverts. All I can do for now is to take little steps. But if I don't take enough steps, I might disappoint him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T04:39:44-07:00","id":240142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">@wulf: If the photo you have on your avatar is your face, you're pretty good looking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly my thought, very handsome. But not everybody puts their own photo as avatar, that's why I didn't comment on it till now, but since you brought up the issue... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T05:09:24-07:00","id":240156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=239374#post239374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, when it comes to men, I have trouble identifying myself with the LGBT community. I don't like how we're represented, with the flamboyant gay stereotype. I'd like to meet someone... &quot;normal&quot;. You know, someone that isn't defined by his sexuality, that doesn't dress in a way that screams &quot;I LIKE GUYS&quot;. It's not a matter of shame, it's more like... I don't know, I don't see why we should be seeing this as something to be proud of. It's just a part of who we are, nothing more</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's not shame, then I also don't know what it is. Feeling attraction by a non-feminine guy is a choice, I get it. But it really sounds like you are hidding your sexuality from everyone and it's getting more important than finding someone who can make u happy. <br /> <br /> This, being not proud of who you are, I'm against. Unless you still live in a situation that is clever to hide, I wouldn't take that road. Really. Sounds like you cannot enjoy gay guys coz you are afraid of other's people opinion. You don't need to raise any flag, but you also shouldn't feel like there is something wrong. <br /> <br /> And when you say &quot;I don't see why&quot;, that's exactly why: so people like you could see its ok to be who you are and feel comfortable about it. It would be &quot;nothing more&quot; if you were straight, coz that's normal. But since you cannot be categorized as normal by ordinary people, that's why they make sure others see they are proud of being different and nobody has to do with it. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, sorry guys.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","name":"Amadeu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T05:29:57-07:00","id":240168,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, I should have been clearer. I am not ashamed of being bi. I just don't want to flaunt it in everyone's face. I don't feel like there is something wrong with me or the gay community, except the image that we have in the media. And I'm sorry if I offended you. When I wrote this yesterday, I wasn't in a good place, and I may have not measured my words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T05:34:01-07:00","id":240169,"title":"","content":"Also, the only people I am hiding my orientation from are from my family. Some of them are openly against gay rights, and I prefer to not confront them for the moment. I am not ready for this. But my friends know about it. If they don't, it's because I never asked for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T05:45:46-07:00","id":240172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=240169#post240169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the only people I am hiding my orientation from are from my family. Some of them are openly against gay rights, and I prefer to not confront them for the moment. I am not ready for this. But my friends know about it. If they don't, it's because I never asked for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's great. I think we should also respect people before imposing our ideas. When it comes to family, you should be really wise to choose the best moment to start this conversation, especially if you still live with them. <br /> <br /> &quot; don't forget what my mama said<br /> People talking b-shit since the beginning of time<br /> Unless they paying your bills, pay them bitches no mind&quot;<br /> <br /> But the rest, if they are not gonna judge you for being bi, they will judge you for something else. For sure. That's why I don't care anymore<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, sorry guys.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","name":"Amadeu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T07:38:57-07:00","id":240270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=239374#post239374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah. I feel lonely at times. I'm not feeling depressed or anything, I have friends, hobbies,.. But I'd just like to finally have someone. My friends keep saying that I'll certainly meet someone that i deserve soon, that I shouldn't rush it... But I'm so tired of waiting. I'm a student, I should be experimenting stuff. I'm at the prime of my life, dammit. So why can't I have someone?<br /> <br /> <br /> There. Sorry to unwind all of this on you guys, but this rant really helped me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You sound like me as a teenager. Keep at it, there is light at the end of the tunnel. What helped me was being out to all of my friends, not worrying about someone saying No if I asked them out, and making time to meet other people who were also GLBTQQA and also just wanted to be normal. I joined a dinner club for gay men when I was 18 and had a blast. We went to all sorts of great restaurants and just had dinner and hung out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T07:40:34-07:00","id":240272,"title":"","content":"Well they were judging me before for being the only one who didn't chose a &quot;successful&quot; degree, I'm studying translation, while my cousins are engineer and military doctors, and my sister works in tourism. But now that I graduated, they seem to have calmed down. Of course, they also don't know (except for my sister, mother and father) that I'm love roleplay and that I do LARP frequently. But oh, well. It's sad, but I'm used to hide stuff from them, my sexuality is only a part of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T01:08:06-07:00","id":250583,"title":"","content":"Not an happy day today.<br /> <br /> Yesterday I accompanied my boyfriend to a massage center. I didn't want to have a massage, but I did it anyways. I'm more of a practical person, which only spends money on less costly things, and estetic centres are not one of them. A voice inside of me told me &quot;IT'S A TRAP <a href=\"http://IT&#39;S A TRAP\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3mL7h6NSOKk</a>&quot;, the other said &quot;No, he'll be doing it to make me try it, how much do you think that will cost?&quot;. Still, I didn't have the courage to ask if that massage was charged. Yeah, I know, I'm a fool like that.<br /> <br /> My boyfriend was happy to spend 40\u20ac on this massage for me. That was quite a good massage, indeed. We had a great experience together.<br /> But I didn't want to make him spend so much for me. He's already spending much for me. Yes, he does have money. I don't. And those I have aren't my own, they are my parents'.<br /> <br /> Today I pointed out to him that I felt uncomfortable for that. The discussion went on. And when we left each other, I asked him if he was going to give me the book he wanted to give me to take a vacation together. He said &quot;I'll think about it.&quot;<br /> <br /> That was it. I raged and went into the car. I said hello, he didn't.<br /> <br /> And now I feel like shit. And it's my fault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 09-06-2014, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T07:26:08-07:00","id":250744,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Jesuncolo;n250583<br /> <br /> My boyfriend was happy to spend 40\u20ac on this massage for me. That was quite a good massage, indeed. We had a great experience together.<br /> But I didn't want to make him spend so much for me. He's already spending much for me. Yes, he does have money. I don't. And those I have aren't my own, they are my parents.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> It's hard to give any advice without knowing you both, but, come on, if it makes you feel happy and if it makes him happy to please you, why would you destroy the mood and complain about it, specially AFTER the money was spent anyway?<br /> <br /> Of course he is gonna have second thoughts about having a vacation with you coz he might wanna do something special and you might again say yes just to fight later on. I get that you feel afterwords bad about someone else spending money with you, but this is his way of saying that he cares and giving you something good that you don't have. I woukd expect a &quot;thank you&quot;, followed by an action that represents that you care, rather than a discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>English is not my native language, sorry guys.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/607-amadeu","name":"Amadeu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T07:36:32-07:00","id":254105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amadeu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=250744#post250744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's hard to give any advice without knowing you both, but, come on, if it makes you feel happy and if it makes him happy to please you, why would you destroy the mood and complain about it, specially AFTER the money was spent anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it didn't make him happy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T09:03:19-07:00","id":254144,"title":"","content":"Handling money can be a bit of a sensitive subject in a relationship. Hell, it's a bit of a sensitive subject in western culture.<br /> <br /> I can totally understand if someone feels uncomfortable with someone else paying for them, particularly if the two are on different levels economically in general and the one knows that that they won't be able to treat the other back. It does create a lopsidedness in the relationship.<br /> <br /> The answer, as so many other times, is probably to talk about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T06:58:54-07:00","id":255235,"title":"","content":"Yeah, lot of &quot;debt&quot; and &quot;obligation&quot; in Western culture, but not a lot of good mechanisms for dealing with them healthily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T16:43:41-07:00","id":255655,"title":"","content":"So, it looks like I finally got lucky. I followed the advice of an internet friend, and tried some dating applications. I was surprised at the number of people who wanted to ask me out. After having sorted out the creeps and the drug dealers, I got to chat with three men, and one of them asked me out for a drink. We went out, it was sweet, not necessarily romantic, but we did find out that we had a lot of culture references in common, so that's good. He was nine years older than me, but weirdly enough, it didn't distrub me, despite my initial reservations. And then, finally, we made out, and despite my fears of being a disappointement in bed due to my non-experience, turns out it had been pretty good on both sides. <br /> So...I don't know yet if we're really in a relationship, or if it's more complicated than that (I'm sure it is), but I just wanted to say thank you to the thread. For cheering me when I was down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T03:26:47-07:00","id":255951,"title":"","content":"Good for you, Evilmarmelade! Be careful though and keep your expectations realistic, relationships are complicated so don't worry if things don't work out the first time around. That said, enjoy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jp