 have some weakness for super convincing 'traps', if you pardon that term I picked up from animu community.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 10-11-2014, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T09:52:43-07:00","id":278193,"title":"","content":"So my aunt and her daughter just stayed at my house while my mom was away and she want to know what we were talking about, I told her it the usual stuffs about education, future jobs and such, just some casual gossiping between parent and children in the evening, but when I mentioned that I told my aunt I like guy when they asked me if I have a girlfriend yet then my mom just suddenly stopped talking and pretended to watch the TV.<br /> <br /> :sigh: It's seem that Don't ask, Don't tell is the best I can hope for atm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T12:31:26-07:00","id":278298,"title":"","content":"My policy is let them think I'm Asexual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T07:43:07-07:00","id":278808,"title":"","content":"Maybe LGBT themed song will help you now...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/moSFlvxnbgk\" data-code=\"moSFlvxnbgk\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/moSFlvxnbgk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I'm moved with my partner to &quot;my&quot; apartment ( family condo, before cousin and brother with his wife lived here ), but we were instructed by my mother &quot;to avoid show up&quot; as couple. Once again &quot;do those (<i>wrong)</i> things, only not do this on public&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T08:54:26-07:00","id":278854,"title":"","content":"My mother is at times now so &quot;worried&quot; about my perceived asexuality that she grumbled that even chasing men would be less &quot;weird&quot; than expressing zero interest in any relationship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T08:36:02-07:00","id":285942,"title":"","content":"Started stuff last year. It's getting to a can't-hide point, so now's the time for these conversations with people.<br /> <br /> Came out to my Mother. (Step-mother, not egg-donor, but the bio one and I are estranged / disowned, my being in this thread is a huge reason for that.)<br /> <br /> ME: &quot;So, umm yeah, 'Hi, I'm Trans'&quot;<br /> HER: &quot;Hi 'Trans', I'm your Mother. ... Hey, look, still here!&quot;<br /> <br /> I love having a smart-ass, accepting, family member.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T17:02:32-07:00","id":289107,"title":"","content":"Hey there. Some news. I'm officially &quot;a good friend&quot; with my now ex-boyfriend. The point is, while I do care, I don't either.<br /> <br /> Tonight I decided to take him to the cinema, and took him to see &quot;Begin again&quot;. I also bought him roses, just to surprise him. He was indeed surprised. But that didn't stop him from telling me that while he does care about me, he doesn't figures a stable relationship with me, because our personalities are really the opposite. And while he can't understand some parts of my personality and wanted me to be something else, I don't want to change him, I like him the way he is, even his flaws, and I don't want to force him in anything he doesn't want to partecipate in. That's fine.<br /> So yay, I wasted 9 euros to have a great evening with him. And we're still friends.<br /> And while I feel a little lost because I can officially start rage-dating anyone who's fool enough to try, I also feel free.<br /> <br /> Some days ago I started feeling a crushing sadness allover my body and my mind.<br /> &quot;<b>Life is a breath play</b>&quot;, I wrote on Facebook.<br /> I felt like suffocating. The relationship was only one-way. I felt the relationship slowly die out. I kinda liked it, and kinda didn't. I'm a masochist like that. Emotions make me feel alive, even bad ones. I started worrying about our relationship, and I feared the possibility to lose him.<br /> <br /> The point is, I didn't &quot;lose&quot; him. He's still my friend. I'm still his friends. We shared some intimacy. That's all.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Life is a breath play.</b><br /> <b>The breath play is over.</b> <b>Someone used the safeword.</b></u>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T05:58:58-07:00","id":298047,"title":"","content":"I really wish I could say that I understand everything felt in the post above me, but I don't. I get very attached to people on an emotional level when in an intimate relationship, and I don't think I could disassociate those feelings of friendship from romantic ones once that line had been crossed. I do understand the feeling that emotions are what is keeping one truly alive, even if they're negative ones. That's a beautiful metaphor, by the way. It's been a long time since I've attempted to take a breath.<br /> <br /> I just felt that the eloquent post above deserved some commentary before I selfishly posted about me me me.<br /> <br /> Anyhoo, my romantic life is at a standstill. Many people that know me think this might be a good thing, as my mental health has been more than a bit shaky.<br /> <br /> Thing is:<br /> <br /> I'm legally disabled. I might be a little &quot;off&quot; forever! I don't want to wait till I get &quot;better&quot; to start dating again if that takes me more than a few years, decades or the rest of my life! I'm not a monk! <br /> <br /> So, with the &quot;stay single until you feel happy, even though [insert terrible fact about reality]&quot; idea thrown out the window, my problem is threefold:<br /> <br /> 1. I'm extremely emotionally attached to a person who is, for all intents and purposes, unavailable to me. Yes, it does hurt.<br /> <br /> 2. I'm extremely physically attracted to a friend/acquaintance (or two), and I have no idea how to both ask if they're attracted to other men in general, and if they might be attracted to me personally. Advice would help.<br /> <br /> 3. SHOULD I TRUST THE INTERNET AT ALL WITH MY SEX LIFE? I have no idea. I've had a few online relationships, but they've always ended in some sort of disappointing crash. Do I keep looking for love online, or do I unplug and go completely local? I'm not a hugely social person, outside of gaming, so bars and clubs don't really appeal much as venues for meeting romantic partners, but where else do you go? I've rarely seen the inside of a bar. <br /> <br /> \u200bA friend once remarked that they &quot;couldn't imagine dating a non-gamer&quot;. I felt more than a little jealous. I've never had a partner that didn't either call my hobby weird, or at best just didn't get it. I've rarely had the luxury of having a partner know what tabletop rpgs even ARE. I usually get a confused, slow half-nod followed by &quot;like World of Warcraft and stuff?&quot;. If I'm lucky, they say Dungeons and Dragons, but still show no interest at all. It would be nice to date someone that would actually enjoy spending time together doing something we both love. That sounds like it would be awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T10:46:35-07:00","id":298290,"title":"","content":"Let's tackle some of this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=298047#post298047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm legally disabled. I might be a little &quot;off&quot; forever! I don't want to wait till I get &quot;better&quot; to start dating again if that takes me more than a few years, decades or the rest of my life! I'm not a monk!<br /> <br /> So, with the &quot;stay single until you feel happy, even though [insert terrible fact about reality]&quot; idea thrown out the window, my problem is threefold:</div> </div> </div> </div>The goal of that particular line of advice is that unless you are happy with yourself, and willing to be who you are, you are always going to be searching for the person &quot;who will complete me&quot;. You don't have to be perfect, but if you go out looking for someone because you NEED someone, then you're setting yourself up a lot of dependency issues and high abuse probabilities in the future.<br /> <br /> As for not being a monk, do you not have hands? Even if you don't there's other options thanks to technology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=298047#post298047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I'm extremely emotionally attached to a person who is, for all intents and purposes, unavailable to me. Yes, it does hurt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this does indeed suck for which you have my sympathies, but there's little that can be done that I am aware of other than time, distance and/or seeking to find the flaws that would make said person less attractive to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=298047#post298047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. I'm extremely physically attracted to a friend/acquaintance (or two), and I have no idea how to both ask if they're attracted to other men in general, and if they might be attracted to me personally. Advice would help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... there's the direct approach of just outright asking them. Assuming you don't want to be that direct, you can jokingly reference all the wild parties and wild women they must hang around with. If you're willing to take a middle approach and don't mind a semi-slight lie, you can approach them for advice. Tell them that you've got some friends that were talking about coming and visiting and you're collecting recommendations for fun/interesting places they've visited. From there if you want to feel the waters out mention that a couple of the friends are a gay couple, do any of the places tend to have a problem with that? From there you can possibly extract information if they're gay, or open to same-sex adventures.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=298047#post298047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. SHOULD I TRUST THE INTERNET AT ALL WITH MY SEX LIFE? I have no idea. I've had a few online relationships, but they've always ended in some sort of disappointing crash. Do I keep looking for love online, or do I unplug and go completely local? I'm not a hugely social person, outside of gaming, so bars and clubs don't really appeal much as venues for meeting romantic partners, but where else do you go? I've rarely seen the inside of a bar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, let's start with flipping the question around... Who else are going to trust with your sex life? You can be fairly certain most of us are largely impartial in the matter, since due to distance there's not much likelyhood that we're going to tell you not to date X because we secretly want to date X and don't want the competition. A large number of use are also not huge social people outside of gaming, so we have similar experiences on which to base our suggestions. And they're just that, suggestions based on our own experience. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=298047#post298047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bA friend once remarked that they &quot;couldn't imagine dating a non-gamer&quot;. I felt more than a little jealous. I've never had a partner that didn't either call my hobby weird, or at best just didn't get it. I've rarely had the luxury of having a partner know what tabletop rpgs even ARE. I usually get a confused, slow half-nod followed by &quot;like World of Warcraft and stuff?&quot;. If I'm lucky, they say Dungeons and Dragons, but still show no interest at all. It would be nice to date someone that would actually enjoy spending time together doing something we both love. That sounds like it would be awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has some advantages and also some drawbacks. Some of the worst gamers I've encountered were couples. When you're a GM you have that gooey urge to help your SO more than others in the game, and friction between the two of you at the table can translate to friction or lack of friction elsewhere in the relationship.<br /> <br /> But generally it's a good thing if you can handle it. Of course most games require several people.... humm... maybe polyamory... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T16:54:52-07:00","id":298552,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the advice, Canuck. I seriously didn't expect such a comprehensive response.<br /> <br /> In reverse order:<br /> <br /> I get what you mean about dating and the internet. It's just some people's opinions, detached yet informative, but only opinions and personal experiences. Nothing more.<br /> <br /> Your advice on how to approach &quot;feeling the waters out&quot; was quite helpful. Thanks for that.<br /> <br /> Now, to the meat of the matter: I don't really feel like I &quot;need&quot; anyone. I feel rather repulsed by the idea of being attached in a needy way to a person. I've done it before, and feeling completely dependent on someone has only hurt me. I'm definitely not planning to do that again, and am consciously avoiding people and situations that put me in that place. I'm happy with who I am. I'm just not happy with how much my psychiatric disorders are interfering with my ability to socialize and have an active life. I just want someone to share the life I'm trying to build with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T03:13:40-07:00","id":298775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=298290#post298290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has some advantages and also some drawbacks. Some of the worst gamers I've encountered were couples. When you're a GM you have that gooey urge to help your SO more than others in the game, and friction between the two of you at the table can translate to friction or lack of friction elsewhere in the relationship.<br /> <br /> But generally it's a good thing if you can handle it. Of course most games require several people.... humm... maybe polyamory... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Concur. Mine partner is &quot;rather new&quot; to RPGs - we play regularly only from two years. But it is placing <b>a lot</b> of friction on our relationship, as I'm mostly GM and we argue a lot about games. He often accused me ( <b>rightly</b> ) of being harsh on his role-playing. I understood why this is only lately, after watching this short movie about gamers and couples:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/GIY1niCIKhQ\" data-code=\"GIY1niCIKhQ\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/GIY1niCIKhQ/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> The clue is this - I subconsciously put so much stress to his play, because I want to assert that he will ideal partner for me, and good husband material. I can't envision myself with someone who at least partially affirm my lives passion - my previous relationship with ex-girlfriend ended because this as one of main reasons. I, almost literally, nWoDed her to death.<br /> <br /> But with my partner I just see I was with wrong person then - I from time to time, goes in my maniacal &quot;listen about this great thing in nWoD&quot;, but he understand it, and even recently started to read my <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> corebook, on his own. I'm so proud of him now!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-01-2014, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T03:22:22-07:00","id":298778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YkyTQP27H6s\" data-code=\"YkyTQP27H6s\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/YkyTQP27H6s/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Being in Seattle this was making the rounds of many a friend of mine on Facebook.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T12:41:29-08:00","id":300315,"title":"","content":"*looks at my write-up for Forsaken 2ed*<br /> <br /> &gt;Gaia &quot;colliding&quot; with Theia (like in that hypothesis) which births Selene and Hekate as dual representations of the Moon<br /> &gt;Selene and Hekate being Mothers of Urathra<br /> <br /> I really need next time to introduce some heteronormative Celestine relationship for balance because so far it makes Black Furies blush.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T13:50:11-08:00","id":300407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=300315#post300315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*looks at my write-up for Forsaken 2ed*<br /> <br /> &gt;Gaia &quot;colliding&quot; with Theia (like in that hypothesis) which births Selene and Hekate as dual representations of the Moon<br /> &gt;Selene and Hekate being Mothers of Urathra<br /> <br /> I really need next time to introduce some heteronormative Celestine relationship for balance because so far it makes Black Furies blush.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths?p=272764#post272764\">Forsaken forum gone to agree that Roman werewolves</a> would goes to <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capitoline_Wolf\" target=\"_blank\">Capitoline (She-)Wolf</a> and Luna as both Mothers to Romulus and Remus ( and their race, at least in Italy ).<br /> <br /> &quot;Uratha, promoting lesbianism from 3000 years!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Really interesting would be topic of two <b>male</b> gods giving birth to half humans monsters - are we know about some ethnicietis myths were are both male Wolf God and Moon God?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T08:20:12-08:00","id":301129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=298290#post298290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The goal of that particular line of advice is that unless you are happy with yourself, and willing to be who you are, you are always going to be searching for the person &quot;who will complete me&quot;. You don't have to be perfect, but if you go out looking for someone because you NEED someone, then you're setting yourself up a lot of dependency issues and high abuse probabilities in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>THIS OMG SO MUCH THIS.<br /> <br /> I will never forgive Tom Cruise for &quot;You complete me&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T09:51:09-08:00","id":301200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=301129#post301129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THIS OMG SO MUCH THIS.<br /> <br /> I will never forgive Tom Cruise for &quot;You complete me&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Heath Ledger as the Joker? Just as bad?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T10:45:34-08:00","id":301299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=301200#post301200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about Heath Ledger as the Joker? Just as bad?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, sometimes things are more complicated. This isn't Heath Ledger, but everyone knows that The Joker won't ever really kill Batman outright and likely why. <br /> <br /> Here's the Situation-As-Relationship-Metaphor a la Batman from another angle. This one has some poignancy for me as a metaphor for some of that emotional bile that comes from a bad relationship:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PgvJorlHZCI\" data-code=\"PgvJorlHZCI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/PgvJorlHZCI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Also, does this mean that acknowledging the fact that you won't outright murder someone, for personal reasons, is romantic? If so, I've been seriously underestimating how active my love-life is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T15:52:54-08:00","id":303812,"title":"","content":"So in the interest of discussion - what was everyone's first &quot;realization&quot; like? When did you acknowledge your orientation/gender identity to yourself, and in what circumstances? (I'd also be curious to hear about early experiences as you first adjusted to your new realizations, but I realize that might get too personal.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T21:36:44-08:00","id":304153,"title":"","content":"My first &quot;realization&quot; was rather early, some time in primary school or kindergarten. I realized that I liked people in a very comparable way romantically, and in relationships in general. I felt distinctly different from the people around me, or at least how they presented themselves.<br /> I withdrew and found sanctuary in my imaginary life , where reality, sex and gender were just footnotes in a greater story. As a result, many of my friends growing up were part of the LGBT community or gamers, often both. I came out partially to a relative at 13, and have identified as something between pansexual and bisexual-gender fluid in the time since.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T22:19:59-08:00","id":304200,"title":"","content":"Before the end of primary school I come realization I like men. A lot. Before junior high I was fantasizing about my older colleges. <span style=\"font-size:8px\">In locker room... <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Year or two later it come I like girls also</span>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T11:26:33-08:00","id":305996,"title":"","content":"I haven't had many relationship, but since I was a kid I always felt that being close to female more than simple friendship was somehow out of place for me. But I when I was a kid I was more interested in playing with toys and being a Power ranger than having relationships with people.<br /> <br /> When I was at middle school, it looked like my classmates &quot;discovered&quot; sex, and I came to know the whole &quot;penis, meet vagina&quot; process on a purely theoretical concept. And it was quite wierd, because I still didn't feel attraction to girls, and I started thinking &quot;ok, that's something that will change with time, I'll find the right girl&quot;.<br /> <br /> About third-middle school - first high school, I still was a complete nerd with little social life outside my best friends, and a jerker. I was playing Gothic at the time, and during &quot;private time&quot; I somehow started picturing in my mind a NPC whipping the main character. After some minutes thinking about this, I started feeling like I was paying attention to the male character more than the female one.<br /> My reaction wasn't particularily strong. I kinda accepted it fairily easy. Something like &quot;Well, I guess that means I'm gay&quot;. I kinda knew it even before realizing it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T20:56:20-08:00","id":314179,"title":"","content":"For most of my childhood, I only really had female friends. I just didn't get along as well with the 'other' boys. In small ways, I had always considered myself more of one of the girls than one of the boys.<br /> <br /> After my parents got divorced, and I started seeing more of my dad (since he wasn't always away, avoiding my egg-donor), he started having some conversations with my brother and I. These conversations were from the perspective that he hadn't spent as much time with us as he'd like to have, and he wanted to get to know us better.<br /> I was 10:<br /> Dad: &quot;So, have you started to like any of the girls in your class yet?&quot;<br /> Me: &quot;I've always liked the girls in a bunch of ways. And yeah, I'm starting to like some of them in 'other ways', now. But, it's odd for me, since I've pretty much always just been one of them. It's like I'm a lesbian with the wrong body.&quot;<br /> My father, who's a bit of a 60's conservative type, did not react well. Fortunately, he just assumed I had an awkward way of saying things, and that he didn't understand what I had tried to say. Of course, I didn't understand at the time either.<br /> <br /> Other than that, there really isn't any one 'ah-ha, that's what I am' moment for me to point out. With how conservative my father is, and how homophobic my egg-donor is, I spent most of my teenage years and you adulthood in denial, trying to convince myself I wasn't Trans. Depression has been a close frenemy of mine because of this.<br /> <br /> As far as adjusting to it, some of the things that I used to maintain the denial were the preconceptions about trans*folk ('Trans equals Gay' being the main one, but also a lack of understanding about how much transition manages). So adjusting to it really just came down to information exposure in ways that chewed through my ability to maintain the denial. Since I've admitted it, I've started to be a lot more proactive in making my life better, haven't had anywhere near so many depressive episodes, and the ones I have had, it has been a lot easier to pull out of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T04:16:11-08:00","id":314366,"title":"","content":"I think I had my first realization around middle school/high school. But it wasn't until after I graduated that I finally allowed myself to come to grips with it. I guess I was always more interested in other guy's bodies, but I tried to convince myself that it was out of a desire to be thinner/more athletic. It seemed like being overweight and gay was perhaps the worst thing that a person could be. I was already hanging on by a thread. Other people noticed somehow, but I took it as just another way my classmates had found to verbally abuse/harass me. I didn't think anyone around me actually knew... in retrospect, I probably didn't hide it well.<br /> <br /> Eventually, when I was free of that place and going to college, I was finally able to admit to myself the truth, and accept that this was part of who I was, and I had a choice of how to proceed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T10:33:31-08:00","id":320022,"title":"","content":"(Just jumping...)<br /> <br /> I've been sexually aware since before I was 5 (attracted to both genders, but not overly sexual; that is, sex is secondary to me in most all cases) -- as a sidenote, I've noted anecdotily that a great number of people who I've talked to who were sexually aware at a very young age are very often bisexual, to a degree that skews the Kinsey bell curve quite a bit. But anywho...<br /> <br /> [ Extended Sidenote: It's telling, though, that the gender (identity) of those I have been with (in many different ways) over the years bare out a gender-pattern: I've had far more *relationships* with women than men, but on the inverse my number of male sexual partners similarly outnumbers the females by a similar ratio (about 5:1 in each direction). That doesn't, though, have to directly do with attraction but rather with how the genders most often work: as a male, I/whomever could spend a number of nights/months dating or seeing a given female and have it often not involve sex (due to holding back on her part), but maintain a serious relationship, never-the-less (though sex may occur later on); on the flip, I can head down to a given club, gym, or similar and find a guy to hook up with within a few hours, if not sooner. That's not due to orientation, itself, but to how the genders more often approach sex: females tend to hold back more, while males will most often pursue an opportunity when given one (again, speaking in broad generalities, of course).]<br /> <br /> I remember having crushes (not intense ones, as again I'm not overly sexual, but simple ones) on both boys and girls starting from around 4 or 5, with my first sexual experience being with another boy when I was 5 and with with a girl at 14/16 (split there because I didn't certain things at one age and other things later on). While I can in theory be in a relationship with anyone, I find as I am older now (40's), I'd ironically enough most likely be more content being in a relationship with a female who identifies as pan-lesbian (just go with me on this for a second) who enjoys a relationship with another person regardless of gender *but* has the sexual attitude of the &quot;stereotypical&quot; mature lesbian -- when we have sex, it's hot and gettin'-it-on, but in general we can go for months at a time without a single thought about it.<br /> <br /> Sorry I got a little off-topic, but one thought came hand-in-hand with the other: past sexual experiences made me think of future ones... &gt;shrugs&lt;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T18:15:22-08:00","id":320293,"title":"","content":"We used to get a scrambled porn channel on cable at home and I would sneak into the basement to peer at the staticky porn in the middle of the night. I pretty much realized I was gay when the obligatory lesbian scene in any straight porn left me bored to tears. I would take my bathroom breaks during them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":1018,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","user":"Ophidimancer","date":". 11-23-2014, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T19:06:03-08:00","id":320307,"title":"","content":"Oh, hey, Fiddy. Good to see you again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T19:37:44-08:00","id":320311,"title":"","content":"Hello! It's been awhile, I know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T04:48:51-08:00","id":320623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=320311#post320311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello! It's been awhile, I know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I *just* sent out a &quot;Where's Ophid?&quot; PM last night! I've been back on DA:M with some other people, IRL and here on the forum, and I was going to see if you were doing anything with it (I remember posting a Foundation/Pillar set for the Akashayana for you a few years back); when I checked, I noted that you hadn't been here for like 6 months (not an unusual thing for me, historically, but unusual for you more &quot;regular&quot; guys). I was all like &quot;Where's he at?!&quot;. You must have heard my telepathic call... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" sm