3\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey there! I loved your Akashayana Foundation/Pillar setup, but I have not been able to find people to play DA:M, unfortunately. Actually I've been having trouble finding people to game at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sucks -- sorry to hear/read that. I'll be posting stuff for DA:M later this week (after moving to the other side of town, I just recently found two more of my old notebooks out of storage), so maybe you'll stop by to comment/contribute? <br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> We now return you to your regularly scheduled thread... #Derailment","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T01:27:51-08:00","id":321558,"title":"","content":"@Just John<br /> <br /> Seems your fanbase is growing! One of these days we have to make a &quot;Just John Appreciation Thread&quot; due to all the extensive material you post about DA Mage! At this point I think you have more &quot;published&quot; material than WW with their two books :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T07:30:33-08:00","id":323621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=321558#post321558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Just John<br /> <br /> Seems your fanbase is growing! One of these days we have to make a &quot;Just John Appreciation Thread&quot; due to all the extensive material you post about DA Mage! At this point I think you have more &quot;published&quot; material than WW with their two books :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Gurl, please -- I *wish* I'd get my shit together enough to actually post all my handwritten stuff from years ago... but I get distracted/Reality(tm) creeps in, and the next thing you know it's 6 months, a year later, and I'm all like &quot;WTF...?&quot;. That's why I ask others to also post stuff -- it gives me a kick in the ass to get on top of things. But anywho... like I said... #Derailment<br /> <br /> We now return you to your regularly scheduled gayness...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T22:04:04-08:00","id":324224,"title":"","content":"Sooo ... marriage equality huh? Since I last posted regularly a lot of stuff has happened in the US regarding marriage equality. It's kind of exciting ... ohhh! Did I tell you guys that my husband got his green card!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T23:00:25-08:00","id":324231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=324224#post324224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooo ... marriage equality huh? Since I last posted regularly a lot of stuff has happened in the US regarding marriage equality. It's kind of exciting ... ohhh! Did I tell you guys that my husband got his green card!?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay on the green card!<br /> <br /> And I'd say I'm less a promoter of marriage equality and more of a strong supporter of marriage apathy. Unless *your* marriage impacts *my* life I don't give a damn, and neither should the law. Legal headaches? We've already *got* issues of taxes, insurance, and so on sorted out when people are in some kind of pair-bond, so there's no real impact there.<br /> <br /> Now if someone wanted to get into a 3-way marriage there would need to be some legal juggling to sort out taxes, insurance and all that jazz, and I'd be going &quot;whoa, slow down! This stuff needs to get sorted as you go, politicians are slow and so is the legal system, so take it easy.&quot; On the flip side I'd say much the same thing if someone wanted to marry a goat, or a bodypillow or a small glen in the california wine country.<br /> <br /> Religion? Sure. I can see a church saying &quot;Gasp! You horrible people you! We do not recognise your marriage!&quot;... and they'd be welcome to do that. Of course it has no weight or bearing on anything but the church, and I can't really see people hanging around a church that doesn't accept their marriage much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T00:50:21-08:00","id":324302,"title":"","content":"Oh,you guys are a so a bit short sighted. In Poland, we still do not have Civil Unions, not to mention some marriage equality. One of our crown arguments for LGBT rights is: &quot;Look, in USA and Western Europe they have those rights and people did not died out, or straight couples stopped make they own marriages. So let us have them too. Aren't we civilized nation?&quot;<br /> <br /> But still, we have to much conservative demographics and Catholic Church have too much impact on society, especially, politicians. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T05:19:34-08:00","id":324417,"title":"","content":"What conservative demographics say and what they do often vary. 75 % of Christian Right Wingers here actually use condoms in spite of talking tough.<br /> <br /> Though I would say marriage equality is not most pressing issue. Reforming labor law warrants priority for me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T18:09:18-08:00","id":324931,"title":"","content":"So...same-sex marriage get green light in Finland, and the bigot rears their ugly head again with the usual &quot;gay mafia/agenda&quot; and &quot;think about the children&quot; trash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T23:07:04-08:00","id":325113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=324417#post324417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I would say marriage equality is not most pressing issue. Reforming labor law warrants priority for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me they are <b>both</b> the prioroity. I live in almost 4 year same-sex relationship, we live together from 3,5 years. I was having all of the classical problems mentioned in Civil Union campaign, without only funeral matters. So, yeah, it <b>is</b> pressing matter.<br /> <br /> Labor law also is large problem, as I lost next job from junk contract (???, in Polish &quot;umowa \u015bmieciowa&quot;) - I just think those things can be solved <b>now</b>, not after 2 decades. Really, what is problem with reforming labor law <b>and </b>making at least Civil Union?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T01:46:36-08:00","id":326734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=325113#post325113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what is problem with reforming labor law <b>and </b>making at least Civil Union?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are both very delicate matters in terms of public opinion, voters and politicians. Getting ONE of them through to the result you want is already so hard and without the guarantee of success. You don't throw another equally controversial subject when you don't even know if you can solve the first.<br /> <br /> It may not seem a big deal to you or your friends, just get it approved and move on bla bla bla. But you have to think nation wide and what kind of politicians were elected.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T03:46:50-08:00","id":326818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=326734#post326734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But you have to think nation wide and what kind of politicians were elected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nation wide Marrige Equality problem is most about 5% of populacy. Labor law is getting to almost 30%. We do not stand a chance in this race. Or any other, as miners or healthcare workers are more numerous groups than we are.<br /> <br /> But also as it is touching this small part of society, it should be much easier to implement. Yes, it's controverstial topic, but also less practicly in living with it in real life.<br /> <br /> Most interesting thing is that Labor Law problems are all over Western world, and most of European countires have problems with them. It do not stoping those countries with the Marrige Equality efforts.<br /> <br /> In Polands it is, only beacuse we have conservative goverment - 3/4 of parlamant is from midly conservative to extremly consevative parties.<br /> <br /> It's just make me so sad in long term... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T04:56:51-08:00","id":326849,"title":"","content":"I also meant it in another way, if 3/4 of the Parliament is conservative, it means a great majority of the population is too. Implementing such a law would cause a great deal of protests, demonstrations, etc (every country had it, even Portugal who has the most quiet people in the world). It would cause a LOT of controversy.<br /> <br /> You can't put up TWO laws that generate controversy. Not only is it too difficult to accomplish but can also lead for Governments to fall and, come on, do you think politicians really want to jeopardize their seats and privileges?<br /> <br /> We managed to get the same sex marriage approved in Portugal because it was somewhat of a concession from the shaking Central-Left Government to the Left Wing interests in a long shot try to gather supporters to other matters. It had nothing to do with human rights, it was pure politics, like in most country. Rarely such a thing is done for the people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T06:19:28-08:00","id":328150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=326818#post326818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But also as it is touching this small part of society, it should be much easier to implement. Yes, it's controverstial topic, but also less practicly in living with it in real life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Key word : it SHOULD.<br /> Here in France, we finally obtained marriage equality last year, but oooh boy, it was ugly. We had months of debate and protests, both anti and pro marriage; the Right was deliberately lenghtening the debates in parliament in hope that the public opinion shift in their favor... It was absolutely ridiculous. The medias were talking about this laws non stop during at least, what 3,4 months? It also stirred a lot of controversial homophobic movements, it was getting dangerous to come out...<br /> <br /> When I saw that this law had passed in England with just an afternoon of debate in the parliament, I was pissed off. It shouldn't have been that difficult. And even now, this law isn't assured to stay : Sarkozy, the official candidate of the Right for the elections in 2017, announced that he was to revoke this law.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T20:14:41-08:00","id":339703,"title":"","content":"I know I shouldn't because it's a stereotype, but I've been surprised a lot lately at how open, swingy, or sexually adventurous I've been discovering my straight friends to be lately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">