69#post340069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless someone is asexual, I think there are equal chances of finding someone not prudish among any other sexuality.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, pretty much. Most of the people I know with SERIOUS kinks happen to be heterosexual. I'm not saying my LGBT friends aren't into kink as well, but from just my own personal observations, seems any and every orientation or gender group can have some kinky members among them.<br /> <br /> I'm a bisexual man, and the only anal play I've ever tried has been with <i>women.</i> Orientation sometimes has less to do with what you're doing than simple intimacy. I suspect that's partly where all those odd apocryphal stories that used to float around about people trying Ecstasy for the first time and then gleefully exploring their butts with a friend come from. Once you trust people, you'll do all sorts of shit around/with them. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T14:17:22-08:00","id":340219,"title":"","content":"If we are talking about anal, generally I'm inclined to be