his stuff <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T20:21:50-08:00","id":414799,"title":"","content":"So I read through this thread and I have much respect for all of you for being so brave and resilient during your hard times.<br /> <br /> Lately I have been under the weather because I got into a big argument with my best female friend who is also bisexual. We have known each other for almost a decade and now things seem to be falling apart with us.The problem began when she had dreams about her boyfriend leaving her and due to that she's become paranoid about it, which I think is totally ridiculous. But I guess she feels like that because her boyfriend may still have a crush on our female friend who is also bisexual. She said if she were to break up with him she would go lesbian from now on because she was becoming tired of men. I didn't say anything but respect her idea. We talked it through about a week ago and turns out we were correct. I told her to talk it through with her boyfriend and see if they can come to an understanding. She did and they kind of resolved it, but now she feels discomfort towards me because she feels that I'm out to steal her boyfriend. I told her she was being ridiculous and should calm down. We talked about it but I felt she wasn't understanding me at all. The thing is she has always been too naive and stubborn--she basically likes to revel in her problems, which I still cannot understand why she does it. But anyways, I kind of see (I think) why she feels like that since I try to sleep with her boyfriend before they were ever together. I liked the guy because he looks like a bear guy. But I would never betray or become a crasher to my friends, its unforgivable. The guy on the other hand is a mess too. At one point he wanted to experiment with me then no then yes then no. He was giving me a nasty case of whiplash. I think because he's afraid of his sexuality due to his family's fear of homosexuality, which I despised so badly. In the end my female best friend decided not to talk to me or my female friend because we could not be trusted.<br /> <br /> Plus she gave me a guilt trip on how I would never be happy because I keep listening to my dick and not my heart. To be honest I haven't been in relationship because I wasn't interested, but now ever since my break up with my friends-with-benefits (due to me falling in love) I realized that I do want somebody to hold hands and snuggle with. I do yearn for that intimacy now. However, do I hate her for what she said to me? No, I can't. I care for her too much and probably forever will. Sorry for the drama you guys. I just want to talk to someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T15:12:14-08:00","id":415745,"title":"","content":"It is ok, is what we are here for <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Mmmmm, sorry about that drama though. If anything I would pitty her for being that way, really. That's a tiring way to live.<br /> <br /> EDIT: best wishes of luck on the finding a snuggling partner thing too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T16:21:05-08:00","id":415817,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Yeah, it is tiring. In our ten years of friendship I have always opened up my doors to comfort her when she feels bad and needs cheering. I have given her so much advice and my wisdom to resolve her issues, but in the end it feels like I'm talking to a wall. And yes, I do pity her as well. But I guess I never stopped caring for her because she has showed me the ropes on how to live around the city and showed me how to get a job. I guess you can say she's been my teacher, my stupid annoying stubborn naive teacher best friend lol<br /> <br /> Thanks dude, I appreciate. I hope so too I would find that snuggling person, whether its a guy or a girl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T07:32:31-08:00","id":417518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=415817#post415817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks dude, I appreciate. I hope so too I would find that snuggling person, whether its a guy or a girl.</div> </div> </div> </div>People keep telling me I'll find that person, too. They tell me because they care, and I appreciate that. I just wish it wouldn't be mentioned when I'm seemingly down, but have not specified verbally or otherwise that I'm sad because I'm alone. I admit, I'm a romantic and cynic, so I'll fall in love and hate myself for it with equal aplomb. I hate to say it, misanthrope that I try to be, that I find it hard not to love someone after you really know them. It's really one of my secret weaknesses, that ease of total love for another human being. It's one of the reasons I try to avoid friendships. <br /> <br /> When your chubby, bearded, dorky friend with&quot;issues&quot; tells you he loves you, things can get awkward. It has for me, as the chubby dork in love, enough times for me to almost give up on love as a thing I can have in my life.<br /> ..Almost. Apparently, I'm too stupid to know when I've lost. Funny thing, eh? Guess I'll just keep fighting with all my heart to find it. To find them.<br /> Some have said that&quot;I'll never learn&quot;,=in that regard. I hope I never do.<br /> <br /> I'm cynical and sarcastic as it is. I can't give up on the cornerstone of my dreams. Whether I like it or not, that's Love. The big kind. All in, even if you're afraid. The genuine article. Indiana Jones had his whip and his search for the Ark, the Holy Grail and some glowy stones and crystal skulls. I just have my heart and the search for love.<br /> <br /> I will admit that it's nice to be on this search without Nazis chasing after me for my secrets. Gracias para Dios for small favors, eh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 02-24-2015, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T14:58:32-08:00","id":418012,"title":"","content":"I understand dude. Dating, meeting new people, and sleeping with new people can be hard at first. It's good to keep your guard up to protect you but doing it constantly will get you nowhere, trust me. I had allot of friends who were like that until I brought them out of their shells. I told them to be confident in meeting new people and try to have fun. And if there already falling in love I tell them to take it slow and easy. Now if they want to fuck, then I tell them if that person is interested in doing that kind of stuff in the beginning, if so then go for it, as long as they are both comfortable.<br /> <br /> Oh trust me dude, I know. My female best friend who I have problems with right now wanted to sleep with me before. At first I was uncomfortable because she is my best female friend and I didn't want us to get complicated or awkward, but then she had real feelings for me and wanted to be in a relationship with me, which I didn't want to because I didn't feel the same way. With so much sincerity and trust I told her right away before things would get bad between us. I pleaded with her for us to stay as best friends, and fortunately she understood and agreed. Communication and trust have always been a key in my sex life and love life.<br /> <br /> If your looking for love dude, then maybe you should start with places or people who have a lot of common with you. That's my opinion, though. I have seen through my friends experiences and that's how most of them found their partners and lovers. One of them found each other by playing an online game that they both really love, and from then on it just happen.<br /> <br /> Sure, it's nice meeting new people who I can relate to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh, and good luck to you dude! I hope your love life in the future will go smooth and with much happiness.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T12:36:36-08:00","id":419159,"title":"","content":"@Cecoyotl<br /> That seems like genuinely sound advice. I do try to be friends with people I'm sexually interested in naturally, simply because I don't have the kind of libido that requires satisfaction without romance. I'm a big softie that way. Sex as recreation has never really been an option, though, so who knows? I just don't have any real experience in JUST sleeping with someone. There's always been a strong emotional component to sexual activity in my life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=418012#post418012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and good luck to you dude! I hope your love life in the future will go smooth and with much happiness.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks so much! And I wish you happiness and wellness in all things, sexual and otherwise. (:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T16:11:16-08:00","id":419505,"title":"","content":"I understand and I respect your decision. Its cool if your the romantic type, theirs lots of men who are like that. As for me, I'm more like the wild guy who likes to live life but in a wise way. I can also be the dirty type but just for fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm usually the romantic type when I'm in a relationship. <br /> <br /> Thanks dude!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T03:30:47-07:00","id":448973,"title":"","content":"I hate how being gay makes talking to people I have a romantic interest in about five times harder.<br /> Of course, it certainly doesn't help that I don't really know any other definitely gay people outside of the Internet.<br /> I mean, just talking about it with them and getting it off my chest would be enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 03-19-2015, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T15:44:50-07:00","id":449840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=448973#post448973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate how being gay makes talking to people I have a romantic interest in about five times harder.<br /> Of course, it certainly doesn't help that I don't really know any other definitely gay people outside of the Internet.<br /> I mean, just talking about it with them and getting it off my chest would be enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may ask, what *exactly* about being gay -- relative to your talking to people you may be romantically inclined to -- makes it so hard for you? That is, I understand the part about not knowing (m)any other gay people presents its own problems, of course, but otherwise what issues does it cause for you? I'm asking because it will influence how I further respond/lend advice, relative to the situation you describe...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T03:55:15-07:00","id":488119,"title":"","content":"So in the newest All-New X-Men comic teen Jean just outed teen Iceman, ooooh I can hear all the butt-hurt comic fan screaming at Bendis.","s