":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T14:28:02-07:00","id":510181,"title":"","content":"Well, it seems that there is a LOT of metrosexuals here. And many gays cultivate an effeminate or androgynous look. Not saying that it's bad, just that it's really not my taste : it's either that, or old bald skinny guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T15:52:49-07:00","id":518534,"title":"","content":"I just wanted share. I started watching this show call Where the Bears Are on YouTube. So far it's...okay, I guess. A little funny here and there but I got to say some of the cast members are hot, I like bears, there totally my type of men.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T19:38:22-07:00","id":518690,"title":"","content":"I'm a fan of <b>Where the Bear Are</b>. It's cast is increadiable, and the murder storylines are almost as convulent as mine own RPG games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's a nice Slasher inspiration with hot bears. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T13:49:42-07:00","id":519986,"title":"","content":"Ha ha nice! And sexy if I may add too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> To be honest I have the hots for detective Martinez and hotty Toddy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T09:03:55-07:00","id":523320,"title":"","content":"So tomorrow is going to be a historic day for the Republic of Ireland, in which the issue of gay marriage is going to be put to the vote.<br /> <br /> A brief bit of background; due to various factors that are too complex to get into here, the Irish Constitution contains clauses related directly to the definition and codification of marriage (as well as privileging the concept of the nuclear family). This means that, up until this point, issues related to extensions of marriage rights to gay people (as well as legal recognition of a family that does not consist of a married man and woman raising children) have had legal impediment in the very foundation of Irish law.<br /> <br /> However, there's an upside to this; due to the fact that the Constitution states that only a referendum put directly to the people in which a majority vote is returned is capable of making modifications to the Constitution, that means that the decision to revise the legal definition of marriage to be extended to homosexuals is going to be directly in the hands of the people.<br /> <br /> Another nice implication of it is that, as a constitutional matter, its ratification will retroactively incorporate the assumption of same-sex marriages into all existing marriage legislation (matters of family units, including adoption, are a technically legally separate issue, but the necessary legislation for that has already been passed and will be enacted within a matter of months).<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if it would necessarily <i>matter</i> if it was in the hands of politicians, considering that at the moment marriage equality has basically unilateral support from all major parties (in the Dail, only a single representative spoke in opposition to the bill to put the referendum before the people, and it passed without division), but it's still nice to be a direct participant.<br /> <br /> As of now, barring any problems with voter turn-out, it the amendment to the constitution will almost certainly pass; current polls indicate that somewhere between 70 and 80% of the Irish population is in favour of gay marriage and, in my personal opinion, the campaign for a &quot;No&quot; vote is astoundingly weak, largely having to rely on vague references to the idea that gay marriage allows for gay parents, which is bad for children (which not only completely disregards the idea of gay marriage <i>without</i> children, but has also been phrased in such a clumsy manner as to offend people related to adoption and surrogacy across the board), or the appeals to the idea that forcing some people to recognise marriage between people of the same sex is just mean.<br /> <br /> From what I've gathered, the most impact such campaigning has had is to confuse some people about what the referendum is actually about, and even that was something I heard several weeks ago.<br /> <br /> For myself, I am going to be quite happy to cast my vote tomorrow for extension and recognition of marriage for gay people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T15:13:13-07:00","id":523733,"title":"","content":"As writing it from Poland, I very much dediacted to watch what Ireland's referendum come to as result. Ireland is very Catholics-centered country. so Polish and Irish were many times likened. Our ex-premier, Donald Tusk, had a campaign slogan that &quot;we will make Poland in to Second Ireland&quot;. Still, when I read there is 70% of support for gay marriage in Ireland, and in Poland we had only bearly 40% in 2013 for Civil Unions - I'm so sad, and depressed by this.<br /> <br /> There is talk, that after our Presidents Election in Sunday, the bill about Civil Unions ( <u><i>very</i></u> restricted ) will be voted to <b>only read</b> on Thusday in Sejm, our parlament. Even if vote would come without the issues like <a href=\"http://www.pinknews.co.uk/2013/02/01/polish-mp-opposes-equal-marriage-because-gays-are-no-use-whatsoever-to-society/\" target=\"_blank\">Homophobic MP making </a><a href=\"http://www.pinknews.co.uk/2013/02/01/polish-mp-opposes-equal-marriage-because-gays-are-no-use-whatsoever-to-society/\" target=\"_blank\">disgusting statements about same sex couples</a> - like the last time - it's almost unreal to see the law passed in this parlament term. And next one will mostly be even more conservative, as showing polls. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The more I think about it, the more I'm depressed - this is fight for at least a next decade, and even then - maybe - we will have only Civil Unions... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-22-2015, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T20:05:44-07:00","id":523883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://i-d.vice.com/en_gb/article/a-powerful-collective-coming-out-in-ireland?utm_source=idtwitter\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i-d.vice.com/en_gb/article/a-powerful-collective-coming-out-in-ireland?utm_source=idtwitter\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i-d.vice.com/en_gb/article/a-powerful-collective-coming-out-in-ireland?utm_source=idtwitter\" target=\"_blank\"> https://i-d.vice.com/en_gb/article/a-powerful-collective-coming-out-in-ireland?utm_source=idtwitter </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A little piece on the activities in Ireland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T10:40:17-07:00","id":524571,"title":"","content":"Aw man... That totally sucks. Good luck to you guys. I hope everything goes smooth from now on. Here in the U.S. gay marriage is almost legal in every state, except for a few conservative states. Where I live, California, its legal now. To be honest I sometimes don't understand the world. What's the big idea of being homophobic? Where's your future in that? Saving people? Ha! Don't make me laugh. Seriously though, the world needs to change, we can't stay in the same place for the next decade or century. I say let people live. In my opinion religion and politics should never go together. It's just a terrible combination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T14:06:03-07:00","id":525887,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.rte.ie/news/vote2015/2015/0523/703205-referendum-byelection/\" target=\"_blank\">It got through</a>, by the way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T23:30:45-07:00","id":526431,"title":"","content":"I am very leery of Where the Bears Are...<br /> <br /> I heard so many good things about the movie Bear City from other bears and it was one of the most poorly acted movies I have ever seen. We are talking porn acting. Blarg. For that reason I don't know if I can trust recommendations for Where the Bears Are... &quot;Bear Blindness&quot; seems to be a thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The best bear movie I have seen (and there aren't many) is a Spanish movie called Cachorro. (Bear Cub in English) It's a little false advertised, though. The box art makes it look like a comedy where a bunch of bears end up having to take care of a child, with the inevitable hijinx ensuing. It's really more of a drama than anything. Still good, though.<br /> <br /> And congrats for any LGBT folks in Ireland. I think we Americans will forever be dragging our feet when it comes to civil rights issues, and patting ourselves on the back when we inevitably finish last.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T00:43:38-07:00","id":526453,"title":"","content":"Congrats, Ireland. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T20:34:20-07:00","id":528451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=526431#post526431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very leery of Where the Bears Are...<br /> I heard so many good things about the movie Bear City from other bears and it was one of the most poorly acted movies I have ever seen. We are talking porn acting. Blarg. For that reason I don't know if I can trust recommendations for Where the Bears Are... &quot;Bear Blindness&quot; seems to be a thing. ;</div> </div> </div> </div>It really is cute. The only disclaimers/caveats are that it is, of course, not a big budget thing (though the timing, editing, and color-toning are all very professional), and it is a comedy-bordering-on-farce (though not quite there -- think of how, for example, Absolutely Fabulous has some farcical qualities that bend the &quot;real world&quot; rules: Patsy surviving being in a full-blown burning room/being afflicted via voodoo doll by her sister, as well as Patsy being &quot;older than she should be&quot;; a needle traveling all the way through Eddie's body; Eddie having two children &quot;temporally out-of-sync&quot; -- married to her first husband and has a daughter, yet the daughter is younger than the son she had with her second husband, years later, and she couldn't even remember what the son looked like; etc.) If you're good with those two things you should love Where The Bears Are, which doesn't stretch reality *quite* that far... for the most part... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":1433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","user":"Just John, Forever...","date":". 05-25-2015, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T05:22:16-07:00","id":543814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=525887#post525887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.rte.ie/news/vote2015/2015/0523/703205-referendum-byelection/\" target=\"_blank\">It got through</a>, by the way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's also been announced that the laws on transgender gender recognition will be changed due to knock on affects from the new gender recognition bill at the Oireachtas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T08:36:21-07:00","id":569237,"title":"","content":"Supreme Court makes legal gay marriges in ALL United States!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://scontent-ams3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfp1/v/t1.0-9/10400044_10207071867219898_6886946194542838290_n.jpg?oh=a668b3244f97f3a912d0930ffb900611&amp;oe=562BCC71\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> In Poland still we do not have even Civil Unions... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T10:03:55-07:00","id":569357,"title":"","content":"Come over and get married! I'm super ecstatic over here!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1015-flintlock","name":"Flintlock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1015_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T10:19:08-07:00","id":569373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=569237#post569237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supreme Court makes legal gay marriges in ALL United States!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://scontent-ams3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfp1/v/t1.0-9/10400044_10207071867219898_6886946194542838290_n.jpg?oh=a668b3244f97f3a912d0930ffb900611&amp;oe=562BCC71\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> In Poland still we do not have even Civil Unions... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flintlock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=569357#post569357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come over and get married! I'm super ecstatic over here!</div> </div> </div> </div>And it still do not mean a thing, as we live in Poland, and it's laws are binding to us - even if we went to USA or other country for ceremony. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If I must emigrate, it would be Britain - we both are <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anglophile\" target=\"_blank\">Britiophiles</a>, and to UK there is easier transportation connection than pass the Ocean it USA. Also, at least for now, no migration barriers to England.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-26-2015, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T11:14:58-07:00","id":569423,"title":"","content":"Yay! It's finally legal here in the U.S. for same sex marriage! After a long battle of discrimination and injustice to the LGBT community we finally did it! So many have fought, struggle, spend sleepless nights, and may there souls rest have died for this right. I hope from now on we can finally progress as human beings into the future and make a better living for everyone. We did it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T15:22:08-07:00","id":569694,"title":"","content":"As happy as I am that the Court decided as it did, I really hope this doesn't come back and bite us in the ass, because I think the decision is wrong, in that it genuinely is a matter for the states; the federal Constitution doesn't have anything particularly on-point that puts gay marriage in their wheelhouse.<br /> <br /> Still, since I'm not sure anyone can say or do anything about it now, I'm gonna chalk it up as a win for the good guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T20:37:09-07:00","id":569891,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/bQCl4Zu.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>For once in a long time I am actually happy to have American citizenship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T21:17:51-07:00","id":569914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=569694#post569694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As happy as I am that the Court decided as it did, I really hope this doesn't come back and bite us in the ass, because I think the decision is wrong, in that it genuinely is a matter for the states; the federal Constitution doesn't have anything particularly on-point that puts gay marriage in their wheelhouse.<br /> <br /> Still, since I'm not sure anyone can say or do anything about it now, I'm gonna chalk it up as a win for the good guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jim, don't sweat it. It won't come back to bite anyone in the ass, because the only way gay marriage could be stopped in America now is if a Constitutional Amendment forbidding same-sex marriage was passed. That would take 2/3 of <i>both </i>Houses of Congress and 3/4 of <i>all </i>States to ratify that amendment. With 62% of all Americans (and climbing!) approving of gay marriage, any anti-gay marriage amendment Just. Won't. Get. Passed.<br /> <br /> And the SCOTUS decision was based on both Equal Protection in the 14th Amendment and on Due Process. Both of those are federal issues so, it was properly decided by the Supreme Court. This just wasn't a state matter at all; SCOTUS had the proper jurisdiction and never mind what the dissent said.<br /> <br /> Gay marriage and ObamaCare are both here to stay. So proud to be an American today. Love Wins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":". 06-27-2015, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T02:28:17-07:00","id":570081,"title":"","content":"God damn I wish I was in San Francisco this weekend<br /> <br /> Pride is going to be BANANAS","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T09:08:58-07:00","id":570288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=570081#post570081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God damn I wish I was in San Francisco this weekend<br /> <br /> Pride is going to be BANANAS</div> </div> </div> </div>I desperately wish I had gotten off work earlier Friday so I could have seen how crazy Capitol Hill probably was on Friday here in Seattle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T19:33:47-07:00","id":570806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=569694#post569694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As happy as I am that the Court decided as it did, I really hope this doesn't come back and bite us in the ass, because I think the decision is wrong, in that it genuinely is a matter for the states; the federal Constitution doesn't have anything particularly on-point that puts gay marriage in their wheelhouse.<br /> <br /> Still, since I'm not sure anyone can say or do anything about it now, I'm gonna chalk it up as a win for the good guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it makes you feel any better I've heard this exact same argument several times in US history (it should be a state matter, feds keep your noses out!).<br /> It came up with segregation.<br /> It came up with women voting.<br /> It came up slavery.<br /> <br /> There have been several others but those are the big three that come to mind.<br /> <br /> In all cases several states were for and against whatever the issue was, and in all cases religion came into play, and in all cases the US federal governments finally stepped in with something like this. Usually after most other western nations had already accepted the measures. When something should be a basic right acknowledged universally and consistently across the country, it MUST be handled at a federal level and not a state level.<br /> <br /> <br /> Taking a step to the side, let me state that this is coming from a hetrosexual white male, so I don't have any wood on the hearth in the debate.<br /> <br /> I *fully* support this as a federal decision, because now it IS federal. It eliminates paperwork, it eliminates confusion and chaos. It eliminates inheritance issues, hospital visitation headaches and above all else it means you *DON'T* have 20+ *different* versions of the same goal in different wording paperwork and with different limits in all the different states.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T08:55:17-07:00","id":571471,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that in all previous cases, federal intervention took the form of a Constitutional amendment by Congress or, in the case of segregation, a ruling by the Supreme Court that states' rights don't trump the fourteenth amendment (as in, Jim Crow laws were deliberate efforts to bypass the plain meaning of the 14th amendment by claiming that only the Federal Government was bound by it). Whether you like the result of this ruling or not, it is <i>not</i> a case of restoring legal sanity against forces who were attempting to pervert the meaning of the Constitution or its amentments. Arguably, it's quite the opposite: I fully expect to see challenges brought forward very soon arguing for polygamy using this ruling as a basis; and I suspect that it will only be a matter of time before lawsuits are brought again churches to force them to officiate or otherwise endorse same-sex weddings. I <i>don't</i> think that the majority of the LGBT community is in favor of such developments; but it doesn't take a majority \u2014 just a vocal minority with legal expertise and a good PR department. <br /> <br /> Personally, I prefer to win an argument by convincing others that I'm in the right, not by compelling them to do things my way or else. And the gay marriage agenda was well on its way to accomplishing the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T18:22:06-07:00","id":572052,"title":"","content":"Too ...many...neurons...firing here....need dumber...topic...<br /> <br /> I'm avoiding both my girlfriend and my fwb (female, fwiw) (it's kosher, no worries) while simultaneously immersing myself in a few classic yaoi mangas and a Stephen King novel that, depending on perspective, CAN be construed as subtly homoerotic.<br /> <br /> Am I shying from female company or just people in general?<br /> <br /> I can't tell sometimes, because most of my social circle and family consists of women.<br /> <br /> I feel like I'm rebelling and using being bi as a vehicle, but I'm also famous for blaming myself for shit I didn't do, so I'm just confused. More to come.<br /> <br /> I have only begun to ramble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T21:52:46-07:00","id":572175,"title":"","content":"Any bisexual people want to talk about bisexuality? I recently read an article on bisexual erasure, which is a term I'm not incredibly proficient with the use of, but it got me thinking there may be more to bisexuality than I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T23:11:06-07:00","id":572320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=572175#post572175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any bisexual people want to talk about bisexuality? I recently read an article on bisexual erasure, which is a term I'm not incredibly proficient with the use of, but it got me thinking there may be more to bisexuality than I know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how much I could articulate on bisexuality, and I've read an article or two on bisexual erasure. Mostly it's the assumptions that often come into play about us bisexual people, particularly I think because it's a wide spectrum. Some of the more common ones are things like we are constantly horny freaky people(personally I am practically asexual these days), that we are &quot;not really&quot; bisexual at all but really gay, lesbian or straight and that we claim bisexuality for a variety of reasons including being afraid of coming out to friends and family, personal insecurities,etc.<br /> <br /> One I've personally had happen a lot is the &quot;But you have a child, how can you also be attracted to guys?&quot; line. The most I do to reply is basically say, you know that fluttery feeling you get when you see someone of the sex you are attracted to that you find appealing? Yeah I get that for people of both sexes. Some people get it( ie understand me), some don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 06-29-2015, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T03:09:21-07:00","id":572489,"title":"","content":"Bisexuality erasure is something cronic and endemic I'm afraid. Even among the LGBT collective.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I mean, I have gay men given me &quot;the look&quot; when I indentified as bisexual. Opinions varied from &quot;actually gay but afraid of coming out&quot; to &quot;Straight guy pretending&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T08:13:35-07:00","id":572652,"title":"","content":"Bi Erasure also shows up at every Pride Festival when our &quot;opposite sex&quot; partners with us. Never mind that the first Pride Festival was orchestrated by a Bisexual Woman and her male partner, who were both participants in the Stonewall Riots...<br /> <br /> Another form of biphobia is that &quot;bisexual&quot; routinely gets accused of being transphobic, yet somehow &quot;gay&quot; and &quot;lesbian&quot; aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T08:39:55-07:00","id":572711,"title":"","content":"Bisexual=Transphobic is one I didn't came across. It kind of baffles me, if anything I expected people to think bisexuals would love transgender(ed)* people.<br /> <br /> *still not sure what the correct form is, sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T09:28:48-07:00","id":572785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=572711#post572711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bisexual=Transphobic is one I didn't came across. It kind of baffles me, if anything I expected people to think bisexuals would love transgender(ed)* people.<br /> <br /> *still not sure what the correct form is, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is that &quot;bisexual&quot; means &quot;both men and women&quot; and therefore reinforces the gender binary and excludes Transfolk. The idea is hogwash. I personally choose it to mean &quot;both homo- and hetero- [in the classical sense of hereto- meaning unidentical, not the modern sense of hetero- as 'straight']&quot; or &quot;both directions on the spectrum&quot;, but a lot of people prefer pansexual these days. I went through enough pain and angst getting to bisexual and I'm not really in a position to rethink my identity as pansexual, though a YouTuber I like recently introduced me to the concept of &quot;meow meow meow&quot; as an orientation non-identity, and that's kind of appealing.<br /> <br /> Transgendered would be the noun form of some sort of verb &quot;transgender&quot; that doesn't exist. Transgender is an adjective. Transgender is correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T13:45:03-07:00","id":573110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=571471#post571471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fully expect to see challenges brought forward very soon arguing for polygamy using this ruling as a basis</div> </div> </div> </div>This might happen and I would welcome the chance to have a national discussion on such an issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=571471#post571471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that it will only be a matter of time before lawsuits are brought again churches to force them to officiate or otherwise endorse same-sex weddings.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, I don't see happening, and I don't see how this case would be used even if it did. Churches have a lot of slack in the law.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T13:48:50-07:00","id":573123,"title":"","content":"To be fair, the terminology homosexual, heterosexual and bisexual all imply that attraction is based on sex as opposed to gender, and that sex is binary. But, like, that's a fault of the language, and the fact that the terms were developed at a time when there was very little trans and intersex visibility. To say that being bi is transphobic because the word bi doesn't account for more than two possibilities is pedantic at best.<br /> <br /> What <i>would</i> be transphobic would be to exclude trans people from the people you're attracted to because they fall outside the binary. But that's not a problem exclusive to bisexual people. Straight, gay, lesbian, bi, pan, what ever you identify as, if you're into men that should include trans men, if you're into women that should include trans women.<br /> <br /> And yeah, it's transgender. Saying someone is transgendered is like saying someone is gayed. It just doesn't really make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T14:45:15-07:00","id":573197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=571471#post571471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that in all previous cases, federal intervention took the form of a Constitutional amendment by Congress or, in the case of segregation, a ruling by the Supreme Court that states' rights don't trump the fourteenth amendment (as in, Jim Crow laws were deliberate efforts to bypass the plain meaning of the 14th amendment by claiming that only the Federal Government was bound by it). Whether you like the result of this ruling or not, it is <i>not</i> a case of restoring legal sanity against forces who were attempting to pervert the meaning of the Constitution or its amentments. Arguably, it's quite the opposite: I fully expect to see challenges brought forward very soon arguing for polygamy using this ruling as a basis<br /> <br /> Personally, I prefer to win an argument by convincing others that I'm in the right, not by compelling them to do things my way or else. And the gay marriage agenda was well on its way to accomplishing the former.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been wanting to talk about this since the ruling came down, and for some reason have only just now found this board. First I should start saying I fully support the rights campaign that's been happening and was very happy with the result of the court's decision. What I discovered that day however, was an angle on the discussion I hadn't seen before via the dissenting judges opinions. I.E. The notion that it should have been done via a constitutional amendment as this ruling creates a new precedent in how the Supreme Court can interact with the Constitution, an interaction that can be seen as dangerous to democracy. The more I've thought about the more that one singular detail actually has some merit to me, and does worry me a little. <br /> <br /> That's really off the LGBT topic though, so back to what this board is for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=571471#post571471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and I suspect that it will only be a matter of time before lawsuits are brought again churches to force them to officiate or otherwise endorse same-sex weddings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree with Ophid here in that I don't see how this case would be used for that at all, nor do I think such cases would get anywhere given how widely accepted the argument is that they strictly violate the First Amendment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T16:10:22-07:00","id":573306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=573197#post573197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been wanting to talk about this since the ruling came down, and for some reason have only just now found this board. First I should start saying I fully support the rights campaign that's been happening and was very happy with the result of the court's decision. What I discovered that day however, was an angle on the discussion I hadn't seen before via the dissenting judges opinions. I.E. The notion that it should have been done via a constitutional amendment as this ruling creates a new precedent in how the Supreme Court can interact with the Constitution, an interaction that can be seen as dangerous to democracy. The more I've thought about the more that one singular detail actually has some merit to me, and does worry me a little.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have to agree with Ophid here in that I don't see how this case would be used for that at all, nor do I think such cases would get anywhere given how widely accepted the argument is that they strictly violate the First Amendment. </div> </div> </div>These two are connected: this ruling basically had no Constitutional basis, but was instead an affirmation of what the majority thought ought to be the case. It's not much of a stretch from there to a ruling that religious objections to same-sex unions amount to bigotry and ought not be protected by the First Amentment \u2014 and by the same reasoning that allowed SCOTUS to establish a right to same-sex unions without any legislative involvement, I could easily see a SCOTUS ruling that declares that religious objections to same-sex unions are invalid, the First Amendment be damned. <br /> <br /> That's what's so dangerous about this precedent: SCOTUS is no longer ruling on what the Constitution says; it's ruling on what five of nine Justices personally consider to be right and moral. It doesn't help that several of the states where gay marriage wasn't legal prior to this ruling are encouraging state officers who object to stand on the First Amendment and refuse to perform said unions; that's setting up a direct confrontation between religious freedom and gay marriage; and given Justice Kennedy's opinion on this ruling, if any of them make it to the Supreme Court, I will not be the least bit surprised if the Court says that the right to gay marriage trumps religous liberty. <br /> <br /> But you're right; this tangent isn't really about LGBT issues, as you ought to be able to have an opinion on whether the Supreme Court acted properly or overreached independent of whether or not you approve of the immediate consequence of same-sex marriage now being legal throughout the US. Put another way: regardless of whether you feel that the national legalization of same-sex unions is a good thing, there's reason to question whether this was the right way to do it. <br /> <br /> Perhaps we should split this off into a separate discussion about the powers and responsibilities of the various branches of the federal government?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T18:48:40-07:00","id":573435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=573306#post573306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These two are connected: this ruling basically had no Constitutional basis, but was instead an affirmation of what the majority thought ought to be the case. It's not much of a stretch from there to a ruling that religious objections to same-sex unions amount to bigotry and ought not be protected by the First Amentment \u2014 and by the same reasoning that allowed SCOTUS to establish a right to same-sex unions without any legislative involvement, I could easily see a SCOTUS ruling that declares that religious objections to same-sex unions are invalid, the First Amendment be damned.<br /> <br /> That's what's so dangerous about this precedent: SCOTUS is no longer ruling on what the Constitution says; it's ruling on what five of nine Justices personally consider to be right and moral. It doesn't help that several of the states where gay marriage wasn't legal prior to this ruling are encouraging state officers who object to stand on the First Amendment and refuse to perform said unions; that's setting up a direct confrontation between religious freedom and gay marriage; and given Justice Kennedy's opinion on this ruling, if any of them make it to the Supreme Court, I will not be the least bit surprised if the Court says that the right to gay marriage trumps religous liberty.<br /> <br /> But you're right; this tangent isn't really about LGBT issues, as you ought to be able to have an opinion on whether the Supreme Court acted properly or overreached independent of whether or not you approve of the immediate consequence of same-sex marriage now being legal throughout the US. Put another way: regardless of whether you feel that the national legalization of same-sex unions is a good thing, there's reason to question whether this was the right way to do it.<br /> <br /> Perhaps we should split this off into a separate discussion about the powers and responsibilities of the various branches of the federal government?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd be perfectly fine with that, as I'd like to continue the discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=573123#post573123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, the terminology homosexual, heterosexual and bisexual all imply that attraction is based on sex as opposed to gender, and that sex is binary. But, like, that's a fault of the language, and the fact that the terms were developed at a time when there was very little trans and intersex visibility. To say that being bi is transphobic because the word bi doesn't account for more than two possibilities is pedantic at best.<br /> <br /> What <i>would</i> be transphobic would be to exclude trans people from the people you're attracted to because they fall outside the binary. But that's not a problem exclusive to bisexual people. Straight, gay, lesbian, bi, pan, what ever you identify as, if you're into men that should include trans men, if you're into women that should include trans women.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, this is where I want to tread carefully, for multiple reasons.<br /> <br /> 1) I want to make sure I understand what your saying, as this is a topic that has interested me for some time as my own knowledge of the meaning behind a <i>lot</i> of the terminology in the LGBT is rather lacking.<br /> <br /> 2) I want to express myself clearly so what I say comes across as what I mean, so please ask for any clarification if you slightly confused on anything I say.<br /> <br /> First; As I understand them and see them the terms sex and gender mean two different things (I know this is obvious and I don't mean to imply you don't already know what I'm saying, I've just had trouble in these kinds of discussions before due to communication errors, so, like I said, clarity). Sex is the biological construction of your body in terms that categorize certain aspects into certain groups, the two most common of these is male and female, and the most commonly used biological difference in common discussion is often the reproductive organs. It is what falls outside of these two categories where I am most ignorant. Gender I see as a social and cultural construction built around these two common categories and they are referred to most commonly as 'man' and 'woman', 'guys' and 'girls' etc. tacked on to these constructions are a massive host of behaviors, modes of thinking, means of expression, likes and dislikes (the list goes on) that are determined to belong to 'men' and 'women'.<br /> <br /> Second; My current understanding of a transgender person is someone who is of the, for example, Male sex but a woman in gender identity, is this how you see it or do we define them as different things? Again, I put forward my own serious lack of knowledge on this topic.<br /> <br /> Third; Addressing your actual post, your are saying it is transphobic to be someone who is hetero-sexual and not attracted to a trans-person of the sex and gender you are attracted to? For example, a someone of the female sex and girl gender is attracted to those of the male sex and male gender, for her to not be attracted to someone of the female sex but male gender (a trans person). Is this correct?<br /> <br /> Addendum; I understand I'm talking in mostly binaries here, which you pointed out isn't the actual reality in all cases. I don't disagree with you, but like I've said I'm incredibly ignorant on the topic and and trying to use the most basic example possible to see if I understand what your saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T19:00:55-07:00","id":573454,"title":"","content":"I don't have a lot of patience with the &quot;supreme court was overstepping their authority&quot; argument, because (a) most of the people I've seen doing these analyses are absolutely not lawyers, much less lawyers with any special grounding in constitutional law, and (b) it <i>juuuust coincidentally</i> began with and is being spread by people who had already been railing against gay marriage for years.<br /> <br /> I'd certainly prefer it not be in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T19:32:41-07:00","id":573477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=573454#post573454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have a lot of patience with the &quot;supreme court was overstepping their authority&quot; argument, because (a) most of the people I've seen doing these analyses are absolutely not lawyers, much less lawyers with any special grounding in constitutional law, and (b) it <i>juuuust coincidentally</i> began with and is being spread by people who had already been railing against gay marriage for years.<br /> <br /> I'd certainly prefer it not be in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I apologize for potentially de-railing the thread, but we have agreed to take it elsewhere as we recognize that's not what this place is for. If you'd like I can pm you when its up and we're talking as I'd love to respond to your opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T21:34:14-07:00","id":573555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=573435#post573435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, this is where I want to tread carefully, for multiple reasons.<br /> <br /> 1) I want to make sure I understand what your saying, as this is a topic that has interested me for some time as my own knowledge of the meaning behind a <i>lot</i> of the terminology in the LGBT is rather lacking.<br /> <br /> 2) I want to express myself clearly so what I say comes across as what I mean, so please ask for any clarification if you slightly confused on anything I say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. I'll do my best to help clarify.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=573435#post573435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First; As I understand them and see them the terms sex and gender mean two different things (I know this is obvious and I don't mean to imply you don't already know what I'm saying, I've just had trouble in these kinds of discussions before due to communication errors, so, like I said, clarity). Sex is the biological construction of your body in terms that categorize certain aspects into certain groups, the two most common of these is male and female, and the most commonly used biological difference in common discussion is often the reproductive organs. It is what falls outside of these two categories where I am most ignorant. Gender I see as a social and cultural construction built around these two common categories and they are referred to most commonly as 'man' and 'woman', 'guys' and 'girls' etc. tacked on to these constructions are a massive host of behaviors, modes of thinking, means of expression, likes and dislikes (the list goes on) that are determined to belong to 'men' and 'women'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. Sex refers to biological differences between people, whereas gender is a social construct. Both exist on a spectrum, but western culture tends to reduce those spectrums down to the two opposite extremes and to link sex and gender. The term intersex is something of a catch-all for people who exist in between the extreme ends of the sex spectrum, but it's not just three possible states. There are people with penises and XX chromosomes. There are people with vaginas and XY chromosomes. There are people with penises and breasts. There are more possibilities on the sex spectrum than would fit into a convenient list, all of them naturally occurring, if somewhat less commonly than the two we often treat as binary. And, of course, people can be of any gender, regardless of their sex.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=573435#post573435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second; My current understanding of a transgender person is someone who is of the, for example, Male sex but a woman in gender identity, is this how you see it or do we define them as different things? Again, I put forward my own serious lack of knowledge on this topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is essentially correct, but still thinking in terms of a binary. Ultimately, a transgender person is someone who's gender identity does not match the gender that was assigned to them at birth. Conversely, a cisgender* person is someone who's gender identity does match the gender that was assigned to them at birth. <br /> <br /> So, someone who was born with a penis and their parents said &quot;yep, that's a boy alright&quot; would be cisgender if they grew up identifying as a boy, and felt that was an accurate description of them. They would be transgender if they instead grew up and decided they actually felt more like something else - maybe they would rather be identified as a girl, but it's also possible they might identify somewhere in-between the two extremes of boy/girl,** or they might not identify with any gender at all.*** Often, people who feel their gender identity is best described by something other than &quot;male/boy/man/guy/etc.&quot; or &quot;female/girl/woman/gal/etc.&quot; prefer that name over transgender, but they are still considered to be on the &quot;trans spectrum.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, for example, I was assigned the gender &quot;male&quot; at birth, due to having the physiology typically associated with the male gender. Growing up, I never felt particularly uncomfortable being identified this way, as many trans people do. However, I found that I occasionally felt that I would be more comfortable being thought of as a girl. I knew that some people felt like they were born &quot;in the wrong body****&quot; , but I assumed that must not be what I was feeling, because being identified as a boy didn't feel wrong <i>per se</i>, and to complicate matters, the feeling wasn't all the time. Sometimes boy seemed more right than girl, other times girl seemed more right. Eventually I learned that gender is far more complicated than just males and females and sometimes people feeling wrong as one and wanting to switch to the other. Not long after I became aware of a term called &quot;gender-fluid,&quot; which describes someone who's gender identity is not constant, but shifts along a spectrum of feeling sometimes more masculine or sometimes more feminine. My research on the matter resonated strongly with me as it perfectly described something I had always felt, but never before understood or been able to articulate. So, now I describe myself as gender-fluid, but because that identity is different from the one assigned to me at birth, that also makes me (a form of) trans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=573435#post573435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third; Addressing your actual post, your are saying it is transphobic to be someone who is hetero-sexual and not attracted to a trans-person of the sex and gender you are attracted to? For example, a someone of the female sex and girl gender is attracted to those of the male sex and male gender, for her to not be attracted to someone of the female sex but male gender (a trans person). Is this correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eehhhh... Sort of, but this analysis conflates the genders &quot;male&quot; and &quot;female&quot; with sexual physiology. What I'm saying is, if someone excludes people who were assigned a different gender at birth from the people they are sexually attracted to, that's transphobic. <br /> <br /> In your example, person A is a cisgender woman; she was assigned female at birth, she agreed with that identity all of her life, no problems. She considers herself heterosexual, meaning she is sexually attracted to men (the &quot;opposite&quot; gender from the one that she identifies with). Person B is a transgender man; he was assigned female at birth, but at some point came to the conclusion that he did not identify with that assignment, and instead began identifying as a man. He also considers himself heterosexual, meaning he is sexually attracted to women (the &quot;opposite&quot; gender from the one he identifies with). If person A and person B meet and find they are mutually attracted to each other, but then at some point down the line person A finds out that person B was assigned female at birth and decides she is no longer attracted to him because of that, that's transphobic. Obviously, if person A isn't attracted to person B because person B is not her type, that's just normal not-being-attracted-to-a-person. Happens all the time. But, if person A <i>would otherwise</i> be attracted to person B, but excludes that possibility because person B is trans, that would be transphobic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=573435#post573435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Addendum; I understand I'm talking in mostly binaries here, which you pointed out isn't the actual reality in all cases. I don't disagree with you, but like I've said I'm incredibly ignorant on the topic and and trying to use the most basic example possible to see if I understand what your saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a problem, I'm happy to help explain. It's worth noting that there are a lot of different models out there, and a great deal of disagreement on which model is &quot;right.&quot; What I am describing here is a very academic model, and one that is generally agreed on by much of the trans community. There are people in the medical community who disagree with it. There are people in the LGBT community who disagree with it. There are people in the trans community who disagree with it. It's a complicated and controversial subject, so there are understandably a lot of conflicting opinions. But, like I said, this model is the one used by a large portion of the trans community (I won't say majority because I only have anecdotal evidence of its usage).<br /> <br /> *\u200b(cis being a latin prefix meaning &quot;on the same side as,&quot; and antonymous with trans, which is also a latin prefix meaning &quot;across from&quot;)<br /> **(this is where you get into even more terms like genderqueer, gender-fluid, bigender, etc.)<br /> ***(typically referred to as agender)<br /> ****(actually a very inaccurate and misleading way to describe the phenomenon of gender dysphoria)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-30-2015, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T08:24:34-07:00","id":573977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=571471#post571471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether you like the result of this ruling or not, it is <i>not</i> a case of restoring legal sanity against forces who were attempting to pervert the meaning of the Constitution or its amentments.</div> </div> </div> </div>This ruling is a natural consequence of the principle behind, and the wording of, the 14th Amendment. That the people who wrote the 14th Amendment likely did not consider this consequence valid is moot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T12:04:53-07:00","id":574172,"title":"","content":"That is indeed what Justice Kennedy said. In deference to those who don't want this discussed in this thread, I'll stop there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T12:19:23-07:00","id":574179,"title":"","content":"It is an interesting topic and might be worth starting a separate thread for though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T12:34:31-07:00","id":574204,"title":"","content":"Fuck, the more I listen to people who I think hold the legally correct position (that this was judicial overreach), the more my own position changes just to spite those assholes. I'm not even kidding. I genuinely feel like these dicks are so wrong, I need to alter my own understanding just to not be like them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T13:24:26-07:00","id":574289,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Hey guys, I know this is a controversial subject and people are understandably passionate about it, but remember to avoid personal and group attacks.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T13:32:36-07:00","id":574321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=574204#post574204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fuck, the more I listen to people who I think hold the legally correct position (that this was judicial overreach), the more my own position changes just to spite those assholes. I'm not even kidding. I genuinely feel like these dicks are so wrong, I need to alter my own understanding just to not be like them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I recommend you read <a href=\"http://www.scotusblog.com/case-files/cases/obergefell-v-hodges/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.scotusblog.com/case-files...fell-v-hodges/</a>, particularly these analyses of the Majority Ruling:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.scotusblog.com/2015/06/symposium-a-fair-and-proper-application-of-the-fourteenth-amendment/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/pito4za5/production/925bcb29d8e6ec019138124ba8a96220a1cf75c6-500x333.jpg?rect=0,37,500,261&amp;w=1200&amp;h=627&amp;fit=crop\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scotusblog.com/2015/06/symposium-a-fair-and-proper-application-of-the-fourteenth-amendment/\" target=\"_blank\"> Symposium: A fair and proper application of the Fourteenth Amendment </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scotusblog.com/2015/06/symposium-a-fair-and-proper-application-of-the-fourteenth-amendment/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.scotusblog.com/2015/06/symposium-a-fair-and-proper-application-of-the-fourteenth-amendment/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> June 26, 2015 is a day to celebrate. (Indeed, we are going to have to make June 26 some sort of gay rights holiday now that Lawrence v. Texas, United States v. Windsor and Obergefell v. Hodges all ca&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.scotusblog.com/2015/06/symposium-sometimes-it-takes-unelected-justices-not-the-political-process-to-give-americans-the-law-they-really-want/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/pito4za5/production/925bcb29d8e6ec019138124ba8a96220a1cf75c6-500x333.jpg?rect=0,37,500,261&amp;w=1200&amp;h=627&amp;fit=crop\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scotusblog.com/2015/06/symposium-sometimes-it-takes-unelected-justices-not-the-political-process-to-give-americans-the-law-they-really-want/\" target=\"_blank\"> Symposium: Sometimes it takes unelected Justices, not the political process, to give Americans the law they really want </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scotusblog.com/2015/06/symposium-sometimes-it-takes-unelected-justices-not-the-political-process-to-give-americans-the-law-they-really-want/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.scotusblog.com/2015/06/symposium-sometimes-it-takes-unelected-justices-not-the-political-process-to-give-americans-the-law-they-really-want/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Steve Sanders teaches constitutional law, constitutional litigation, and family law at the Indiana University Maurer School of Law. He was co-counsel on an amicus brief in support of the petitioners&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.scotusblog.com/2015/06/symposium-the-constitution-has-everything-to-do-with-it/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/pito4za5/production/925bcb29d8e6ec019138124ba8a96220a1cf75c6-500x333.jpg?rect=0,37,500,261&amp;w=1200&amp;h=627&amp;fit=crop\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scotusblog.com/2015/06/symposium-the-constitution-has-everything-to-do-with-it/\" target=\"_blank\"> Symposium: The Constitution has everything to do with it </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scotusblog.com/2015/06/symposium-the-constitution-has-everything-to-do-with-it/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.scotusblog.com/2015/06/symposium-the-constitution-has-everything-to-do-with-it/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Judith E. Schaeffer is the Vice President of the Constitutional Accountability Center Whether by design or serendipity, today&rsquo;s historic ruling in Obergefell v. Hodges came on the anniversaries of tw&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They may help you alter your own understanding, even if it's just to be better equipped to disagree with those of us that agreed with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T20:34:22-07:00","id":574673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=574289#post574289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:red\">Hey guys, I know this is a controversial subject and people are understandably passionate about it, but remember to avoid personal and group attacks.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry.<br /> <br /> Ten characters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T13:05:06-07:00","id":575529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=573977#post573977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This ruling is a natural consequence of the principle behind, and the wording of, the 14th Amendment. That the people who wrote the 14th Amendment likely did not consider this consequence valid is moot.</div> </div> </div> </div>And personally I don't know of what consequence there is for armchair lawyers to get from engaging in an attempt to poison a victory for civil rights with what sounds to be little more than a variation on &quot;States rights!&quot; cries. If there was a real case to be made that the Constitution isn't equipped for it, it failed to make it's case apparently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T16:18:11-07:00","id":575753,"title":"","content":"Since there is a lot of interest in the topic I have created a separate thread for discussion about the SCOTUS Ruling in a legal-ish sense. In order to not further de-rail the LGBT topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/575747-discussing-the-scotus-ruling\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/575747-discussing-the-scotus-ruling\"> Discussing The SCOTUS Ruling - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/575747-discussing-the-scotus-ruling\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/575747-discussing-the-scotus-ruling </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I'm creating this topic because there seems to be a lot of interest in expressing not just support or disagreement with the Supreme Courts recent ruling, but also in the legal mechanics behind it. Many people, have been mulling over whether or not the ruling truly was a form of judicial over-reach. Therefore </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T11:25:03-07:00","id":654103,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://media.giphy.com/media/136V8raQQogOfm/giphy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Why has this thread been ignored for a month? People be acting like they ain't got time for they message boards. Shoot.<br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> <br /> Random issue: I sometimes find furriness cute on people. Not as in Yiff. I mean body hair. Sorry, Furries I may have excited for a moment. I'm bi, so I find it kinda silly to discriminate about that for either gender. Hairy bear? Awesome? Full-on &quot;my vagina was a p.o.w. in Vietnam&quot; bush? Into the jungle!<br /> <br /> But I'm finding myself getting rejected a lot recently because of the flipside of that: hairless body. I very recently got into a great conversation online with this (out of my league. I aim for the stars just in case I can randomly be the first guy to punt a meteorite) very handsome guy. He flirted. I flirted. It got VERY blush-worthy. <br /> <br /> You kinda get where this is going, but let's finish the ride together. <br /> Eventually we realize that we're two people flirting on camera and that Zero cases of crabs are contracted that way, so we start getting sexual. First just verbally and then the clothes started coming off like two weird lizards squaring off, maintaining eye contact while systematically doing a slow elbow and knee filled dance that just coincidentally gets you naked. <br /> <br /> ..And within two minutes the words &quot;I really wish you had more hair on you. Later&quot; came out of the mouth he used for his face every day. He didn't type that shit or kinda just insinuate sudden disinterest. He appraised me, and NOPED my ass for having no chest hair to my face with his talky hole while looking me in the eye. I just used a lot of body parts in that last sentence.<br /> <br /> It's happening with women too, just not as dramatically as that. I know that some people like a lot of hair sometimes, myself included. I have it on my head and junk. ..just not anywhere else. I've also been told repeatedly that chihuahua-like hairless quality is attractive, by men and women. It just seems like there's a little unfair play here. <br /> <br /> \u200bNext person who has purposely shaved their OWN body and decides to critique my gaia-given smoothness is hearing &quot;I'd complain about YOU, but I'm not an asshole like that.&quot; <br /> Wait, one more thing. I kinda have a little crush (read: I'd totally steal her pillow to cuddle it) on a fellow comedian. That belongs here. I'll explain later maybe.<br /> <br /> OH, ONE MORE THING!!<br /> <br /> I totally WAS dating someone! Hangover Me was right! They dumped me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T15:11:12-07:00","id":654481,"title":"","content":"Oh, Az. Sorry about the dumping you part. I'm curious about your fellow comedian crush though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:21:01-07:00","id":654534,"title":"","content":"The dumping was understandable. We had absolutely nothing in common, except for a lot of things. Thanks for the sympathy, though. It was just another case of being presented with a good relationship on the surface that would slowly consume me spiritually from within like a vicious extradimensional parasite.<br /> <br /> The comedian crush...<br /> <br /> God, it's so one-sided I could cry monopoles. It's mainly because I've said nothing to her about finding her attractive, or just made light flirty conversation. She's nice. I dunno. We've been corresponding regularely in various ways for a few weeks. I kinda don't want to share more about her, just because you know the internet, some asshole will find this and go &quot;Omfg I've seen her on YouTube. Going to Facebook immediately!!&quot; and unlike me, her fanbase is getting respectable. It's being posted in THIS thread, so there's a little bit more to it. If I ever get lucky enough to go out with her, you'll totally see her stuff so you can smirk until your face hurts. Until then, isn't that kinda too much info to go on further, considering both of us are technically public figures? I'm actually looking to get an answer here.<br /> <br /> Jesus jackrabbit set on high Christ, I'm technically a public figure now.<br /> Please tell me I'm wrong. Come on. I'm kinda baked now. I drink. I could be totes wrong.<br /> If not...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><u><b><span style=\"font-size:26px\">Joey Polanco for President 2024!</span></b></u></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 09-06-2015, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:32:55-07:00","id":654540,"title":"","content":"Sorry dude, that sucks. But hey, don't let that get you down. I'm sure there are men who like hairless guys, though be careful cause some are expecting to see a nice model athletic body, hmph! As for women, most like it when a guy is hairless, that's my experience. But don't give up dude! I'm sure you'll find someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T17:00:11-07:00","id":654578,"title":"","content":"If it helps, I generally like my guys fairly smooth. I mean I'm married and off the market, but there are guys who like their guys fairly smooth, just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T09:13:07-07:00","id":655199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_contain