 class=\"message\">Oh, crap. I know is stupid but I can't shake the feeling that I jinxed it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless you're Tom Riddle, I'm pretty sure it's just lame circumstances and people deciding of their own free will that I'm personally not worth pursuing. You're not Voldemort, are you?<br /> ....Are you? Couldn't be. Anyway, you're all good, buddy.<br /> <br /> I just have to respect that and move on. Sometimes it can he extremely hard when the rejection is followed by them wanting to be friends. This happened and has before. I'm thinking about it. They're great people. I wouldn't have been so interested if they weren't. I'm just wary of adding yet another person to the list of &quot;friends who I would date, except reality said no&quot;.<br /> That list is getting depressingly long, especially depressing because a huge chunk has already abandoned that &quot;still friends&quot; part. I'm just a guy they used to know.<br /> <br /> So, in a desperate attempt to be safe but still feel like not punching myself to sleep, I tried getting a little sexy on Omegle. Again. Remind me never ever to do that again. Ever. Seriously, just.. fuck.<br /> <br /> I'll do some 'splaining, Lucy:<br /> <br /> I'd medicated and tried to chill. Felt lonely and figured &quot;hey, I have hands. I might be able to go to sleep soon, after all&quot; and prepared to wank. I made the snap decision to maybe find someone to do that with, so I got into my punk rock lingerie (naked but totally wearing a hoodie because comfy), and got on omegle. As some might know, you can get specific there about who you might wanna see/have see you. It's not exactly Chatroulette.<br /> So I type in &quot;Chubby Gay&quot; because that describes my figure, a figure I like on others, and the type of digital fondling I was looking for. Anyone who matched that &quot;Interest&quot; came up. As always, there's a few folks who just click away.<br /> Keep in mind, I'm in mid fap at this juncture. The 