eactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T18:47:30-07:00","id":660209,"title":"","content":"Man, why are people so shitty to each other?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T19:44:24-07:00","id":660236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=660209#post660209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, why are people so shitty to each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes us feel big.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T20:33:04-07:00","id":660273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=660236#post660236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes us feel big.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unfortunately. It's some weird throwback to when the winner of an argument was the one still standing. We can be goddamn cave people sometimes. Funnily enough, a comedian hero of mine once explained that very human way of seeing the world:<br /> &quot;I'm laughing, you're crying. That means I win.&quot;<br /> We're all just trolls waiting to be activated. We need to fight that wiring.<br /> <br /> Now that I'm posting here, I have a genuine question that I forgot to ask but whose subject was discussed here a few pages ago:<br /> <br /> I've seen the terms transgender and transsexual used interchangeably for as long as I've heard the terms. I'm no expert, but that's kinda linguistically imprecise, right? There's also the fact that many people are attracted specifically to transgender people. Wouldn't that be more &quot;transsexual&quot; because it's about actual sexual interest? I'm one of those. A transgender hottie that's showing off their body is sexy to me. It annoys the bleeding fuck outta me that it's treated like a fetish so often.<br /> &quot;What, are you into tranny* porno?&quot; No, fucktard. I'm into the transgender woman or man IN the porno. Why? They, personally, are hot. They're a person, not a fucking strapon or a fleshlight with great abs.<br /> <br /> This is bothering me right now because, among other reasons, one of the girls I'd been talking to and trying my damnedest to get a date with, is trans. I'm not into her just because she's trans. I'm into her because she's a beautiful woman who is funny as fuck. Her being transgender is incidental. Do I find her gender identity kinda sexy? Honestly, yeah. But I like her for HER. Not what she's got going on downstairs.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot even sure if the issue would bother her, but I'm missing her voice and so I am now bitching about a thing because it's better than sitting with my phone in hand hoping she'll call me after I behaved like an idiot and then acted like a depressed mopey cunt. You remember. It was yesterday I think.<br /> <br /> *if anyone was offended by my use of the term &quot;tranny&quot;, me fucking too. I don't want to call people or hear them called something I usually associate with a broken thing I need to fix in my car.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 09-10-2015, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T21:50:48-07:00","id":660344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=660273#post660273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen the terms transgender and transsexual used interchangeably for as long as I've heard the terms. I'm no expert, but that's kinda linguistically imprecise, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are often used interchangeably, but they're not actually interchangeable. It has to do with the fact that people often use the words &quot;gender&quot; and &quot;sex&quot; interchangeably, even though they mean different things. A few pages back I wrote a lengthy post on the difference between sex and gender, and defining transgender as having a gender identity that does not match the gender they were assigned at birth. Transsexual is wanting to change sex - that is to say, the anatomical and/or bio-chemical features related to sexual reproduction. Many transgender people are also transsexual, but there are also many transgender people who are not transsexual, and are comfortable with their bodies exactly as they are. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=660273#post660273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the fact that many people are attracted specifically to transgender people. Wouldn't that be more &quot;transsexual&quot; because it's about actual sexual interest? I'm one of those. A transgender hottie that's showing off their body is sexy to me. It annoys the bleeding fuck outta me that it's treated like a fetish so often.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... If a person, let's say a heterosexual man, is attracted to a trans woman <i>specifically because she is trans</i>, that's what I would call &quot;chaser&quot; behavior. If, on the other hand, he is attracted to a trans women because he's a heterosexual man and she is a woman he finds attractive, that's... Well, that's just run-of-the-mill attraction, nothing wrong with that.<br /> <br /> The thing is, trans women are just as much women as cis women are. Trans men are just as much men as cis men are. Being an object of attraction <i>because</i> you are trans is just as invalidating to a trans person's identity as being an object of disgust because of it. Both come from a place of viewing them in terms of how they are different from other people of their gender. Wether you think it's gross that I have a dick or you think it's super hot, either way you're judging my attractiveness by how I am anatomically different than other women, rather than by who I am as a person of (one of) the gender(s) that you are attracted to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=660273#post660273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;What, are you into tranny porno?&quot; No, fucktard. I'm into the transgender woman or man IN the porno. Why? They, personally, are hot. They're a person, not a fucking strapon or a fleshlight with great abs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's a totally reasonable attitude. You're watching a porno, and you find the person in it attractive. Them being trans or not isn't a deciding factor. There's nothing fetish-y about that at all.<br /> <br /> Of course, the pornography industry has a habit of tailoring content that features trans people to appeal to chasers and fetishists, so like... Even if you personally are not objectifying and fetishizing the model, you still want to be aware of wether or not the porno is portraying him or her in an objectifying or fetishized manner, and try to make good choices with which producers you support. But that's an issue with the industry, not with the people who watch it, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=660273#post660273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is bothering me right now because, among other reasons, one of the girls I'd been talking to and trying my damnedest to get a date with, is trans. I'm not into her just because she's trans. I'm into her because she's a beautiful woman who is funny as fuck. Her being transgender is incidental. Do I find her gender identity kinda sexy? Honestly, yeah. But I like her for HER. Not what she's got going on downstairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say she's a lucky lady. You seem like a decent fellow, you respect her for who she is, and you're attracted to her physically, neither inspite of, nor because of, her gender identity. If more people treated trans people this way, the world would be a better place. Just... Be careful about saying things like &quot;I'm one of those people who is attracted specifically to transgender people&quot; because it makes you <i>sound</i> like a chaser, and a lot of trans people will take a statement like that as a huge red flag.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=660273#post660273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bNot even sure if the issue would bother her, but I'm missing her voice and so I am now bitching about a thing because it's better than sitting with my phone in hand hoping she'll call me after I behaved like an idiot and then acted like a depressed mopey cunt. You remember. It was yesterday I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope things work out for the best. If you ever need any more info about trans stuff, I'd be happy to help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-11-2015, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T22:42:15-07:00","id":660356,"title":"","content":"I completely understand how saying I'm attracted to trans folks of either gender comes off as &quot;chaser&quot; mentality in action. And I agree, it's as objectifying and fetishizing as what I'd previously griped about. I do honestly think that pornography does really play into that sexually and emotionally unhealthy portrayal of ordinary people for their differences.<br /> <br /> I think a better way of articulating my point is saying that, as always, I'm bi/pansexual and I myself am attracted to people regardless of their gender or sex. If I like someone, I like someone. Sexually or not. I just happen to be attracted to, and hopefully still in contact with, a beautiful woman who identifies as trans. I might seem a little eager just because I'm hoping she'll call me.<br /> I'm also just attracted to people being proud of their bodies and celebrating themselves. That's completely separate from the transgender issue, but I'm just noting that to clarify my remark about a &quot;transgender hottie showing off&quot; being about, yes, a hottie. A hottie who is proud of their body, in whatever form that takes. I pictured a very specific person naked when I typed that, so that might've influenced my choice of words. At the same token, I'd have payed good money to watch Moby strip slowly for me at one point (don't judge me. His music calms me, and he has a sweet smile. Fuck you.).<br /> <br /> The chaser thing got me thinking, though; I can't think of something that's my &quot;thing&quot;. Or of a person that's &quot;my type&quot;. Nothing with a running theme. Short, fat, skinny, tall, tattooed, scarred, penis, vagina, glitter wand*, brunette, redhead, bald, furry, spectacles, shades.<br /> <br /> ...huh.<br /> <br /> I think my only deal breakers are social intolerance, being older than my grandparents, disliking marijuana for no reason and really liking The Beatles a lot.<br /> \u200b Otherwise, I'm apparently willing to give love a chance.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, completely random: I like your new signature, Charlaquin. It's informative and strangely comforting.<br /> <br /> *I'd explain further, but you know where that glitter wand went. Just remember, you'd be surprised at the things you can be literally unable to retrieve from your own ass without assistance. Play safe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 09-11-2015, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T23:47:03-07:00","id":660448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=660344#post660344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are often used interchangeably, but they're not actually interchangeable. It has to do with the fact that people often use the words &quot;gender&quot; and &quot;sex&quot; interchangeably, even though they mean different things. A few pages back I wrote a lengthy post on the difference between sex and gender, and defining transgender as having a gender identity that does not match the gender they were assigned at birth. Transsexual is wanting to change sex - that is to say, the anatomical and/or bio-chemical features related to sexual reproduction. Many transgender people are also transsexual, but there are also many transgender people who are not transsexual, and are comfortable with their bodies exactly as they are. [....<br /> <br /> ......] If, on the other hand, he is attracted to a trans women because he's a heterosexual man and she is a woman he finds attractive, that's... Well, that's just run-of-the-mill attraction, nothing wrong with that.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's a totally reasonable attitude. You're watching a porno, and you find the person in it attractive. Them being trans or not isn't a deciding factor. There's nothing fetish-y about that at all.<br /> <br /> I'd say she's a lucky lady. You seem like a decent fellow, you respect her for who she is, and you're attracted to her physically, neither inspite of, nor because of, her gender identity. If more people treated trans people this way, the world would be a better place.<br /> <br /> I hope things work out for the best. If you ever need any more info about trans stuff, I'd be happy to help.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot to say thank you for these parts. Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T07:53:22-07:00","id":660705,"title":"","content":"The 23rd marks the 9 year anniversary of the first time my girlfriend and I went on a date, I'm still trying to process that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T15:46:06-07:00","id":662311,"title":"","content":"Even as a 40 year old no longer living at home, coming out to your parents is scary as hell.<br /> <br /> Whelp, that was my day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod 