edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T15:28:14-07:00","id":676894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=676417#post676417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? Really? This actually exist? Cool! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> too bad I missed it, oh well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Totally a real thing. We'll all plan ahead for next year, okay guys?<br /> We'll throw a little thread-party that gets us all banned for two weeks!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T06:41:37-07:00","id":677575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=676233#post676233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damm, I missed it! I had no idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#800080\">Bisexual Erasure.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T11:20:39-07:00","id":677818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=677575#post677575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Bisexual Erasure.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>This is an actual problem I'd like to discuss here, but I'm having trouble finding the words to start the conversation.<br /> <br /> I know once it gets going I'll have something to say. I just can't figure out how to start the discussion with a decent post.<br /> <br /> <br /> Would anyone else like to try? Seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T12:24:04-07:00","id":677856,"title":"","content":"Well, bisexual people are often seen either as basically gay and unwilling to commit, or as basically straight and trying to get attention. I've often heard sentiments to the effect of &quot;well I think everyone prefers one or the other, some people are just willing to make exceptions when they're in love or horny.&quot; I've also heard both gay and straight people that say that a potential partner identifying as bi is a red flag, because they might just be experimenting and end up leaving for someone of the opposite gender. It seems like non-bi people have a lot of trouble trusting bi people's intentions, always suspicious they might secretly be playing for the other team.<br /> <br /> Despite being openly pansexual, almost everyone I know tends to think of me as straight (or lesbian, if they know I'm trans) because I'm AMAB and my partner is AFAB. Even when they came out as bigender, they got so many people saying &quot;does [charlaquin] know? How does he feel about it? Are you two still going to stay together? Won't that be hard for him?&quot; Now, the last thing I want to do in a conversation about bi erasure is contribute to bi erasure myself, so I feel it's important to point out that pan and bi are not the same thing, and I don't claim to have faced the same struggles. I just wanted to provide an example of a personal experience with similar attitudes of &quot;you can only have one favorite&quot; in hopes of helping kickstart the conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-25-2015, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T13:10:34-07:00","id":677910,"title":"","content":"I identify as bi-sexual, but whenever I talk about it, I either get told that I'm just horny, that it's just a phase, or (when they talk to me a little more) that I should really identify as pan-sexual.<br /> <br /> I've been told that the difference lies in the wonderful arch-nemesis of the LGBT community: gender binary.<br /> <br /> I'm being told that since I'm Bi, I must be transphobic or queer-phobic. And I think that's where the problem lies. Maybe I just call myself Bi because I didn't heard Pan beforehand? Maybe I like my partner to be cis-gendered? Maybe I'm just putting a very broad label on myself without caring for the actual semantic of things?<br /> <br /> Charlaquin said something important:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just wanted to provide an example of a personal experience with similar attitudes of &quot;you can only have one favorite&quot; in hopes of helping kickstart the conversation. </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'll admit it, I have a preference for girls. So what? I thought sexuality was a beautiful spectrum. That's what every LGBT representative tells me every time I talk about the subject. So why can't I be 60-40 in my desires?<br /> <br /> It reminds me of the Video Gaming community. &quot;You ain't a <i>REAL</i> gamer!&quot; I feel like I ain't a &quot;real&quot; member of the LGBT.<br /> <br /> Tl;Dr: Bisexual with a preference for girls, get treated as straight scum by local LGBT community.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Am I the only one thinking it's funny how LGBT stands for Lesbian Gay <b>Bi</b> &amp; Trans?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":2589,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","user":"Magnum Opus","date":". 09-25-2015, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T14:05:11-07:00","id":677980,"title":"","content":"M.O. made some very valid points about having specific preference, the spectrum of attraction and especially about the Bi label.<br /> <br /> Char, I I think you kinda hit the nail on the head with your thoughts on relationship hurdles for bisexual people. There are a lot of instances where people just assume that, for one reason or another, being bisexual means being unsure or unreliable...like it's an indecisive state instead of an sexual identity. I myself, if I'm being inclusive and not too lazy to explain pansexuality to someone, really identify as pan. The simple reason has been previously stated; the damned gender binary. &quot;I like women AND men&quot; is just SO much easier to explain than &quot;I'm sexually attracted to people regardless of sex or gender. Really, it's more about the feelings they evoke in me upon meeting and their personalities. Genitalia in general looks weird, anyway. I just feel love for a person sometimes. Have I overshared?&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think I do have phases where my attraction to a specific type of person gets more focused, but it's usually when I'm attracted to a person and that type matches them. First I like the person, and then I start the process of going &quot;ok, so I guess THESE are my favorite parts of you, if I'm going to objectify you playfully and pick some pieces&quot;. I go through phases where goth girls are the sexiest thing ever, and times when chubby or nerdy guys in glasses drive me nutter-butters, but it's nearly always when it's actually a single person I like and my brain's just decided to let me enjoy their traits in others.<br /> <br /> As for being marginalized personally, it happens so often it's almost routine. I've come out as bi to my mom. It's been years now. She still just treats me as straight, asks about girls I've talked to and goes silent when I mention guys. My sister understands, because she's also pansexual, and in a healthy heterosexual relationship where her partner actually knows and accepts her sexuality. My dad doesn't know I'm in any way less than straight. He wouldn't understand and I don't talk to him enough to bother trying to explain it. My grandmother is a weird mix of my mom and my sister in her reaction; she goes on about grandchildren and me getting &quot;some ladies&quot; (yeah, quotations. That lady seriously tells me I should go get laid...like, a lot. Far too much for a grandmother that isn't getting a cut of a dowry) but then will just happily hug me and wish me luck in love and tell me &quot;any Man would be lucky to have you. Or a lady, if you feel like it.&quot; Funny old hippie. Gotta love her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 09-25-2015, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T16:16:24-07:00","id":678186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=677910#post677910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I identify as bi-sexual, but whenever I talk about it, I either get told that I'm just horny, that it's just a phase, or (when they talk to me a little more) that I should really identify as pan-sexual.<br /> <br /> I've been told that the difference lies in the wonderful arch-nemesis of the LGBT community: gender binary.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually something that frustrates the hell out of me. Nobody has any business telling you what you &quot;should&quot; identify as but you. Trying to say &quot;well the way you describe it makes it sound like you're actually pan&quot; destroys bi identity. In my opinion, if you say that you're bi, that's what you are, there shouldn't be a question about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=677910#post677910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm being told that since I'm Bi, I must be transphobic or queer-phobic. And I think that's where the problem lies. Maybe I just call myself Bi because I didn't heard Pan beforehand? Maybe I like my partner to be cis-gendered? Maybe I'm just putting a very broad label on myself without caring for the actual semantic of things?</div> </div> </div> </div>I made a comment on this myself a little ways up thread. The argument that identifying as bisexual inherently makes you transphobic or queer-phobic is ridiculously pedantic. Now, personally I chose to use the term pan because I prefer the implied inclusivity of the language, but I wouldn't assume that just because someone prefers the term bi that they <i>don't</i> include non-binary genders among the people they find attractive. Maybe they just prefer the way the word sounds, or maybe they say bi because they don't feel like explaining what pan means all the time, or maybe they like their men masculine and their women feminine, wether they are cis, trans, or otherwise, and they feel that bi gets that idea across better than pan does. The terms we use have a lot of different meanings to a lot of different people, and it's honestly ridiculous to blame bisexual people for a fault in the language.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=677910#post677910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charlaquin said something important:<br /> <br /> Ok, I'll admit it, I have a preference for girls. So what? I thought sexuality was a beautiful spectrum. That's what every LGBT representative tells me every time I talk about the subject. So why can't I be 60-40 in my desires?<br /> <br /> It reminds me of the Video Gaming community. &quot;You ain't a <i>REAL</i> gamer!&quot; I feel like I ain't a &quot;real&quot; member of the LGBT.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should clarify, I did not mean to suggest that there is anything wrong with having a preference, or that having a preference somehow makes you somehow &quot;less bi&quot;. In fact, I also have a preference for femininity (in men and women). I sincerely apologize if my phrasing made it sound as though I was marginalizing those who have a preference. What I meant to express was that, in my experience, many people would assume that since you have a preference for women, you must be straight if you are a man, or lesbian if you are a woman. And that is a frustrating to have to deal with. It's one of the big issues with bi erasure, because it's very difficult to be perceived as &quot;really bi&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=677910#post677910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tl;Dr: Bisexual with a preference for girls, get treated as straight scum by local LGBT community.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, I'm sorry you've had to go through that. Our community still has a lot of growing to do just in terms of accepting <i>each other</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=677910#post677910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Am I the only one thinking it's funny how LGBT stands for Lesbian Gay <b>Bi</b> &amp; Trans?</div> </div> </div> </div>So... Unpopular opinion time... The LGBT community sometimes gets way too hung up on the language we use. Yes, words are important and it's good to be able to accurately express the way we feel with the terms we use to identify ourselves. But I just have to roll my eyes when people try say bisexuality is transphobic, or that the acronym needs to include however many more letters, or that if you feel a certain way you should be using this term and not this one. Honestly, I find the difference between bi and pan to be extremely academic, and maybe that's problematic of me, but I really do think a lot of the time the difference comes down to nothing more than <i>what we think sounds better</i>. I acknowledge and respect that we face very different struggles simply by virtue of the words we choose; &quot;bi&quot; as a term has completely different stigmas attatched to it than the term &quot;pan&quot; does. But at the same time, if someone who identified as bi described to me the way they feel and it turned out to be identical to my own feelings? I still would not question that they are bi, and I would thank them not to question that I am pan, because we choose those terms for reasons that are very personal to us, and trying to tell someone that their identity is wrong is insulting and counter-productive.<br /> <br /> EDIT: sorry for the typos, I'm on mobile which always messes me up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-25-2015, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T18:31:00-07:00","id":678390,"title":"","content":"I find this to be relevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K1xnnY7oKtI\" data-code=\"K1xnnY7oKtI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/K1xnnY7oKtI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T18:38:46-07:00","id":678391,"title":"","content":"Gay man here, sending my love and acceptance to all you Bi folks out there!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T20:07:39-07:00","id":678439,"title":"","content":"Bisexual guy here. Thought I'd introduce myself.<br /> <br /> I'd like to hand it to Onyx Path/White Wolf for making sexuality such a non-issue with their games. I love how I can have queer people in Exalted and most people are totally cool with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T21:28:55-07:00","id":678487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=678439#post678439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bisexual guy here. Thought I'd introduce myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Happy to meet you - from the Bi Bear Nerd. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=678439#post678439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to hand it to Onyx Path/White Wolf for making sexuality such a non-issue with their games. I love how I can have queer people in Exalted and most people are totally cool with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should see New World of Darkness - I was really pleased to read about in the <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b> 2ED example of Touchstone for gay cop werewolf as his boyfriend that he would want to be more in his life, but knows his life as Uratha will endanger him. Or that in <b>Beast: The Primordial </b>is character idea of &quot;IT manager by day, Drag King by night&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T02:13:17-07:00","id":678646,"title":"","content":"Yea WW tends to be pretty queer friendly with all their properties.<br /> <br /> I am still not sure why the distrust of bisexuality is still a thing. Other than the fact people can be close minded about others easily, it is odd that there is so much misunderstanding. I have several bisexual players, and no two are quite alike with it, so that is a thing I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-27T12:10:02-07:00","id":680241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=678646#post678646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea WW tends to be pretty queer friendly with all their properties.<br /> <br /> I am still not sure why the distrust of bisexuality is still a thing. Other than the fact people can be close minded about others easily, it is odd that there is so much misunderstanding. I have several bisexual players, and no two are quite alike with it, so that is a thing I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gay people have placed a lot of stock in the fact that they are attracted to their own sex. It's what makes them different than straight people, and it forms a core of their identity. But it requires that sexuality be a dichotomy. Us bi people reject this dichotomy with our very existence. As such, some gay people get incredibly defensive and accuse us of basically being &quot;not gay enough&quot; or &quot;just gay people who are giving into homophobia&quot; (people really like being patronizingly condescending to whom they look down on).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T01:18:50-07:00","id":680754,"title":"","content":"Im bi. As I like to to say to people when I feel like joking &quot;I really like women, but sometimes you need a bit of cock in you, you know?&quot;.<br /> <br /> More seriously, I can be attracted to a lot of sex and gender variations. I've dated / been attracted to trans girls, cis guys and girls, and genderfluid people, and I've had a blast each time. I still identify as bi rather than pan though. And I feel like it's important, because in a way, I think the label &quot;bi&quot; is actually sometimes more including than &quot;pan&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;But Tipex&quot; you're going to say &quot;don't you know that by saying you're bi, you're contributing to trans opression, and saying that you'd never date a trans person?&quot;<br /> <br /> To which I'd respond :<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, person I just invented in my head, no, not really. If I were straight, for exemple, and only dated women, I'd date both cis women and trans women. Since I say I'm bi, I tend to date both men and women... As in, both cis and trans men and women. Granted, that tends to leave out people who walk the spectrum between that, but to me, saying you're pan and not bi because you date both trans and cis people is weird too, because it hints that you'd consider trans people to... not be completely their choosen gender, somehow.<br /> <br /> If you really want to find an issue in how people express their choosen sexuality, both terms can be interpreted as problematic : bi tends to leave out intersex and genderqueer people, pan tends to create an unecessary distinction between cis and trans. That's the way I see it, anyway. So I indentify as bi, but I'd date pretty much anyone I happen to like, no matter their sex and/or gender.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for my interaction with the rest of the LGTB community... I rarely had a problem. It helps that a lot of my LGTB friends are more interested in debate than in being defensive. (Granted, the debates can get pretty heated at times, but more in the &quot;I need to bake apology cakes now&quot; heated than &quot;I need to cut that person out of my life now&quot; heated.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":541,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","user":"LeTipex","date":". 09-28-2015, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T06:49:36-07:00","id":680964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=677856#post677856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, bisexual people are often seen either as basically gay and unwilling to commit, or as basically straight and trying to get attention. I've often heard sentiments to the effect of &quot;well I think everyone prefers one or the other, some people are just willing to make exceptions when they're in love or horny.&quot; I've also heard both gay and straight people that say that a potential partner identifying as bi is a red flag, because they might just be experimenting and end up leaving for someone of the opposite gender. It seems like non-bi people have a lot of trouble trusting bi people's intentions, always suspicious they might secretly be playing for the other team.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are also people who are worried you'll get bored with their sex organs and eventually need a different set to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T07:58:44-07:00","id":680982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=680964#post680964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are also people who are worried you'll get bored with their sex organs and eventually need a different set to play with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could it be that people believe Bi want <i>both</i> while Pan wants <i>the right one</i>? Could it be as simple as that?<br /> <br /> Let me explain a little: Since Pan is described as &quot;loving for the person no matter their gender/sex&quot; and Bi is &quot;loving <i>both</i> men and women&quot;, maybe people are subconsciously thinking that Bi will <i>need</i> both rather than only one, whereas Pan simply looks for the right person.<br /> <br /> Does this make sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T08:41:06-07:00","id":681034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=680982#post680982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could it be that people believe Bi want <i>both</i> while Pan wants <i>the right one</i>? Could it be as simple as that?<br /> <br /> Let me explain a little: Since Pan is described as &quot;loving for the person no matter their gender/sex&quot; and Bi is &quot;loving <i>both</i> men and women&quot;, maybe people are subconsciously thinking that Bi will <i>need</i> both rather than only one, whereas Pan simply looks for the right person.<br /> <br /> Does this make sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely what conservative talk radio hosts think &quot;bisexual&quot; means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T09:03:41-07:00","id":681044,"title":"","content":"Well, from watching <b>Doctor Who</b> franchise and it's Captian Jack Harkness, I always thought that Pansexual ( or Omnisexual ) could - theoretical - sleep with everything humanoid. Human, alien, robot - only if they &quot;like it&quot; they can sex it. Just see Captain Jack. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=v2KuwlMiYj0\" data-code=\"v2KuwlMiYj0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/v2KuwlMiYj0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> And Bisex just sleep with human. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T09:08:00-07:00","id":681045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=681044#post681044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, from watching <b>Doctor Who</b> franchise and it's Captian Jack Harkness, I always thought that Pansexual ( or Omnisexual ) could - theoretical - sleep with everything humanoid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I once had a roommate we jokingly called an &quot;Aspiring Omnisexual&quot;. We were pretty sure he'd fuck a couch if the couch could consent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Jo