nk-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T11:46:50-07:00","id":681275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=680982#post680982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could it be that people believe Bi want <i>both</i> while Pan wants <i>the right one</i>? Could it be as simple as that?<br /> <br /> Let me explain a little: Since Pan is described as &amp;quot;loving for the person no matter their gender/sex&amp;quot; and Bi is &amp;quot;loving <i>both</i> men and women&amp;quot;, maybe people are subconsciously thinking that Bi will <i>need</i> both rather than only one, whereas Pan simply looks for the right person.<br /> <br /> Does this make sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely a misconception that exists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=681044#post681044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, from watching <b>Doctor Who</b> franchise and it's Captian Jack Harkness, I always thought that Pansexual ( or Omnisexual ) could - theoretical - sleep with everything humanoid. Human, alien, robot - only if they &amp;quot;like it&amp;quot; they can sex it. Just see Captain Jack. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And Bisex just sleep with human. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And this is another one (hence one of the cases of two names that mean basically the same thing coming attached with very different stigmas). The &quot;will fuck anything and everything&quot; stereotype of pansexuals has some really negative implications, and is always used to play pansexual characters for laughs.<br /> <br /> Personally, the reason I prefer the term pan is because I have certain qualities that I find attractive, and I find them attractive in people of all genders. I would use bi if I had different preferences in partners of different genders, like my earlier example of someone liking masculine men and feminine women.<br /> <br /> Again though, that's just what pan vs. bi means to me. I'm sure they have different meanings to others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T08:03:26-07:00","id":682069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong