um/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T18:31:09-07:00","id":713373,"title":"","content":"I mentioned before that I have this crush on this one guy at my school. I see him almost every Monday and Wednesday. Unfortunately I haven't approached him because I am unsure if he's gay or bi and I don't want to make him uncomfortable or make things awkward for both of us. I have no problem approaching guys who are gay/bi but it is kind of difficult when trying to figure out masculine guys who might be gay/bi. This guy plays football, not for the school but for a class. I'm guessing he likes football, of course. Anyways, he looks like a really cute cub, as in a bear (my opinion). Yeah, that's my type, though I admit I'm one myself. And then something extraordinary happen today. I was on the bus going to school with the guy I have a crush on when I noticed a lot of guys who look like bears on the bus. I was like...what the fuck! *Sigh* I wish it was easier and more open to tell if a masculine guy is gay/bi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2360,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","user":"Cecoyotl","date":". 10-21-2015, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T01:37:31-08:00","id":781011,"title":"","content":"Apparently before I was given a chance to defend my position the thread was locked with the snide insinuation that I was defending bigoted statements, and told to go post in this thread.<br /> <br /> Sure. Why not.<br /> <br /> Here is the post I had compiled before the threadlock:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/779385-sjw-sidebars-in-ex3-or-sjws-ate-my-corebook?p=780973#post780973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check the link. I did NOT take that line out of context at all. Kyeudo said that people who identify as LGBT are outside the norm and are comparable to mental illness.<br /> <br /> Then later he said that he likes MLK's view of equality, and he said to me that he was trying to show that his side of the debate are more than just hateful bigots.<br /> <br /> While having equated LGBT people to having a mental illness.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I think that the mods were MORE than justified in banning Kyeudo, since what he said there was SO far out of line. He was not presenting any reasonable discourse, he was not listening to points raised at him without raising his deflector shield. If you want me to dig up the post he made equating homosexuals to people who cut themselves by using &quot;Spiritual Self-Harm&quot;, I fully can. My point is that yeah, there's a danger of some people on Tumblr being fuckwits and idiots, but you do <i>not</i> want to throw in with Kyeudo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for that. Following the chain of quotes and comments back, it seems that the origin of the chain started when Segev asked (paraphrased): &quot;If you identify as no gender, why do you care if you're gendered?&quot; To which Eurhetemec replied (quoted): &quot;This is the end of rational discussion, isn't it? You're essentially labeling this a mental illness. Welcome to 1950 or even 1890, I guess.&quot; After which Kyeudo gave the quote you provided.<br /> <br /> In my judgement, Segev asked a question (perhaps more aggressively than need be) relating to the dynamics of gender politics, to which Eurhetemec responded by (perhaps more aggressively than need be) pointing out that the nature of the question bore similarities to attitudes back in the 1890s-1950s, to which Kyeudo responded by pointing out (perhaps less elegantly than it could have been) that back in those ye olden days, basically anything outside the norm was considered a mental illness.<br /> <br /> I try to look at what I feel is the intent behind the statement, as well as the statement itself. So I am inclined to give all the people involved in that chain the benefit of the doubt and say that the emotionally charged nature of the discussion polluted the intention and prevented an interesting conversation from happening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/779385-sjw-sidebars-in-ex3-or-sjws-ate-my-corebook?p=780985#post780985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For another stance that was objected to, see also:<br /> <br /> &quot;Just because my beliefs aren't provable doesn't mean I shouldn't try to force them on others 'for their own good'.&quot; Great, we're back to a few steps away from 'tortured into conversion'; what's a finite period of agony in exchange for the hypothetical salvation of your hypothetically eternal soul, assuming the Mormons are the ones who are right and not the Egyptians, the Greeks, the Hindu, the Buddhists, the Jehovah's Witnesses, the Pastafarians...[edit] Oh, the Norse, forgot the Norse. I bet they're the ones who are secretly right, Valhalla sounds frickin' awesome.<br /> And of course, again, equating 'I love this person' with 'I have an uncontrollable psychological compulsion to consume in excess and then purge it from my system'. But only if the love is two of the same sex, two opposite sex people who love each other are never under any suspicion of suffering from any mental disorder as a result, nope nope.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... honestly don't know what to make of that quote. The bulimic metaphor is lost on me completely, and the whole spiritual injury thing is just nonsensical. I feel like there might be some greater context I'm missing, but I can't find it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TavelGorge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/779385-sjw-sidebars-in-ex3-or-sjws-ate-my-corebook?p=780990#post780990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well said, Im sure now that JayTee has had a chance to catch up on this forums recent events that they know to tread lightly unless they are going to provide an appropriate opinion. The consequences are clear otherwise.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no! Please don't judge me, random internet stranger who until this point I have never even conversed with! I would hate for you and all the other people who I have never met and will likely never form any meaningful relationships with to look down on me! Is there any way I can earn my way back in to your good graces? Do I need to do a little dance? Sing a little song? Get down tonight? I'm ever so sorry that I may have tread harder than I should have! Do I need to wear loafers? Or maybe cashmere slippers? I can get them, I promise! Please don't be mad at me!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/779385-sjw-sidebars-in-ex3-or-sjws-ate-my-corebook?p=780994#post780994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They said that homosexuality was sinful. This is <i>wrong</i>. As in, it is factually incorrect; it is untrue. It is a hurtful untruth that insults countless people (including many users on this forum) to no purpose. And as I said above, I do not accept that it is merely an innocent error; in the modern world, with many, many people they could easily interact with to learn that it is wrong, holding on to that belief requires a deliberate and knowing commitment to hurting others through their willful rejection of reality. Maybe they continue to hold on to it because it feels good, on some level, or because they can't handle the cognitive dissonance that would come from challenging it at this point; I don't really care. The end result is the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>No arguments here. If you can provide a direct quote, that would be a pretty damning piece of evidence whoever said it and would be grounds for my withdrawal of support for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> The rest of your post had me confused because I couldn't tell if you were agreeing with me or arguing against me, considering how you've vocalized positions that I've always had but have never been able to put to words accurately.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Chist, I came at this from an admitted position of ignorance and a willingness to learn and be proven wrong, and I get one edgelord straw-manning me and an internet tough guy threatening me with the invisible glower of dozens of anonymous role-players. If this is how you guys inform someone seeking to enlighten himself, don't ever become teachers. You'll probably send the quality of education back to the stoneage.<br /> <br /> Discuss this at your own leisure, or don't. I don't care anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T02:05:08-08:00","id":781027,"title":"","content":"Edit: Never mind, I thought I was discussing why the actions were offensive in order to explain to him, but that's too close to discussing bannees, so removing it completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 12-06-2015, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T02:10:39-08:00","id":781032,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Posting about LGBT stuff is welcome here, But do not discuss bannees. Period. Stop this line of discussion. </span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T02:42:15-08:00","id":781045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=677856#post677856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, bisexual people are often seen either as basically gay and unwilling to commit, or as basically straight and trying to get attention. I've often heard sentiments to the effect of &quot;well I think everyone prefers one or the other, some people are just willing to make exceptions when they're in love or horny.&quot; I've also heard both gay and straight people that say that a potential partner identifying as bi is a red flag, because they might just be experimenting and end up leaving for someone of the opposite gender. It seems like non-bi people have a lot of trouble trusting bi people's intentions, always suspicious they might secretly be playing for the other team.<br /> <br /> Despite being openly pansexual, almost everyone I know tends to think of me as straight (or lesbian, if they know I'm trans) because I'm AMAB and my partner is AFAB. Even when they came out as bigender, they got so many people saying &quot;does [charlaquin] know? How does he feel about it? Are you two still going to stay together? Won't that be hard for him?&quot; Now, the last thing I want to do in a conversation about bi erasure is contribute to bi erasure myself, so I feel it's important to point out that pan and bi are not the same thing, and I don't claim to have faced the same struggles. I just wanted to provide an example of a personal experience with similar attitudes of &quot;you can only have one favorite&quot; in hopes of helping kickstart the conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The second part is a huge thing, based on my observations. If you're in a monogamous relationship with someone, you obviously only are into people of that gender... it's like other preferences that also are there are Shcrodinger's Cat and disappear as soon as they aren't seen.<br /> <br /> Sexuality is way more complex than a binary option, or even a spectrum. I'm a trans lesbian, but I'm also demisexual and yet find I can form romantic relationships with people of any gender identity. I sometimes feel like the language has been lagging as part of a social... resistance to change. Not active so much as &quot;But change is scary!&quot; in the same way people don't want to switch to the Metric system.<br /> <br /> On a completely separate topic, were you ever into Exalted? I knew someone seemingly FOREVER ago who was and went by that nickname.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T03:34:06-08:00","id":781057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=781045#post781045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second part is a huge thing, based on my observations. If you're in a monogamous relationship with someone, you obviously only are into people of that gender... it's like other preferences that also are there are Shcrodinger's Cat and disappear as soon as they aren't seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well shit, better tell my bisexual fiance that apparently she's actually straight, and the discussions we've had about wanting to do fun things to various women we see pictures of online are clearly the result of some kind of delusion of hers.<br /> <br /> (I personally would say I'm straight, but I've had the VERY occasional moment of &quot;I'd consider trying the other team for him&quot;. And they're for guys SO far out of my league it's not even funny. So like... 99.9% straight?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T03:50:06-08:00","id":781059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=781057#post781057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well shit, better tell my bisexual fiance that apparently she's actually straight, and the discussions we've had about wanting to do fun things to various women we see pictures of online are clearly the result of 