0bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T22:56:39-08:00","id":781570,"title":"","content":"My wife has been most displeased with one of our cats, for the wrecking of the Christmas tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T01:34:08-08:00","id":781606,"title":"","content":"My girlfriend and I have a cat. Her name is Rose, and she's huge. I mean, 21+ pounds, bigger than some small dogs, and strong enough to actually break open weak cat carriers from the inside huge.<br /> <br /> She's also a giant sweetheart, comes when my girlfriend calls her, and when she rolls over for belly rubs, she'll just let you ruffle away without objecting, and will even start purring. We joke that she sometimes acts more like a dog than a typical cat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T01:51:58-08:00","id":781609,"title":"","content":"Well, I did have a cat as a kid. He was huge, like 17 pounds half Siamese... all muscle. Would leap from the floor up to the top of the door and perch along it between door and celing. Also notorious for stealing food... one time, he was sitting on my mom's shoulder, he'd do this at the breakfast nook to look out the window, and she had been eating breakfast... suddenly, as she brings a spoon of cereal towards her face, his head darts out trying to steal milk and cereal. He was the best... contrasted with the cat my uncle had. Only would be nice to him and myself... oh, she'd purr and rub up against your leg, but it was just to try and get your hand and/or face within claw range.<br /> <br /> I learned metalworking art from a guy in my home town, and his cat loved to have the shop vac used on it. Would flop over for belly rubs with that running (so you'd vacuum it's side and belly).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T10:07:24-08:00","id":781739,"title":"","content":"I have a gecko. It's name is Doctor Alphys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T10:10:45-08:00","id":781741,"title":"","content":"We have 3 cats. They spend the whole days sleeping, purring and moving slowly around the house. Until we go to bed, where they start doing speed races around the whole place, moving things around and doing noise like crazy... and when we get up to see what's going on, they're all on the couch, &quot;sleeping&quot;, looking at us like nothing happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T13:20:53-08:00","id":781818,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to arbitrarily call one of my two cats a pansexual with intimacy issues to nudge us back on topic. In other, non pet related, my most serious ex (gender fluid, mostly. Identifies herself sexualiy as bi) has randomly begun to message and call me, in an emotionally needy remember-how!happy-we-were kind of way. I'm not sure how to feel at all. On one side, I'm enjoying the attention and the familiarity. As a couple, we fit like psychosexual Lego pieces. On the other side, I've dated and been dumped by her twice. I've also dated and dumped HER once. So.... no freaking clue what I'm doing here. <br /> <br /> My struggling libido is reminding me of nothing but great experiences (she's work the pants in the relationship, in many ways, from time to time. I'll leave that open to interpretation, because you're probably right no matter WHAT you imagined).<br /> <br /> The rest of me is confused as fuck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T13:52:34-08:00","id":781826,"title":"","content":"This may or may not be any help, AF, but I figured I would toss it out.<br /> <br /> So, you two broke up 3 times. Can you look it what went wrong each time and find a solid reason why the breakups occurred, and then see how likely it is to happen again? If it happened multiple times because someone cute came by, well there is likely to be a problem this time too. If it was not listening, or drinking, or drugs that gives you something to watch for. Take into account your ages at the time too (if you both had -teen in your age I would not worry too much)<br /> <br /> Second, She is approaching in an emotionally needy way, according to your words. Do you have the emotional fortitude to care for her? Does she for you? How does this interact with your emotional issues?<br /> <br /> Third, if looking at a possible future with her, what do you two like to do together not involving fucking? There is nothing wrong with &quot;we like to fuck and watch TV together,&quot; but I see those break up more than &quot;We both like hikiing/gaming/tae kwn do/classic cars/beach trips&quot; My wife and I, for example, both like gaming, like similar music, both like similar video games, have similar ideas about spending and travel, similar but not identical political beliefs, etc.<br /> <br /> If you both need someone to talk to and you need some lovin', is a friends-with-benefits something that could be on the table? Are YOU capable of this arrangement? Is she? Depending on how you feel about sex, FwB can be a helpful step between &quot;I like her a lot, we talk and want to sleep together&quot; and &quot;I want this person as my partner in this life.&quot; I know I have sexual chemistry with more people than I would make a good wife for, not everyone is equipped to handle my anxiety issues, for one. But some people (and nothing wrong with it) can't let it stay at that. If Jealousy will be an issue, put FwB down and walk away quickly. Alternately, if it sounds good, is a poly arrangement something that may work (this can help if you have uneven sex drives, or you two both fall in love easily. Again, Jealousy is the monster to watch).<br /> <br /> So, you know what went wrong, You think you can handle her and she can help you, You have clothed activities in common, you want it to be more serious than FwB and you back away slowly from Poly (or not!!). Last step is can you communicate your interests and and concerns, and can she back. Should you ask her to ask herself any of these questions? How well you know her could be a thing here.<br /> <br /> Then, if you want to try, keep communication open, and good luck. If you want to have fun, have fun. And if you need to walk away, walk away. A sexy adventure can be fun, I recommend them to a lot of people, but know what you are getting into. Have your eyes open.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T16:26:07-08:00","id":781928,"title":"","content":"I'm going to agree on these things as well as add that if you are interested in ANY sort of future (even just the carnal kind) you probably should try and meet and communicate with those OFF the table. Try and see how they've changed (and let them see the same with you). Based on when I've seen others do this, it feels like breakups in weirdly because the people HAVE changed, but had expected they were more getting into a relationship with someone who was the same person they broke up with before. The same things that can make it work THIS TIME are the same things can can make it fail.<br /> <br /> But overall, I think you have to most of all keep attention to your own reactions to things... the visceral instant ones before your brain can change the context on you. And even if there are bumps, communication can deal with those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T23:04:03-08:00","id":782095,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Baroness. You too, haren.<br /> I considered responding to your statements and queries in exact order, but this is emotionally complicated and I'm going to try to be honest and as unbiased as I can, so my typical rambling style will have to suffice:<br /> <br /> I've known her for years, though I'll preface any further explanation with the fact that our relationship in every stage has been long-distance. If that makes this issue seem less than serious to you, I don't know what to say beyond that having the option for physical intimacy would be great. I just don't have that.<br /> <br /> We became friends online originally, meeting in a chat room for clean fantasy role playing that was owned by an online acquaintance of mine. We had and have a lot in common in how we view the world, and things in general. We appreciate most of the same things. We can talk for hours or just turn on a Skype call with video and be silent with each other, just shooting smiles and laying about with music on. Hell, we've slept like that on occasion, accidentally dozing with laptops next to our beds. Sometimes we did it intentionally as comfort, to know the other was there as we slept.<br /> <br /> Our break ups always seemed nebulous. Out of the three, the last being when I myself left her, she only sought new romantic companionship after the last. Each break up before just seemed to stem from her deciding she wasn't &quot;meant to be loved&quot;, or wasn't &quot;ready&quot;. Ready for what, that remained a question. We were emotionally intimate and open with others about our relationship to the extreme. We knew each other's mothers (both closer to our mothers) on a casual first name and affectionate &quot;mom&quot; basis.<br /> Our hobbies are dissimilar, but not completely. We both love gaming, but completely different kinds of games. We'll spend six hours straight working on some homemade game stuff, but mine will be pnp fluff and crunch. She'll have built a labyrinth filled with zombies as a moat of undead nightmares to surround her impressive Minecraft castle. Just different that way.<br /> <br /> As for polyamory; as strange as it sounds knowing this is long-distance, we've tried it. Early on, in fact. Our first run as a thing included a mutual friend as our co-girlfriend. This was group calls with intimate activities and the like, but also a genuine try at an open relationship where we could be emotionally intimate as well. That didn't last, as the third party participated in some serious emotional and physical infidelity. My ex and I found we were actually happier as a two-some, though, and continued on for over a year after.<br /> <br /> She and I have discussed a genuine future together every time we've been together officially. She wants children, and someone to be her equal and partner. She really believes in love, from what I've observed and everything we've talked about over the years. In those respects, we're nearly identical.<br /> I've always wanted to be a dad. Really, it almost overshadows my desire to procreate. I mean, sex is awesome. Haven't had it in years, but I 'member. I just don't really care about a child being raised by me carrying my DNA. I'm not emotionally attached to my genetic material.<br /> <br /> In regards to emotional issues, we both have them. They're not the same by far, but it's almost been a boon to us during some of our harder personal times, when nobody else understood. Granted, those issues stem from the same places that the bad decisions and breakups might have come from. I honestly don't know. If I did, I can't say she wouldn't take my hand and want to confront them together. ...We're alike in how we see ourselves, and that can be the pit that we fall into.. She can't see that she's a good and loveable person. I've been told I'm the same. I'm dealing with that in my way. I just don't know if making the attempt at a relationship won't show me that it's just her own issues, or (if I'm going to be selfish here) that she doesn't want ME. Just someone like me.<br /> <br /> \u200b...my brain is quoting the Litany Against Fear from Dune, now, so I'll just call this a good place to stop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 12-08-2015, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T01:01:22-08:00","id":782137,"title":"","content":"I don't see the long distance as making it less real. Depending on the people, it might be more real in some ways. I've known people more than happy to act more like themself, if one without some of the anxieties and worries of in person interaction and that can lead to enhanced honesty and communication, which it sounds like you had well in hand.<br /> <br /> My thoughts are then... it sounds like most of the breakups were due to personal emotional issues leading to... I'm not sure, but a breakup. It's more about the self than the relationship itself (from what I'm reading from this)... <br /> <br /> Based on people I've known, they've broken up with people for those sorts of fuzzy reasons because deep down they felt they were going to screw it up irrepairably and better to break things off for the moment rather than lose something precious forever. Is that the case here? No clue. I am absolutely awful at my own relationships, but have a talent for reading people... as long as it has nothing to do with potential attraction to myself. But this is still at best somewhat experienced speculation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T02:38:04-08:00","id":782167,"title":"","content":"It's not my place comment, really. I've given you hopefully some diagnostic tools. I hope the decisions are sound.<br /> <br /> As for long distance, it can work. it works best when there is an ultimate plan for how to get to the same place, but even that is not necessarily required if temperaments are right. They do have a higher fail rate, but it can still work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T09:14:51-08:00","id":782332,"title":"","content":"Most* long distance relationships work out when there is an end goal of ending the long distance part of the relationship and living in the same home/city. It could be when a partner is done with their degree program ends or when the relationship has grown enough for one or both parties to feel comfortable enough to leave their life in one city to start a new life with their romantic partner.<br /> <br /> Is that possible between the two of you? It doesn't happen have to for years, but it is something that needs to be brought up.<br /> <br /> *There is always exceptions to everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T09:33:42-08:00","id":782347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=782332#post782332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most* long distance relationships work out when there is an end goal of ending the long distance part of the relationship and living in the same home/city. It could be when a partner is done with their degree program ends or when the relationship has grown enough for one or both parties to feel comfortable enough to leave their life in one city to start a new life with their romantic partner.<br /> <br /> Is that possible between the two of you? It doesn't happen have to for years, but it is something that needs to be brought up.<br /> <br /> *There is always exceptions to everything.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At the moment, it's mostly her being stuck in her hometown that's a major roadblock. If she could move with some assured security, she'd be happy to live with me. I'm planning to move to Oregon to further my comedy career on mostly saved cash and wishes, and she's borderline broke in the Midwest. Living with parents until she's financially stable. My hope is that, after getting the day job I'll need to stay afloat between gigs, I can move her out to Portland. It's the uncertainty about how things would go that gets her. Without relieving some of that uncertainty, I dunno....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T09:41:25-08:00","id":782353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=782347#post782347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> At the moment, it's mostly her being stuck in her hometown that's a major roadblock. If she could move with some assured security, she'd be happy to live with me. I'm planning to move to Oregon to further my comedy career on mostly saved cash and wishes, and she's borderline broke in the Midwest. Living with parents until she's financially stable. My hope is that, after getting the day job I'll need to stay afloat between gigs, I can move her out to Portland. It's the uncertainty about how things would go that gets her. Without relieving some of that uncertainty, I dunno....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This may be a case of &quot;Two ships passing in the night.&quot; You and your friend seem to be compatible, but all those logistical things that romantic comedies don't talk about, like money and life goals and plans, about come between you two.<br /> <br /> A potential relationship may work out, because Love and a Strong Will can make anything work out. However, it isn't going to be all rainbows and unicorns. Love doesn't make things easier. It just makes you willing to stick around when things get tough.<br /> <br /> /Advice from some random person on the internet that doesn't really know you and should mind their own business. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 12-08-2015, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T10:06:34-08:00","id":782363,"title":"","content":"On and off, for years now, I have been mulling something in my mind. It just struck me again this morning and I feel like talking about it to demonstrably rational and inclusive bunch. So I'm just gonna jump into this thread and get started.<br /> <br /> First off, I'm a married 34 year old white straight cisgendered male - the only thing that makes me slightly less boring is the fact that I'm from Serbia and recently moved to Canada. I make no pretense at knowing the hardships and difficulties of the LGBT community and this isn't an attempt to make myself sound as if I do. Still, inclusiveness and acceptance of the minorities is very important to me (which is a recipe for getting an ulcer very early in life if you're living in Serbia... or at the very least, getting beaten and insulted; but then, that's why I left).<br /> <br /> So, that said, I want to express my frustration with the &quot;born this way&quot; argument. I realize the LGBT community has gained a lot out of it and it helped overcome some rather idiotic issues in the society, such as religious nuts convincing people that you can and should change yourself if you happen to be any of the letters in LGBTQIA+. I don't mind that at all. But it still makes me cringe when I hear at, and here's why.<br /> <br /> First off, it puts you on the defensive. It literally sounds as if someone is saying you're a freak, and your reply is - I can't help it. So then a person should be allowed to be less-than-normal for reasons of inability to change. I do not like that at all. If you squint a little, it almost sounds as if you're agreeing with the opponents of equality in a weird way. If you were born a certain way and can't change it, does that mean we should revisit the &quot;not-normal; should change&quot; argument once genetic research has advanced enough to allow that to change? Basically - I do not think a person should apologize for being a certain way, whatever that way may be. You need not and SHOULD not provide genetic analysis in order to be allowed to like what you like and love what you love. We should strive to be a free society, our arguments should be that people are allowed to do whatever they like as long as they're not hurting anyone.<br /> <br /> Secondly, gender identity and sexual preference are literally the only aspects of modern society where genetics are used as an argument for anything. If you don't like kale, you do not say that you were born a certain way so that your digestive systems can't process kale normally. You say that you don't like kale, and that's enough. You do not say you were born unable to play basketball, you say you're not good at it and don't like it. All that could change at some point. Or not. You are allowed to not be pinned down as a non-basketball-playing kale-hater. Even if you stay that way for your entire life. It is perfectly reasonable and it should be normal for a person to say that they prefer sex with certain genders. Maybe that changes. Maybe it doesn't. It's none of anyone's business and they should stay the fuck out of it.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I firmly believe that people have long passed the point of being defined by their biological makeup. We are slowly but surely transcending what we originally were. Culture is more defining to us than biology and if anyone thinks there is such a thing as &quot;natural human behavior&quot;, they are wrong as wrong can be. There is a lot of cultural baggage, some of it still by necessity of procreation - so heterosexual cisgendered behavior is a lot more popular than the alternatives. I am the prime example of that - men do not attract me. And while I did wear makeup for a while, it wasn't for reasons of being transgender (but maybe it could've gone in that direction? who knows!). But just as I like denim jeans and sneakers, these are all cultural artifacts. And I feel they should be recognised as such. In a different society with a different cultural makeup, I am convinced it would be proven that everyone is, essentially, bisexual and gender fluid. These things will show up more and more as we advance. We should prepare in advance by not letting arguments about genetics drag us down.<br /> <br /> People should be free to choose what they are and not be required to provide justification for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","name":"Dawngreeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T12:01:26-08:00","id":782418,"title":"","content":"Ideally arguing one was born this way or not should not matter. And, frankly, given the shit LGBT+ persons have to deal with I can't understand why a lot of people would choose that. Some sure, but a lot? No. And I anticipate that down the line it won't be a thing.<br /> <br /> But LGBT+ persons have had to defend ourselves from a lot. No one is arguing people who don't like Kale should be given the death penalty or not allowed to be married...and people argued both in public in the US this year, and both positions were backed by candidates running for president, explicitly or implicitly. That fact it is not a choice when everything comes down is very significant. And I think it has helped with our public acceptance. Homosexuals have often been painted as, well, often men who go out looking for men because they want kicks, or are evil, or bored, or something. And people have to be told that that is not how it works...and telling people that is working. Even bisexuals don't choose who they fall in love with; a bisexual woman who falls in love with a woman and pursues her is following her heart, not choosing to be gay, just like a bisexual woman who falls in love with a man and pursues him is following her heart, not choosing to be straight.<br /> <br /> I agree people should be free to choose, and not have to provide justification, but we are not there yet. Trust me, we are not there yet, and not exclusively because of religious nuts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T12:43:09-08:00","id":782445,"title":"","content":"I read a great article recently on the &quot;born this way&quot; narrative and how it has historically been necessary, but is reaching the point where it has outlived its usefulness and in some ways may be holding us back. I don't know if I'll be able to find it again, but I'll give it a shot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T02:26:19-08:00","id":783311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=782353#post782353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This may be a case of &quot;Two ships passing in the night.&quot; You and your friend seem to be compatible, but all those logistical things that romantic comedies don't talk about, like money and life goals and plans, about come between you two.</div> </div> </div> </div>You were right, and wrong. I'm apparently not what was wanted romantically. <br /> I'm not bothered much, however. I've recently been assured, in my heart of hearts, that my love and affection belong elsewhere. <br /> <br /> It's a little sad. I'll admit that. I've introduced this woman to my family. I met her family. We'll remain friends if things go well, and that's acceptable. Really, she's almost better as another buddy, in certain ways. <br /> <br /> Love is... interesting. That's for sure.<br /> <br /> Old Chinese curse (lifted from Stephen King's Firestarter): May you live in interesting times.*<br /> <br /> *if this culturally inaccurate, email Stephen King. He wrote it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T04:46:11-08:00","id":783372,"title":"","content":"Update: I've severed ties from my ex fiancee in brutal fashion. I feel like crumbling into pieces, because I think I just also ruined a friendship that's lasted about half a decade. I just want to know what a loving relationship FEELS like. How much will I have to sacrifice to even approach that? ...I feel sick. The world has less color in it today, for me. That's probably for the best. The colors might hurt my eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T07:30:03-08:00","id":783432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=783372#post783372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Update: I've severed ties from my ex fiancee in brutal fashion. I feel like crumbling into pieces, because I think I just also ruined a friendship that's lasted about half a decade. I just want to know what a loving relationship FEELS like. How much will I have to sacrifice to even approach that? ...I feel sick. The world has less color in it today, for me. That's probably for the best. The colors might hurt my eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sucks, but sometimes completely breaking away from the person is for the best. It might hurt like hell now, but in the long run you'll be better off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T13:22:44-08:00","id":783616,"title":"","content":"I have to get off my chest my frustrations and rant a bit, I hope that's okay.<br /> <br /> I am not looking forward to going to my parent's place for Christmas. I never should have let them guilt me into going back. I mean, I like some of my family, but even then the sheer religious culture of the place I grew up in is oppressive without any intentional malice, due to the doctrine on LGBT people. I don't think even the nice members of my family realize why I get uneasy when all they talk about is &quot;church activity this&quot; and &quot;church activity that.&quot; I don't like being reminded that my family believes in a religion that thinks I am somehow so flawed and....not worthy enough to be respected and treated like a person. Anytime I bring it up, they just get defensive and upset that I am &quot;attacking their religious beliefs.&quot;<br /> <br /> And then there's my dad. He....well. I told him I was gay. After the rounds of being told I was &quot;in the clutches of the devil&quot; and &quot;going to die of AIDS&quot; (He is a <i>doctor</i>, he should know better!) I went back to school for a semester. And then, after not talking about it for a long time, he cuts off my education so I wouldn't be &quot;further corrupted by the liberals,&quot; or some crap like that. The idea was that he would force me to go to the local religious college. Oh, and such a lovely person, he made sure to cut off funding for my schooling <i>when the bill is in the mail</i>. I had a month or two as a person without credit, a job, and travelling to a unpaid dormitory to come up with thousands and thousands of tuition money.<br /> <br /> And he has the gall to tell me I need to apologize to <i>him</i> for &quot;breaking his heart.&quot; Gah<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":845,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","user":"Dragonmystic","date":". 12-10-2015, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T14:37:57-08:00","id":783664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topi