reat Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T01:58:20-07:00","id":853396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853379#post853379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't see a potential rapist going through the trouble to &quot;disguise&quot; themselves as a woman just so they can follow women/little girls into the restroom to rape them. That's a bullshit, fallacious argument if I ever saw one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus, if the fear is that men who look like women will 'secretly invade' the women's bathroom NEWSFLASH! They already have. They're called trans men*, but you don't see reports of them performing clandestine sex acts in the handicapped stall (because they aren't).<br /> <br /> The bottom line is that, for the most part, people are decent and public bathroom perversion is rare (and not restricted to men). Rape by a stranger is even rarer (especially in the case of pedophiles), but we as a public tend to latch onto it because the concept is chilling, but slightly less chilling than the truth, that you or your child are more likely to be assaulted by someone you know than by a complete stranger.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*Please don't take this as me accusing trans men of being insidious bathroom lurkers, I'm not, that would be insane. The point being made is that there are already men in women's bathrooms and <b>nothing bad</b> has come of it.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 03-26-2016, 05:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T07:03:07-07:00","id":853448,"title":"","content":"And the examples often mentioned long and hard in support of these kinds of laws... never happened. There's been police departments who were like &quot;What this happened and we know about it? News to us.&quot; Fact is, the talking points are just an excuse and &quot;think of the children&quot; is an attempt to appeal to the instinct some people have. When there are literal day camps to train people how to best help get these laws made, and parroting the same few (false) examples is part of it... I tend to distrust the reasons they give for wanting it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T11:04:55-07:00","id":853577,"title":"","content":"&quot;Think of the children&quot; is the laziest appeal to emotion logical fallacy there is. There's a reason it's a go to argument when people can't actually cite facts and figures to support their bigoted, irrational arguments against something. I heard a lot of that bullshit as a kid with regards to DnD, and how parents had to think about the children while protecting them from it's soul corrupting, demon worshipping influence. And just like DnD, being transgender is just too difficult a concept for the religious conservatives to to try and understand, so they just have to pass laws to protect their fragile little minds from being strained by thinking too hard about a subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T15:54:40-07:00","id":853724,"title":"","content":"Someone pointed out that more US senators have been busted for sexual misconduct in bathrooms than trans people, who have been busted for that not even once. So if anything we should be banning senators from bathrooms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T15:58:03-07:00","id":853726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853724#post853724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone pointed out that more US senators have been busted for sexual misconduct in bathrooms than trans people, who have been busted for that not even once. So if anything we should be banning senators from bathrooms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I thought/heard the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T17:26:17-07:00","id":853759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853724#post853724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone pointed out that more US senators have been busted for sexual misconduct in bathrooms than trans people, who have been busted for that not even once. So if anything we should be banning senators from bathrooms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had not heard that... but boy do I believe it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T19:33:18-07:00","id":853815,"title":"","content":"Picking one at random:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853379#post853379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't see a potential rapist going through the trouble to &quot;disguise&quot; themselves as a woman just so they can follow women/little girls into the restroom to rape them. That's a bullshit, fallacious argument if I ever saw one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said anything about sexual predators disguising themselves as women? The generic &quot;trans-friendly&quot; bathroom policy doesn't allow you to interfere with anyone from entering the women's restroom. In theory, its to prevent transgendered individuals from being embarrassed, or having their gender identity questioned. In practice, that means <i>anyone</i> (trans or not) can walk right in - and if you try to stop them, it opens <i>you</i> up to charges of harassment and/or discrimination.<br /> <br /> And if the girls or women inside feel threatened or uncomfortable? The issue came up . . . oh, about a month ago at a Planet Fitness. They're a gym chain that has a trans-friendly locker policy, and a woman complained to the management about an individual claiming to be transgendered in the women's locker room. The management's response was to throw <i>her</i> out, not the suspect individual.<br /> <br /> So you can't stop a suspicious individual from entering the women's restroom. And, once inside, the girls and women can't appeal to a third party if they feel threatened, or believe the person to be a possible sexual predator. That nixes any sort of preemptive effort to head off a sexual assault - no one can interfere until an attack is actually happening.<br /> <br /> Health insurance. Seat belts. Fire alarms. From guard rails on bunk beds to car seats to babysitters, we do a lot to make the world safe for kids. A policy where you can't intervene to stop a sexual predator until a little girl is screaming in fear is a terrible one. There's a reason the Houston anti-discrimination bill went down over the bathroom issue, despite having a populace and government considered friendly to the gay/lesbian/transgendered community.<br /> <br /> Implementing a policy in the real world is always messier than pondering it as an abstract concept - and there are often ugly tradeoffs that have to be made. The policy that you favor may not be the best for society as a whole, or it may have unacceptably bad side effects on other groups. Thus there may well be pushback when you present your proposed policy to the general public, and thus having alternate proposals is a good idea.<br /> <br /> Having a third (non-gender specific) bathroom seems like a reasonable option. <b>PenDragon</b>'s children-only idea (although meant facetiously) could work, too - still would be a safety issue for women, but the details could be hammered out later. Requiring transgendered individuals to flash some form of medical certification might also be an option (although I suspect there wouldn't be a lot of support for that proposal).<br /> <br /> Opposing transgendered access to the bathroom isn't about bigotry (although I'd be surprised if that wasn't a factor for some), or somehow accusing them of being sexual predators. Its about the side effects - such as how it opens a huge loophole for actual sexual predators.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: Oh, and with regards to some of the other posts - &quot;Think of the children&quot; is a classic rhetorical device, not a logical fallacy. It has a strong emotional pull on the audience, and often addresses real concerns. <br /> <br /> An <i>argument ad hominem</i>, on the other hand, <i>is</i> a logical fallacy. The moral/social failings of your opponent in an argument have no bearing on whether they're raising good points - and (as Cicero noted) such a criticism usually implies that there are huge flaws in the argument <i>you</i> are trying to advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 03-26-2016, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T20:26:35-07:00","id":853845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853815#post853815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Picking one at random:<br /> <br /> Who said anything about sexual predators disguising themselves as women? The generic &quot;trans-friendly&quot; bathroom policy doesn't allow you to interfere with anyone from entering the women's restroom. In theory, its to prevent transgendered individuals from being embarrassed, or having their gender identity questioned. In practice, that means <i>anyone</i> (trans or not) can walk right in - and if you try to stop them, it opens <i>you</i> up to charges of harassment and/or discrimination.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about preventing transgender (its an adjective, not a past-tense verb) individuals from being embarrassed or having their gender identity questioned. It's about preventing transgender individuals from being assaulted. You may not realize this, but public restrooms are absolutely terrifying for trans women. I can't count the number of times I've had to make a call between<br /> <br /> a.) Risking being beaten up and potentially raped for being a fag.<br /> b.) Risking being shouted out, beaten up, maced, and potentially arrested for being a sexual predator.<br /> c.) Being uncomfortable the whole time I'm out and risking pissing myself.<br /> <br /> That's just not an acceptable state of affairs for anyone. Full stop. And again, the current laws that segregate restrooms by sex rather than gender don't stop people who want to go into the &quot;wrong&quot; restroom anyway. This is not a choice between who you're putting at risk. People will always be at risk of being assaulted in restrooms and locker rooms. Allowing people to self-select the restrooms they want to use doesn't significantly increase the risk of cis people being assaulted, but it does significantly decrease the risk of trans people being assaulted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853815#post853815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if the girls or women inside feel threatened or uncomfortable? The issue came up . . . oh, about a month ago at a Planet Fitness. They're a gym chain that has a trans-friendly locker policy, and a woman complained to the management about an individual claiming to be transgendered in the women's locker room. The management's response was to throw <i>her</i> out, not the suspect individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>And no one was assaulted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853815#post853815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you can't stop a suspicious individual from entering the women's restroom. And, once inside, the girls and women can't appeal to a third party if they feel threatened, or believe the person to be a possible sexual predator. That nixes any sort of preemptive effort to head off a sexual assault - no one can interfere until an attack is actually happening.<br /> <br /> Health insurance. Seat belts. Fire alarms. From guard rails on bunk beds to car seats to babysitters, we do a lot to make the world safe for kids. A policy where you can't intervene to stop a sexual predator until a little girl is screaming in fear is a terrible one. There's a reason the Houston anti-discrimination bill went down over the bathroom issue, despite having a populace and government considered friendly to the gay/lesbian/transgendered community.<br /> <br /> Implementing a policy in the real world is always messier than pondering it as an abstract concept - and there are often ugly tradeoffs that have to be made. The policy that you favor may not be the best for society as a whole, or it may have unacceptably bad side effects on other groups. Thus there may well be pushback when you present your proposed policy to the general public, and thus having alternate proposals is a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm frankly a little disturbed by the fact that you are consistently framing this in terms of adult men abusing trans-friendly laws to target young girls. As though men don't target young boys. As though men don't target adult women. As though men don't target adult men. As though women don't target all of those same groups. And as though the vast majority of physical and sexual assaults in restrooms weren't <i>against trans people</i>, especially trans women.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853815#post853815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a third (non-gender specific) bathroom seems like a reasonable option. <b>PenDragon</b>'s children-only idea (although meant facetiously) could work, too - still would be a safety issue for women, but the details could be hammered out later. Requiring transgendered individuals to flash some form of medical certification might also be an option (although I suspect there wouldn't be a lot of support for that proposal).</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, many locations already have non-gender specific restroom options, usually called family restrooms. I know it's often a relief to me to know a place has them. But that option has a lot of problems, not the least of which is the fact that a lot of locations simply don't have the infrastructure to install a third restroom option with equal capacity to the the existing men's and women's restrooms. Second of all, no, there would not be a lot of support for the idea of requiring medical certification to use restrooms, and with good reason. Apart from the sheer ridiculousness of the idea of putting bouncers at restrooms to check people's ID's, there are enough issues with trans people getting recognition within the medical community without asking us to get a doctor to legally validate our right to take a piss without fear of being beaten or maced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853815#post853815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Opposing transgendered access to the bathroom isn't about bigotry (although I'd be surprised if that wasn't a factor for some), or somehow accusing them of being sexual predators. Its about the side effects - such as how it opens a huge loophole for actual sexual predators.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may not come from a place of intentional malice, but it is founded on inherently transmisogynistic assumptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853815#post853815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><u>Edit</u></i>: Oh, and with regards to some of the other posts - &quot;Think of the children&quot; is a classic rhetorical device, not a logical fallacy. It has a strong emotional pull on the audience, and often addresses real concerns.</div> </div> </div> </div>The logical fallacy that the &quot;Think of the Children&quot; rhetorical device falls under is called <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Appeal_to_emotion\" target=\"_blank\">The Appeal to Emotion Fallacy</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853815#post853815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An <i>argument ad hominem</i>, on the other hand, <i>is</i> a logical fallacy. The moral/social failings of your opponent in an argument have no bearing on whether they're raising good points - and (as Cicero noted) such a criticism usually implies that there are huge flaws in the argument <i>you</i> are trying to advance.</div> </div> </div> </div>It usually implies that the person resorting to <i>Ad Hominem</i> has an incomplete or flawed understanding of the point they are trying to argue, or at least that they do not care to construct a stronger argument in defense of their point. It does not imply that their point is inherently flawed. To suggest otherwise is called <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argument_from_fallacy\" target=\"_blank\">The Argument from Fallacy Fallacy</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-26-2016, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T20:42:15-07:00","id":853849,"title":"","content":"Having laws forcing individual to use bathrooms based on their biological sex isn't going to stop some sicko rapist from coming in to a bathroom and doing horrible things. I doubt employees are going to patrol bathrooms to keep &quot;suspicious&quot; people out no matter if there was a law or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T20:52:44-07:00","id":853859,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://media.giphy.com/media/oNTggpJCGjOhi/giphy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T21:02:47-07:00","id":853865,"title":"","content":"And the sort of laws you're talking about don't just risk the health of trans people because of assault. It's incredibly uncomfortable to use the wrong gender's bathroom, so I know I and others I've talked to... wait way past the healthy point. This has resulted in at least some developing UTIs, and that isn't just a problem for us then... since they're also people who tend to be more on the lower income, often that means YOU and everyone else are paying for that medical treatment with taxes. So the law does nothing to protect anyone, and does a lot to cause harm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T21:48:50-07:00","id":853888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853849#post853849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having laws forcing individual to use bathrooms based on their biological sex isn't going to stop some sicko rapist from coming in to a bathroom and doing horrible things. I doubt employees are going to patrol bathrooms to keep &quot;suspicious&quot; people out no matter if there was a law or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>nor would it have been legal to do so prior to this law.<br /> <br /> And out of interest I decided to look up the situation with woman getting kicked out of the fitness chain... and there's a slight bit of additional information. The woman in question noticed that one of the patrons in the female locker rooms had a penis. She went to the front desk to complain/comment (being concerned and afraid) and was informed of the gender locker room policy, to which she was rather upset that they didn't make the information more obvious in the sign up process for the chain. <br /> <br /> She then spent the next three days at the gym telling the other female patrons that they (the gym chain) allows men into the womens room. And THAT is what got the company to yank her membership. An active campaign to misrepresent the company policies.<br /> <br /> Even after that however, the woman still indicated she supported the solution of unisex rooms. And the chain has indeed changed the way they present the information in signups to make it more clear.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Overall I'd say it's kinda pointless, if someone is going to go into a bathroom to commit a crime, going into the &quot;wrong&quot; bathroom isn't going to be a major issue. Now I'm also going to set aside the obvious issue of assaults on trans individuals because frankly it's there, obviously a risk and a problem and frankly there is no way to try and justify encouraging it as a good thing.<br /> <br /> Now there's the more real issue of people's comfort, because let's face it that's a large part of what is driving this pointless crap law and the ones like it. People think if trans individuals can use the bathroom it's going to be creepy! It's going to be scary! There's going to be awkward questions from your kids about why the scary man with the beard is allowed in the ladies room mommy.<br /> <br /> And the big thing I have there, and I might need a point of clarification from someone due to not knowing any openly trans people directly in my life, is that my understanding is that using a relevant bathroom is usually driven by what they present as. Which means the people going into the ladies are the ones that dress and act female (I'm not simply saying are female because right now the gendered language is giving me a headache for clarification) and the ones that are dressing and acting in a male manner are going into the mens room. So you're not avoiding that awkward conversation with the kid, in fact you're increasing the odds. You're not eliminating seeing people that fail to match your gender expectations in the bathroom, you're increasing the probability.<br /> <br /> Of course there's still the question of people that present as a mix of gender traits, and what do you tell the kids? Well, if you don't want to explain just use the solution everyone else does when they kid asks &quot;Oh, they're just going to a comic convention and are dressed up.&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There's an old expression that seems appropriate for what these laws are trying to do. &quot;You're trying to pick fly shit out of pepper&quot; The laws ain't going to do anything, and are just wasting time and money.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T22:25:29-07:00","id":853903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dman1123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853269#post853269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh I am interested and do participate in politics. I'm just a cynical asshole.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not so much directing that at you but at the seething anger I feel about that situation. I don't say this as a claim of being some sort of expert on transgender, intersex,etc issues. But I grew up with a friend in secondary school who was transgender and I have a cousin here who has a transgender girlfriend and the way in very loud, very legally weighted words these bills try to declare that transgender, intersex, etc people are not people and not worthy of the considerations of basic humanity. Just in the history of the United States. The Aboriginal Americans, African Americans, Hispanics, the commies(Red Scare), Reefer Madness, &quot;The Gay Agenda!&quot;,etc. How many scapegoats do these people need before they realize the lesson of history that not only is inventing an OTHER as the source of your ills and fears puts those you care about at risk because you are focusing on the wrong thing, but that the social atmosphere that is created actively destroys lives. I would bet that most if not all of the legislators are what is generally known as pro-&quot;life&quot;. Some of those they claim to care about are going to be born intersex, will be LGBT. I mean call me crazy but I expect people's actions to match their intentions and if their intentions were to &quot;think of the children!&quot; they are doing a rather poor job of creating a culture, a society,etc that drives some into homelessness, depression and suicide.If there is any political impetus of the American people on this issue. I would hope that shaming these legislatures would be the action to take because they need to be shamed. They need to be reminded of transgender service members and transgender children and where the pretty picture in their heads of the types of people they often claim to respect is juxtaposed with the types of people they hate so much.<br /> <br /> Sorry for ranting folks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T22:26:54-07:00","id":853905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853888#post853888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the big thing I have there, and I might need a point of clarification from someone due to not knowing any openly trans people directly in my life, is that my understanding is that using a relevant bathroom is usually driven by what they present as. Which means the people going into the ladies are the ones that dress and act female (I'm not simply saying are female because right now the gendered language is giving me a headache for clarification) and the ones that are dressing and acting in a male manner are going into the mens room. So you're not avoiding that awkward conversation with the kid, in fact you're increasing the odds. You're not eliminating seeing people that fail to match your gender expectations in the bathroom, you're increasing the probability.<br /> <br /> Of course there's still the question of people that present as a mix of gender traits, and what do you tell the kids? Well, if you don't want to explain just use the solution everyone else does when they kid asks &quot;Oh, they're just going to a comic convention and are dressed up.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I can offer my experience here as a genderfluid person who presents different mixes of masculinity and femininity at different times. Generally speaking, my decisions of restroom use depend on my presentation on a given day. If I feel like my appearance reads generally male, I'll just use the men's room. As long as I don't feel like my appearance is going to be confusing, I feel like the men's room is the safest option. If I've got some mix, I'll use a single-occupancy or family restroom if one is available, and if not I will hold off as long as possible, and if absolutely necessary I'll use a men's room and try to get in and out as quickly as possible. When it comes down to it, I would rather put myself in a situation where I might have to defend myself physically than put myself in a situation where I could make a lot of women feel unsafe. If I'm presenting totally feminine, I will again avoid using public restrooms (apart from single-occupancy and family restrooms) at all costs and I <i>will not</i> use a men's room. If my partner is with me I <i>might</i> go into the women's room with them, <i>if</i> I feel like I'll be able to pass, but I won't go alone. I will leave early if I have to and deal with whatever I've got to deal with once I'm out of public space.<br /> <br /> That's the thing, my restroom choices are always based on safety. I would love to be able to chose based on where I would feel most comfortable, but that's just plain not practical. And that's exactly the problem. The college I went to made the decision to remove gender identifiers from restrooms in my third year. Restrooms were labeled &quot;Stalls&quot; and &quot;Stalls and Urinals&quot; and anyone could use which ever they wanted. I can't tell you how liberating that was, I could just use which ever restroom was most convenient (usually stalls and urinals, cause that's just easier most of the time) and not feel like I was invading anyone's space or putting myself in a dangerous situation. And there were no issues with people abusing the gender neutrality of the restrooms to assault anyone, sexually or otherwise in the time I was there. I went to a pretty liberal school, but that's my anecdotal evidence of gender neutral restrooms doing nothing but good.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Apologies if this post was TMI for anyone. Restroom stuff can be uncomfortable to talk about, but I feel like it's also an important issue to be able to discuss openly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-27-2016, 01:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/