heir intentions were to &quot;think of the children!&quot; they are doing a rather poor job of creating a culture, a society,etc that drives some into homelessness, depression and suicide.If there is any political impetus of the American people on this issue. I would hope that shaming these legislatures would be the action to take because they need to be shamed. They need to be reminded of transgender service members and transgender children and where the pretty picture in their heads of the types of people they often claim to respect is juxtaposed with the types of people they hate so much.<br /> <br /> Sorry for ranting folks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I understand that. I was just letting you know. Also on a personal note, I'd say that that's not a rant so much as a well put together argument about why these types of laws are stupid, ineffective, and influenced my humanities innate fear of the &quot;Other&quot; that has held us back from advancing as a society","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":2227,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","user":"dman1123","date":". 03-27-2016, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T22:51:58-07:00","id":853911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853903#post853903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not so much directing that at you but at the seething anger I feel about that situation. I don't say this as a claim of being some sort of expert on transgender, intersex,etc issues. But I grew up with a friend in secondary school who was transgender and I have a cousin here who has a transgender girlfriend and the way in very loud, very legally weighted words these bills try to declare that transgender, intersex, etc people are not people and not worthy of the considerations of basic humanity. Just in the history of the United States. The Aboriginal Americans, African Americans, Hispanics, the commies(Red Scare), Reefer Madness, &quot;The Gay Agenda!&quot;,etc. How many scapegoats do these people need before they realize the lesson of history that not only is inventing an OTHER as the source of your ills and fears puts those you care about at risk because you are focusing on the wrong thing, but that the social atmosphere that is created actively destroys lives. I would bet that most if not all of the legislators are what is generally known as pro-&quot;life&quot;. Some of those they claim to care about are going to be born intersex, will be LGBT. I mean call me crazy but I expect people's actions to match their intentions and if their intentions were to &quot;think of the children!&quot; they are doing a rather poor job of creating a culture, a society,etc that drives some into homelessness, depression and suicide.If there is any political impetus of the American people on this issue. I would hope that shaming these legislatures would be the action to take because they need to be shamed. They need to be reminded of transgender service members and transgender children and where the pretty picture in their heads of the types of people they often claim to respect is juxtaposed with the types of people they hate so much.<br /> <br /> Sorry for ranting folks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No no, I think a lot of us can understand that. On the &quot;think of the children&quot;... notice how trans children are treated as just as much predatory monsters as trans adults? This shows their life... if they cared about &quot;children&quot; they'd care about ALL CHILDREN. It wouldn't matter if they were not white, if they were not straight, if they were trans. Nothing would matter but them being children. But somehow, &quot;think of the children&quot; is &quot;Think of the white kids who are so fragile we should keep them in a bubble.&quot;<br /> <br /> And it doesn't just hurt the trans kids... it's an insult to the cis kids who don't care. As if what they feel and think doesn't matter AT ALL, even though they would be the one sharing facilities. And more often than not, you hear that they don't much care, because... they show more decency than the adults who get to make the decision.<br /> <br /> &lt;/rant&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T23:05:56-07:00","id":853914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853911#post853911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And more often than not, you hear that they don't much care, because... they show more decency than the adults who get to make the decision.<br /> <br /> &lt;/rant&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate trimming your wonderful post down to that one point, but that point hit me. Like I've always thought it. But seeing in relationship to this issue it was a real epiphany moment.<br /> <br /> Kids show more decency than adults when dealing with someone different. What happens between childhood and adulthood that changes that in some people but not others?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T23:38:47-07:00","id":853921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dman1123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853914#post853914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hate trimming your wonderful post down to that one point, but that point hit me. Like I've always thought it. But seeing in relationship to this issue it was a real epiphany moment.<br /> <br /> Kids show more decency than adults when dealing with someone different. What happens between childhood and adulthood that changes that in some people but not others?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's largely learned from the adults in their lives. Kids often take things adults tell them at face value, and they imitate the behaviors they see in the adults in their lives. If you tell your kids some people are one way, other people are another way, and there's nothing wrong with that, they will believe it's normal. If they see you treating people with respect, they will treat people with respect. If you tell your kids that God or Nature or what ever standard you want to set says that these people are normal and those people are freaks, they will believe that those people are freaks. If they see you acting uncomfortable around people who are different than you, then people who are different than them will make them uncomfortable. The more we can make LGBT a normal part of life, the more kids will grow up believing it's a normal part of life.<br /> <br /> That's why I always cringe when I see people talking about &quot;having to explain (insert thing that makes the person uncomfortable) to their kids.&quot; If you feel like you &quot;have to&quot; explain homosexuality or trans gender or what ever else in a different, more delicate way than you explain anything else about sex to them, you're already starting them off from a place of viewing it as abnormal or taboo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-27-2016, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T00:00:39-07:00","id":853924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853921#post853921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's largely learned from the adults in their lives. Kids often take things adults tell them at face value, and they imitate the behaviors they see in the adults in their lives. If you tell your kids some people are one way, other people are another way, and there's nothing wrong with that, they will believe it's normal. If they see you treating people with respect, they will treat people with respect. If you tell your kids that God or Nature or what ever standard you want to set says that these people are normal and those people are freaks, they will believe that those people are freaks. If they see you acting uncomfortable around people who are different than you, then people who are different than them will make them uncomfortable. The more we can make LGBT a normal part of life, the more kids will grow up believing it's a normal part of life.<br /> <br /> That's why I always cringe when I see people talking about &amp;quot;having to explain (insert thing that makes the person uncomfortable) to their kids.&amp;quot; If you feel like you &amp;quot;have to&amp;quot; explain homosexuality or trans gender or what ever else in a different, more delicate way than you explain anything else about sex to them, you're already starting them off from a place of viewing it as abnormal or taboo.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. It just makes me sad that some people can only see the differences and not the similarities. I know I'm just another bleeding heart, but humanity could be so much more if the people in power weren't... human. Because being human implies us having weaknesses, having blind spots in our judgement, having bias.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T00:01:34-07:00","id":853925,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see transgender people not being conflated with sexual predators, as if laws that allow them to use the bathroom of the gender they identify as is also somehow blanket protection for sexual predators. This is like voter ID laws, a solution in search of a problem that doesn't exist, with arguments being made in favor of those laws based on non reality based fear mongering. But sure, let's keep othering people because we think they're icky and gross, it's something we seem to be pretty good at in the US, so why the fuck not. Maybe we should start requiring them to wear special identification on their clothing, maybe get some identifying tattoos while we're at it. I know, let's start making people present photo ID with their chosen gender clearly stated before we allow them to use a public restroom, after a criminal background check is run on them in case they have sex offender status. You know, just to be sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T00:09:52-07:00","id":853927,"title":"","content":"It's also worth noting I can and have seen men acting suspicious/creepy be escorted from men's rooms. If a man is acting that way in a women's room and claiming to be trans, creepy behavior does not get a pass. In many circumstances, they can be removed anyway. If not, they probably won't stop a man in the ladies room either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 03-27-2016, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T02:45:12-07:00","id":853950,"title":"","content":"H'okay, I need to break this down point by point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853815#post853815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who said anything about sexual predators disguising themselves as women? The generic &quot;trans-friendly&quot; bathroom policy doesn't allow you to interfere with anyone from entering the women's restroom. In theory, its to prevent transgendered individuals from being embarrassed, or having their gender identity questioned. In practice, that means <i>anyone</i> (trans or not) can walk right in - and if you try to stop them, it opens <i>you</i> up to charges of harassment and/or discrimination.<br /> <br /> And if the girls or women inside feel threatened or uncomfortable? The issue came up . . . oh, about a month ago at a Planet Fitness. They're a gym chain that has a trans-friendly locker policy, and a woman complained to the management about an individual claiming to be transgendered in the women's locker room. The management's response was to throw <i>her</i> out, not the suspect individual.<br /> <br /> So you can't stop a suspicious individual from entering the women's restroom. And, once inside, the girls and women can't appeal to a third party if they feel threatened, or believe the person to be a possible sexual predator. That nixes any sort of preemptive effort to head off a sexual assault - no one can interfere until an attack is actually happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgive my saying so, but you seem to have conflated one experience into a universal constant. Your locker room example, while certainly unfortunate for many reasons, is anecdotal at best and lacking severely in details. Moreover the whole &quot;can't appeal to a third party angle&quot; is complete bullshit. In your own example the woman absolutely appealed to a third party (the gym management) and that third party, after what I assume was due consideration, deemed that it was she who was in the wrong. Now in my eyes that's the system working as intended. <br /> <br /> And who's to say you can't stop suspicious individuals from entering the womens (or men's) restroom? Currently, unless the bathroom has a lock, the best you can do is report suspicious peoples to management or authorities and unless I am grossly mistaken there is no law, current or proposed, that forces a private establishment to permit any and all behavior in their lavatories. As a practical example, if I (a man) go into the men's room, stand at the line of urinals and watch other men pee I can reasonably expect to be swiftly evicted. The argument &quot;But I'm a man, I'm allowed to be here&quot; wouldn't carry much weight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853815#post853815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Health insurance. Seat belts. Fire alarms. From guard rails on bunk beds to car seats to babysitters, we do a lot to make the world safe for kids. A policy where you can't intervene to stop a sexual predator until a little girl is screaming in fear is a terrible one. There's a reason the Houston anti-discrimination bill went down over the bathroom issue, despite having a populace and government considered friendly to the gay/lesbian/transgendered community.<br /> <br /> Implementing a policy in the real world is always messier than pondering it as an abstract concept - and there are often ugly tradeoffs that have to be made. The policy that you favor may not be the best for society as a whole, or it may have unacceptably bad side effects on other groups. Thus there may well be pushback when you present your proposed policy to the general public, and thus having alternate proposals is a good idea.<br /> <br /> Having a third (non-gender specific) bathroom seems like a reasonable option. <b>PenDragon</b>'s children-only idea (although meant facetiously) could work, too - still would be a safety issue for women, but the details could be hammered out later. Requiring transgendered individuals to flash some form of medical certification might also be an option (although I suspect there wouldn't be a lot of support for that proposal).</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, we all want to protect children, blah, blah blah. Here's a question: do segregated bathrooms accomplish that? Is there any data to support that by keeping biologically male and female people in segregated bathrooms there is a considerable reduction of rapes and assaults? Because without evidence the claim is nothing more than speculation. All the while trans men and women suffer very real, very provable consequences.<br /> <br /> And I wasn't being facetious (well, I don't think children's bathrooms will help, but the point was honest), if you are genuinely concerned about children being assaulted in adult bathrooms then you should be looking for solutions that keep all bathroom's safe. Because, assuming the threat of bathroom pedophiles is as pervasive as you fear it is, all this solution does is put the brunt of the bathroom rapes on little boys. And that is not, to my ears, a fucking solution. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853815#post853815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Opposing transgendered access to the bathroom isn't about bigotry (although I'd be surprised if that wasn't a factor for some), or somehow accusing them of being sexual predators. Its about the side effects - such as how it opens a huge loophole for actual sexual predators.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's not about keeping children safe, as I believe my above point thoroughly illustrated, and it's not about keeping adults safe, because by far the most likely persons to be assaulted in a public bathroom are trans individuals. Then what the hell is it about? Because to my ears it's abso-fucking-lutely bigotry. Not the conscious malice sort, but the softer more insidious 'this is foreign to me so I'm gonna fight it' form of bigotry that even open-minded people fall prey to.<br /> <br /> Here, let me end this with a comparison. Let's say it's 1965 and segregated locker rooms have just been abolished. Now let's replace the trans woman with a biologically female black woman and the accuser with a biologically female white woman, then run your exact scenario again. Would you still be saying the while woman was without recourse? That the management overstepped their bounds? At the very least I expect you'd want considerably more details about the nature of their altercation, otherwise is really is 100% bigotry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T02:51:12-07:00","id":853952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853921#post853921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's largely learned from the adults in their lives. Kids often take things adults tell them at face value, and they imitate the behaviors they see in the adults in their lives. If you tell your kids some people are one way, other people are another way, and there's nothing wrong with that, they will believe it's normal. If they see you treating people with respect, they will treat people with respect. If you tell your kids that God or Nature or what ever standard you want to set says that these people are normal and those people are freaks, they will believe that those people are freaks. If they see you acting uncomfortable around people who are different than you, then people who are different than them will make them uncomfortable. The more we can make LGBT a normal part of life, the more kids will grow up believing it's a normal part of life.<br /> <br /> That's why I always cringe when I see people talking about &quot;having to explain (insert thing that makes the person uncomfortable) to their kids.&quot; If you feel like you &quot;have to&quot; explain homosexuality or trans gender or what ever else in a different, more delicate way than you explain anything else about sex to them, you're already starting them off from a place of viewing it as abnormal or taboo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have experiences that back that up. I had a pretty rough childhood growing up in a small town after my mom was one of the people who came in a large group to work at the power plants. And the adults (Much of the town has blood ties... like the only one of my classmates that was part of an older family that wasn't... she was adopted) didn't like that there were all these &quot;outsiders&quot; coming into &quot;their town&quot;. As the only kid of any workers (most were single or didn't have kids)... it wasn't pleasant.<br /> <br /> The only reason kids don't follow in the footsteps is if they have a reason to go against it. Say they dislike something about their parents' ideas and go the totally opposite direction.<br /> <br /> I also worked at a gas station and a lot of high schoolers came in. The only one who was rude was the manager's daughter (and her friends called her out on it), because I treated them with respect. It took time, but they understood I wasn't going to look down on them or assume they were too stupid to have any real thoughts or feelings. That too affects how young people change as they grow up. I think the lack of respect for people based on age is a problem that combined with them growing up can have really negative effects. But... this is just based on my observations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T02:58:33-07:00","id":853954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853950#post853950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> biologically female</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope this doesn't come off as pedantic, but... that's a really questionable term from a scientific stance. I was in biotechnology in university, and I won't claim to be the end all be all, but I keep up on the science of genotype and phenotype... and it's starting to look a lot like (unsurprisingly) sex is as complicated a spectrum as gender. And probably more widely spread demographically. But a lot of these things aren't necessarily obvious. <a href=\"http://www.nature.com/news/sex-redefined-1.16943#/spectrum\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.nature.com/news/sex-redef...6943#/spectrum</a> I don't know if it's useful, but kinda a collection of some findings and examples.<br /> <br /> Edit: If it did come off badly, I apologize for my bad behavior. It's just one of those things that bothers me and I sometimes overreact without thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","user":"haren","date":". 03-27-2016, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T03:38:19-07:00","id":853960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=853954#post853954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope this doesn't come off as pedantic, but... that's a really questionable term from a scientific stance. I was in biotechnology in university, and I won't claim to be the end all be all, but I keep up on the science of genotype and phenotype... and it's starting to look a lot like (unsurprisingly) sex is as complicated a spectrum as gender. And probably more widely spread demographically. But a lot of these things aren't necessarily obvious. <a href=\"http://www.nature.com/news/sex-redefined-1.16943#/spectrum\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.nature.com/news/sex-redef...6943#/spectrum</a> I don't know if it's useful, but kinda a collection of some findings and examples.<br /> <br /> Edit: If it did come off badly, I apologize for my bad behavior. It's just one of those things that bothers me and I sometimes overreact without thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to refute the assertion that letting trans women use the bathroom they are comfortable with is a slippery slope to widespread rape and pedophelia. After that we can get the the masters level gender gradient, for now forgive my generalizations. Baby steps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T03:46:05-07:00","id":853962,"title":"","content":"Sorry, like I said, I reacted, but I knew you were speaking well and kindly. Thank you very much!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T14:09:16-07:00","id":854203,"title":"","content":"The generally accepted term is cis gender or cis woman/cis man. Cis simply means not trans.<br /> <br /> So far in the 9 months I have been living full time as myself I have been using the ladies room and no one in person has had a problem with it. most of this hysteria is a blow back from the legalization of same sex marriage. Scared people reacting to one thing that scares them by attacking another more vulnerable group. <br /> <br /> I will say that the current push for theses law scare me. Kansas is trying to put a bounty on trans people, as well as passing a law that declares us criminal and a threat to cis people. The laws are not written that way but it's there intent.<br /> <br /> I just wonder how far it will go, will I need papers to travel, perhaps wearing a rainbow star on my clothing so everyone knows, or mabye they will just put us all in a camp somewhere for our protection. That all seems insane but we have done as much and worse to others in the past when fear and hate controlled people. Given our very limited numbers and even more limited power there is very little transgender people can do to stop something like that.<br /> <br /> But I get up every day, get dressed and face the world because I have to be me or I would be dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2939-avaron","name":"Avaron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T14:44:14-07:00","id":854217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avaron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/58142-the-lgbt-thread?p=854203#post854203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The generally accepted term is cis gender or cis woman/cis man. Cis simply means not trans.<br /> <br /> So far in the 9 months I have been living full time as myself I have been using the ladies room and no one in person has had a problem with it. most of this hysteria is a blow back from the legalization of same sex marriage. Scared people reacting to one thing that scares them by attacking another more vulnerable group.<br /> <br /> I will say that the current push for theses law scare me. Kansas is trying to put a bounty on trans people, as well as passing a law that declares us criminal and a threat to cis people. The laws are not written that way but it's there intent.<br /> <br /> I just wonder how far it will go, will I need papers to travel, perhaps wearing a rainbow star on my clothing so everyone knows, or mabye they will just put us all in a camp somewhere for our protection. That all seems insane but we have done as much and worse to others in the past when fear and hate controlled people. Given our very limited numbers and even more limited power there is very little transgender people can do to stop something like that.<br /> <br /> But I get up every day, get dressed and face the world because I have to be me or I would be dead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> After doing a bit of research on this, and I do mean a bit (I looked at 1 article), that scares me. (Here is the article I read <a href=\"http://www.advocate.com/transgender/2016/3/23/kansas-lawmakers-target-trans-students-dangerous-bathroom-bill\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.advocate.com/transgender/...-bathroom-bill</a>). Interestingly, it also brings up a bill in Indiana which I was unaware of. In addition to both of those interesting bills, it also brings up numerous studies about violence perpetrated by trans individuals in bathrooms (Spoiler, there is none) compared to violence against trans individuals in bathrooms (another spoiler here, it happens).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":2227,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","user":"dman1123","date":". 03-27-2016, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T16:49:39-07:00","id":854249,"title":"","content":"By the way, it's &quot;transgender,&quot; not &quot;transgendered.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T18:00:10-07:00","id":854280,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>You know what, I think this thread has pretty much reached the end of its life. There are more and more group attacks both subtle and overt being slung around. I'm done.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}